France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,"🔴 Israeli settlers beat French mayor, attack European diplomatic cars in West Bank","🔴 Israeli settlers beat French mayor, attack European diplomatic cars in West Bank","🔴 Israeli settlers beat French mayor, attack European diplomatic cars in West Bank Israeli settlers on Saturday attacked a convoy carrying a European delegation in the occupied West Bank, beating up a 78-year-old French mayor. While Israel's Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu – who is just days from a crucial election – described the incident as a ""smear"" campaign against Israeli settlers, France's top diplomat urged Israel to ""urgently halt criminal violence"". Issued on:17/10/2026 - 16:58Modified:17/10/2026 - 21:38 Israeli settlers on Saturday attacked a convoy of European diplomats and beat up a visiting French mayor, in a new escalation of violence during the Palestinian olive harvest, witnesses and diplomats said. The 78-year-old mayor said masked settlers yelled defamatory comments about France, kicked him and hit him with iron bars as he joined Palestinian olive farmers in the West Bank alongside the top French and Belgian representatives in Jerusalem and Polish diplomats. “I think that if settlers are behaving like this, there is a tolerance on the part of the Israeli government,” Bernard Baudoux, mayor of the northern French town of Aulnoye-Aymeries, told AFP after he was attacked. “The whole world needs to know what’s happening,” he said. “For me, I’ll go back to my country and everything will be fine. Those who continue to suffer the most are those who are here.” Baudoux, who was wearing a sash with the French tricolour, was seen collapsed on the side of the car after the attack but did not need hospital care. Read moreUS journalist injured during ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:58:54 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261017-israeli-settlers-attack-european-delegation-convoy-in-west-bank-beat-french-mayor,2026-10-18 01:45:57
