France 24 (EN),Western Europe,en,"Kenya reports third Ebola case, contact tracing continues","Kenya reports third Ebola case, contact tracing continues","Kenya reports third Ebola case, contact tracing continues Kenya has confirmed a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from the Democratic Republic of the Congo. The health ministry said the 65-year-old woman tested positive while in quarantine, where she has been since 5 October. The second patient, a 39-year-old man from the same family, is in a stable condition. Health officials say there is no evidence of community transmission, as both individuals were under quarantine. However, three contacts have yet to be traced. Our correspondent Bastien Renouil tells us more. To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Issued on:17/10/2026 - 12:56 Kenya has confirmed a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from the Democratic Republic of the Congo. The health ministry said the 65-year-old woman tested positive while in quarantine, where she has been since 5 October. The second patient, a 39-year-old man from the same family, is in a stable condition. Health officials say there is no evidence of community transmission, as both individuals were under quarantine. However, three contacts have yet to be traced. Our correspondent Bastien Renouil tells us more. Keywords for this article The content you requested does not exist or is not available anymore.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:56:48 GMT",https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-kenya-reports-third-ebola-case-contact-tracing-continues,2026-10-18 01:45:59
