Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,US ambassador urges Israel to prosecute attackers of American journalist,US ambassador urges Israel to prosecute attackers of American journalist,"US ambassador urges Israel to prosecute attackers of American journalist Trump-appointed Ambassador Mike Huckabee calls attack in occupied West Bank a &#039;despicable act of terror&#039;. Save Share United States Ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee has demanded Israel prosecute and jail those responsible for the attack on Washington Post journalist Heidi Levine in the occupied West Bank. “Attacking a female photographer is a despicable act of terror carried out by masked cowards,” Huckabee wrote on X on Saturday. “Those who attacked unarmed reporter should spend YRS in prison,” he added. “We have called for a full investigation, arrest, and prosecution to the fullest extent of the law to whoever participated in this.” Levine was covering Palestinians’ annual harvest of olives on Friday in the occupied West Bank when Israeli settlersbrutally attackedher and several Palestinians. Israeli settlers stormed the area, beat her and stole her passport, telephone, wallet and equipment, according to witnesses. The perpetrators, armed with bottles and slingshots, “were kicking me for like 10 minutes, and I was trying to hold onto my cameras and my bag”, Levine said. Jasper Nathaniel, an independent journalist who witnessed the attack, told Al Jazeera that Levine “was in very, very bad shape. She couldn’t really get up off the ground.” Levine, 64, was taken to hospital after the assault in Abu Falah, northeast of Ramallah. The American photojournalist underwent surgery on her finger, which was nearly detached from her hand, and was left with a broken rib and multiple broken vertebrae, as well as lacerations, her daughter told The Associated Press news agency. Israeli Prime","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:40:59 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/17/us-ambassador-calls-on-israel-to-prosecute-settlers-over-journalist-attack?traffic_source=rss,2026-10-18 01:46:01
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Saudi-led coalition intercepts drones as Egypt weighs sending help,Saudi-led coalition intercepts drones as Egypt weighs sending help,"Saudi-led coalition intercepts drones as Egypt weighs sending help Forces intercepted and destroyed four drones over Saudi Arabia&#039;s Riyadh, Eastern Province and southern region. Save Share The Saudi-led coalition fighting Yemen’s Houthis has said it intercepted and destroyed four drones over Riyadh and other regions, the latest in a wave of Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia’s airports and oil facilities. “We intercepted and destroyed four drones over the past few hours in the regions of Riyadh, the Eastern Province, and the South,” coalition spokesperson Major-General Turki al-Maliki said on Saturday. He also posted footage of what he described as the air force intercepting cruise missiles and drones and striking ballistic missile launchers belonging to the Houthis. Riyadh’s King Khalid airport has come under at least 20 attacks – including one last week that killed 13 people – since the fighting between the Houthi rebels and the Saudi-backed Yemeni government flared in July. On Thursday, at least five people were killed inmissile strikesnear the presidential palace in Aden, the seat of Yemen’s internationally recognised government. It blamed the Houthis for the attack. On Friday, the Yemeni government said the Houthisfired two missiles at Aden’s airport, while government forces said they had advanced in Marib province, northeast of Sanaa. Saudi Arabia is backing a government counteroffensive, known as Dawn of Yemen, and has carried out air strikes on the Houthis, including on an oil facility in Sanaa. Egyptian President Abdel Fattah el-Sisisaid on Saturday he was willingto “carry out any measure to protect” Saudi Arabia should the kingdom ask. Egypt wa","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:21:57 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/17/saudi-led-coalition-intercepts-drones-as-egypt-weighs-sending-help?traffic_source=rss,2026-10-18 01:46:01
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,Photos: No Kings rallies in US urge midterm voters to cast ballots early,Photos: No Kings rallies in US urge midterm voters to cast ballots early,"Photos: No Kings rallies in US urge midterm voters to cast ballots early Thousands gathered at events throughout the country on Saturday, building on two years of No Kings marches. In Pictures Save Share Rallies organised by the No Kings network opposed to United States President Donald Trump were held Saturday in cities and communities across the US, with an aim of getting people out to vote early in the midterm elections. No Kings has more than 3,000 events planned across the US. The planned events, this time dubbed “No Kings: Vote Early”, were billed as nonpartisan, though they sought to build on nearly two years’ worth of No Kings marches and demonstrations by people upset with Trump’s presidency. “It’s a day of nonpartisan voter participation: we are bringing our community together to make a plan to vote early and ensuring every eligible voter understands their options for how to vote and has the opportunity to make their voice heard,” organisers said in a statement. By advocating for voting early, the “No Kings” organisers hope to cut off the potential for any malfeasance once election day rolls around. A band entertained what appeared to be a few hundred people in caps and coats at the Lincoln Memorial in Washington, DC. Despite the chilly weather, many in the crowd danced to the tunes. “VOTE EARLY” and “HANDS OFF MY VOTE!” were among the many signs held aloft. At an Atlanta rally, City Councilman Michael Julian Bond told the crowd to urge others to vote ahead of the November 3 general election. “The Constitution gives you one power, right? That is the power to vote. Are you gonna use that power?” he said. “You don’t see Superman giving up his po","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:08:10 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2026/10/17/photos-no-kings-rallies-in-us-urge-midterm-voters-to-cast-ballots-early?traffic_source=rss,2026-10-18 01:46:01
Al Jazeera (EN),Middle East (English),en,"Cost of living protests hit Belgium, Italy, Portugal and France","Cost of living protests hit Belgium, Italy, Portugal and France","Cost of living protests hit Belgium, Italy, Portugal and France Hundreds of thousands took to the streets for separate demonstrations, putting pressure on governments across the EU. Save Share Hundreds of thousands of Europeans have taken to the streets in separate, uncoordinated demonstrations to protest against the rising cost of living in their countries. Saturday’s wave of unrest in Belgium, France, Italy and Portugal has put pressure on governments across the European Union. France experienced one of its mostturbulent days of protestsin decades, with more than 550,000 people joining demonstrations, according to the Ministry of Interior, and police facing off with protesters across the country. The marches, which followed weeks of student protests, degenerated into clashes, looting and fires after violent fringe groups targeted public buildings, luxury boutiques and supermarkets, as well as attacked police vehicles and officers. French Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu said 1,200 people were arrested and 150 police officers were hurt. “It’s a miracle the toll wasn’t higher,” he said as he visited officers deployed in central Paris. Dozens of shops were looted in Paris, Marseille, Nice, Nantes, Bordeaux, Limoges, Lille, Toulouse and Strasbourg, the French news agency AFP reported. Whole streets in the capital “have been devastated”, Paris Mayor Emmanuel Gregoire said. A fire set by masked protesters in Limoges largely destroyed the more than 140-year-old town hall, while city halls in Marseille and Lille were broken into and vandalised. In Lyon, protesters torched the city’s tourist office. President Emmanuel Macron said on X that those responsible wou","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:02:26 +0000",https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/17/cost-of-living-protests-hit-belgium-italy-portugal-and-france?traffic_source=rss,2026-10-18 01:46:02
