The exhibit named “Xabnameh” runs until October 30 at the gallery that can be found at 10 Mirza Taraj, opposite Dowlat St., Shariati Ave. Ech Gallery is playing host to an exhibition of paintings by Sahar Farah. The exhibit named “Xabnameh” runs until October 30 at the gallery that can be found at 10 Mirza Taraj, opposite Dowlat St., Shariati Ave. Painting * Iranshahr Gallery is showcasing paintings by Mani Mehrzad in an exhibition. The exhibit named “After Snow” will run until October 27 at the gallery that can be found at 69 Sepand St., off Karim Khan Ave. * Melina Bahrami is showcasing her latest paintings in an exhibition at Bostan Gallery. The exhibit named “Absence” will run until October 27 at No. 71, 22th Alley, Larestan St. off Motahhari Ave. * An exhibition of paintings by Negar Nasiri is currently underway at Afrand Gallery. The exhibit named “Unrelated” will continue until October 30 at the gallery located at 48 Jalal Hosseini St., Jahan Ara St., off Jalal Ale-Ahmad Highway. * Paintings by Habibeh Louri are on display in an exhibition at Asr Gallery. The exhibit entitled “The Memory of Imagination” will run until October 26 at the gallery located at 18 Delaviz St. off North Mirzaye Shirazi St. * Paintings by Bahar Akhavan are currently on display in an exhibit at Jaleh Gallery. Entitled “Growth”, the exhibition runs until October 23 at the gallery located at No. 3, Noshahr Alley, Iranshahr St., Karim Khan Ave. * An exhibition of paintings by Vahik Hartounian is currently on view in an exhibition at Dena Gallery. The exhibition will run until October 30 at the gallery that can be found at 4 Sussan Al","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:45:48 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531146/What-s-in-Tehran-art-galleries,2026-10-18 01:46:48
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,TMoCA cinematheque to review 6 films by Stanley Kubrick,TMoCA cinematheque to review 6 films by Stanley Kubrick,"TMoCA cinematheque to review 6 films by Stanley Kubrick TEHRAN – The cinematheque of the Tehran Museum of Contemporary Art (TMoCA) will review six films by Stanley Kubrick on Sunday. TEHRAN – The cinematheque of the Tehran Museum of Contemporary Art (TMoCA) will review six films by Stanley Kubrick on Sunday. The films will be examined from a philosophical perspective in a session titled “Kubrick and the Cinema of Machines,” Mehr reported. In this program, Farzad Karimi, a postdoc in interdisciplinary studies of literature and philosophy, will analyze the works alongside screening excerpts from six films by the late filmmaker. The event will feature excerpts from the films “Dr. Strangelove,” “2001: A Space Odyssey,” “A Clockwork Orange,” “The Shining,” “Full Metal Jacket,” and “Eyes Wide Shut”. Attending this program is free and open to the general public. Stanley Kubrick (1928 – 1999) was an American filmmaker and photographer. A prominent figure of the New Hollywood era, Kubrick is regarded as one of the greatest and most influential filmmakers. His films spanned a number of genres and gained recognition for their attention to detail, innovative cinematography, extensive set design, and dark humor. Kubrick's “Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb” (1964) was a satirical black comedy. Kubrick became preoccupied with the issue of nuclear war as the Cold War unfolded in the 1950s, and even considered moving to Australia because he feared that New York City might be a likely target for the Russians. He studied over 40 military and political research books on the subject and eventually reached the conclusion that ""nobody really ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:45:28 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531150/TMoCA-cinematheque-to-review-6-films-by-Stanley-Kubrick,2026-10-18 01:46:48
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Researcher calls for greater understanding between religion and music in Iran,Researcher calls for greater understanding between religion and music in Iran,"Researcher calls for greater understanding between religion and music in Iran TEHRAN- A deeper understanding of the relationship between religious institutions and the arts is essential to addressing longstanding challenges surrounding music in Iran, cultural sociologist Hossein Sarvi says, emphasizing the need for informed dialogue and a reassessment of institutional relations. TEHRAN- A deeper understanding of the relationship between religious institutions and the arts is essential to addressing longstanding challenges surrounding music in Iran, cultural sociologist Hossein Sarvi says, emphasizing the need for informed dialogue and a reassessment of institutional relations. Speaking to Mehr News Agency, Sarvi, whose book “Religion and Music in Contemporary Iran” examines the historical and social dimensions of the subject, said some of the tensions between religion and music stem not necessarily from fundamental conflicts but from insufficient understanding of the nature, functions and sensitivities of the two fields. “One of the main objectives of this research has been to help improve what I call ‘mutual institutional literacy’ between religious institutions and the arts,” Sarvi explained. The concept refers to the ability of each institution to better understand the other's internal logic, functions, requirements and concerns, creating opportunities for more informed and realistic interaction. Sarvi argued that the relationship between religion and music in Iran remains an important subject for cultural and social debate. Questions concerning the relationship between religious and artistic institutions, cultural policymaking on music, and the scope and methods of official intervention continue to require reflection and scholarly discussion, he said. According to the researcher, examining these issues solely through a historical lens would overl","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:45:05 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531149/Researcher-calls-for-greater-understanding-between-religion-and,2026-10-18 01:46:49
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,26th Tehran Auction realizes over $4.6 million,26th Tehran Auction realizes over $4.6 million,"26th Tehran Auction realizes over $4.6 million TEHRAN – The 26th Tehran Auction, dedicated to modern and contemporary Iranian art, grossed more than $4.6 million. In this edition, Parviz Tanavoli’s bronze “Heech” sculpture was sold as the most expensive artwork in the history of the auction. TEHRAN – The 26th Tehran Auction, dedicated to modern and contemporary Iranian art, grossed more than $4.6 million. In this edition, Parviz Tanavoli’s bronze “Heech” sculpture was sold as the most expensive artwork in the history of the auction. Held at the Parsian Azadi Hotel in Tehran on October 16, the 26th Tehran Auction presented 100 works by 93 modern and contemporary Iranian artists, celebrating the diversity of artistic expression and the enduring value of Iran’s art scene, Honaronline reported. The total estimated value of the artworks in this edition was announced at $2.941 million. Ultimately, amidst intense competition among art buyers, all 100 offered works were sold for a total of $4,603,500. The most expensive work of this auction was a bronze sculpture titled “Heech” by Parviz Tanavoli, which had a base price of $750,000 and was hammered down at $1.77 million. This work broke the sales record across all editions of the Tehran Auction. Following Tanavoli’s “Heech” sculpture, an untitled mirror mosaic work by Monir Farmanfarmaian, with a base price of $377,000, was sold for $461,538, setting the second-highest record in the auction’s history. The third landmark artwork in the Iranian art market was a piece by Kourosh Shishegaran titled “Inside and Outside,” which had a base price of $204,000 and was sold for $252,800. The other best-selling artists whose works were offered at the auction include Abolghasem Saidi, Mohammad Ehsai, Hossein Zenderoudi, Mansour Ghand","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:44:38 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531151/26th-Tehran-Auction-realizes-over-4-6-million,2026-10-18 01:46:50
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Israelis beat Washington Post journalist in military-backed West Bank raids,Israelis beat Washington Post journalist in military-backed West Bank raids,"Israelis beat Washington Post journalist in military-backed West Bank raids TEHRAN — The men came down from a hilltop settlement shortly after 8 a.m. on Friday, dressed in black, carrying slingshots and batons. At least one had a gun. By the time they finished, olive groves around Abu Falah, northeast of Ramallah, were burning, villagers were bleeding, and an American photographer for The Washington Post lay on the ground being kicked. TEHRAN — The men came down from a hilltop settlement shortly after 8 a.m. on Friday, dressed in black, carrying slingshots and batons. At least one had a gun. By the time they finished, olive groves around Abu Falah, northeast of Ramallah, were burning, villagers were bleeding, and an American photographer for The Washington Post lay on the ground being kicked. Heidi Levine wore a helmet and a vest marked “PRESS” front and back. Videos show settlers beating her with bats and sticks as she lay prostrate. “They just kept kicking me and kicking me,” she told reporters. Her cameras and phone were taken. She suffered four broken vertebrae and a broken rib. Soldiers arrived while the attack was under way. They fired tear gas at Palestinians, then shot village council member Abdel Jaber Hassan in the leg. The Israeli military claims he ran at troops with a sharp object. Residents say he carried harvesting tools. Activist Jonathan Pollak, who was there, said soldiers stood “shoulder-to-shoulder with settlers.” Abu Falah was one of at least eight villages hit on Friday, with cars and trees burned in Turmus Ayya. Yesh Din has logged at least 170 attacks since the harvest began on September 27. The Palestinian Health Ministry reports at least four Palestinians killed and more than 100 injured this season. Ali Hassan al-Bazzari, 44, was killed near Nablus on October 7. A day earlier, settlers beat AFP photographer Jaafar Ashtiyeh with rifle butts. Ziv Stahl from the Israeli organization ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:40:51 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531167/Israelis-beat-Washington-Post-journalist-in-military-backed-West,2026-10-18 01:46:51
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Trump’s White House chaotically turns on itself as Republicans brace for defeat,Trump’s White House chaotically turns on itself as Republicans brace for defeat,"Trump’s White House chaotically turns on itself as Republicans brace for defeat TEHRAN — A press secretary hired on a Friday and gone the next. An ambassador’s ouster announced during her only briefing. Loyalists feuding over money while the chief of staff’s family draws scrutiny. With the November 3 midterms less than three weeks away, Donald Trump’s White House has stopped hiding its disorder. TEHRAN — A press secretary hired on a Friday and gone the next. An ambassador’s ouster announced during her only briefing. Loyalists feuding over money while the chief of staff’s family draws scrutiny. With the November 3 midterms less than three weeks away, Donald Trump’s White House has stopped hiding its disorder. Katie Zacharia, a Fox News commentator few in the building knew, got the job because Trump was angry that nobody defended him on television as Republican prospects sank. He offered it in an Oval Office talk Chief of Staff Susie Wiles missed. “Did anyone vet her?” one adviser asked. Officials told CNN no one had. Her only briefing, on Tuesday, ran 14 minutes and took three questions, all from friendly outlets. Asked where she had passed the bar exam, she answered, “When I moved to China.” She later admitted she failed the California bar in 2011, though her own X reposts and the White House announcement called her “an attorney.” After Sean Hannity and “Fox & Friends” pressed her, Trump claims he told her, “Honestly, if I were you, I’d reconsider.” Hours later, it was leaked that she is gone. Citing two anonymous sources, CNN reports that Wiles helped arrange the Hannity slot, one calling it a “sanctioned hit.” Purges, feuds and a sidelined friend The single piece of real news delivered during Zacharia’s brief time at the podium was that Kimberly Guilfoyle had been asked to resign from her post as ambassador to Greece. Guilfoyle, a television commentator and the for","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:40:27 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531169/Trump-s-White-House-chaotically-turns-on-itself-as-Republicans,2026-10-18 01:46:52
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"War on Iran has cost EU more than $112 billion, Spanish PM Sánchez says","War on Iran has cost EU more than $112 billion, Spanish PM Sánchez says","War on Iran has cost EU more than $112 billion, Spanish PM Sánchez says TEHRAN- Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez has warned that the war against Iran has cost Europeans more than €100 billion ($112 billion), arguing that ordinary citizens are paying the price for a conflict they opposed. TEHRAN- Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez has warned that the war against Iran has cost Europeans more than €100 billion ($112 billion), arguing that ordinary citizens are paying the price for a conflict they opposed. In a post on X on Friday, Sánchez said those who had spoken out against the war had been right to warn of its consequences. “Those of us who raised our voices against the war were right when we said NO to war,” he wrote. “We knew ordinary people would end up paying the bill.” “Now, it's time to put an end to this disaster,” Sánchez said. His remarks underscore mounting concerns in Europe over the economic fallout of the war, particularly its effects on energy costs, household budgets and business competitiveness. European citizens face the economic fallout The €100 billion figure cited by Sánchez highlights the scale of the economic burden that the conflict has placed on Europe. Higher energy costs can feed through to transport, manufacturing, food prices and household expenditure, placing additional pressure on governments already grappling with economic challenges. The economic repercussions raise a broader question for European governments: how can they protect their populations from the consequences of a conflict while addressing the extent to which their own military infrastructure has supported US operations? British base used by US bombers in strikes on Iran The debate has gained a further dimension following reports by major Western media outlets that","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:37:12 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531180/War-on-Iran-has-cost-EU-more-than-112-billion-Spanish-PM-S%C3%A1nchez,2026-10-18 01:46:53
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Iran’s missile capabilities have changed the equation, caretaker defense minister warns US","Iran’s missile capabilities have changed the equation, caretaker defense minister warns US","Iran’s missile capabilities have changed the equation, caretaker defense minister warns US TEHRAN- Iran’s caretaker Defense Minister, Brigadier General Majid Ebn al-Reza, has responded to US President Donald Trump’s threats against Iran, warning that any renewed military action would carry consequences for Washington’s international standing, economy and domestic political calculations. TEHRAN- Iran’s caretaker Defense Minister, Brigadier General Majid Ebn al-Reza, has responded to US President Donald Trump’s threats against Iran, warning that any renewed military action would carry consequences for Washington’s international standing, economy and domestic political calculations. In a post on X, Ebn al-Reza dismissed speculation about the possible use of the US military’s most powerful conventional bomb against Iran, stressing that the size and name of a weapon would not determine the outcome of a confrontation. “The names and dimensions of bombs do not matter!” he wrote. “Your bombs will explode somewhere else: in your global standing, the US economy, and even your electoral calculations!” he added. The Iranian general said the country’s missile capabilities had fundamentally altered the strategic equation, telling US officials that Washington would have to adjust to a new reality. “It is our missile power that has changed the equations and brought you to the point where, from now on, you must say: ‘Yes, sir!’” he wrote. Ebn al-Reza’s remarks came amid reports that the US military had considered additional strike options involving the GBU-43/B Massive Ordnance Air Blast (MOAB), commonly known as the “Mother of All Bombs.” The weapon is one of the largest conventional bombs in the US arsenal. Reports have raised the possibility of further attacks on Iranian infrastructure and nuclear-related facilities should Trump order a resumption of military operations. ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:34:06 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531179/Iran-s-missile-capabilities-have-changed-the-equation-caretaker,2026-10-18 01:46:53
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Lavrov to visit Tehran on Monday for talks with Araghchi,Lavrov to visit Tehran on Monday for talks with Araghchi,"Lavrov to visit Tehran on Monday for talks with Araghchi TEHRAN — Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov will visit Tehran on Monday for talks with his Iranian counterpart, Abbas Araghchi, Russian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Maria Zakharova has announced. TEHRAN — Russian Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov will visit Tehran on Monday for talks with his Iranian counterpart, Abbas Araghchi, Russian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Maria Zakharova has announced. Speaking at a press conference on Friday, Zakharova said the talks would cover a broad range of international and regional issues, with particular attention to developments surrounding Iran and Moscow’s efforts to help ease tensions. She said the current tensions affecting Russia’s friendly countries in West Asia stem from actions by the United States and Israel. Zakharova added that the meeting would focus on implementing agreements reached during recent high-level contacts between Iranian and Russian officials, as well as identifying practical steps to further strengthen bilateral cooperation. The talks will also address the implementation of the Comprehensive Strategic Partnership Agreement between Tehran and Moscow, which provides a framework for expanding cooperation between the two countries across a range of fields.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:32:08 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531178/Lavrov-to-visit-Tehran-on-Monday-for-talks-with-Araghchi,2026-10-18 01:46:54
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Ceasefire must cover all fronts to end regional war, says diplomat","Ceasefire must cover all fronts to end regional war, says diplomat","Ceasefire must cover all fronts to end regional war, says diplomat TEHRAN— Iran has stressed that ending hostilities on all fronts is essential to achieving lasting peace in West Asia, warning that continued fighting in any part of the region would mean the war remains unresolved. TEHRAN— Iran has stressed that ending hostilities on all fronts is essential to achieving lasting peace in West Asia, warning that continued fighting in any part of the region would mean the war remains unresolved. Iranian Deputy Foreign Minister Saeed Khatibzadeh made the remarks in an interview with Lebanon’s Al Mayadeen television network on Friday, emphasizing that an end to Israel’s war on Lebanon was integral to broader efforts to bring the regional conflict to a close. Khatibzadeh, who arrived in Beirut on Wednesday for talks with Lebanese officials, said Iran remained committed to ending Israeli military aggression against Lebanon and had pursued that objective within the framework of the memorandum of understanding reached between Iran and the United States in Islamabad in mid-June. He described Lebanon as one of the key issues discussed in Iran’s engagements with Washington, adding that his visit was intended, in part, to help bring the two sides closer together. During his stay in Beirut, Khatibzadeh held what he described as positive talks with senior Lebanese officials, including Parliament Speaker Nabih Berri, Prime Minister Nawaf Salam, and representatives of the Foreign Ministry. Iran calls for an end to hostilities across the region The Iranian deputy foreign minister stressed that Israel must end its military campaign in Lebanon and across the Levant, arguing that developments on the different regional fronts are closely interconnected. “One of Iran’s condit","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:30:23 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531177/Ceasefire-must-cover-all-fronts-to-end-regional-war-says-diplomat,2026-10-18 01:46:55
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Pezeshkian: Iran’s missile, defense capabilities built on foundations laid by schools, universities","Pezeshkian: Iran’s missile, defense capabilities built on foundations laid by schools, universities","Pezeshkian: Iran’s missile, defense capabilities built on foundations laid by schools, universities TEHRAN — President Masoud Pezeshkian has underscored the contribution of Iran’s schools and universities to the country’s defense and missile capabilities, saying investment in education and younger generations is essential to strengthening national security and safeguarding the country against external threats. TEHRAN — President Masoud Pezeshkian has underscored the contribution of Iran’s schools and universities to the country’s defense and missile capabilities, saying investment in education and younger generations is essential to strengthening national security and safeguarding the country against external threats. Speaking on Saturday at a ceremony inaugurating a series of educational projects, Pezeshkian described education as a foundation of Iran’s scientific and technological progress. “If we are capable of defending our country today, building missiles and standing against threats, it is because our education system and universities have played a role in this path and laid the groundwork for such capabilities,” he said. The president stressed that strengthening Iran’s ability to deter potential aggression requires continued efforts to develop the country’s scientific, educational and technological capacities. Although positive steps have been taken to protect Iran’s territory from threats, he said, more work remains to ensure that adversaries cannot threaten the country’s security. Pezeshkian emphasized that young people are central to achieving this objective, adding that their potential can be realized only if adequate investment provides them with opportunities to learn, innovate and contribute to national development. During the ceremony, the president also paid tribute to those who lost their lives in the Islamic Revolution, particularly student martyrs and the victims","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:25:42 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531176/Pezeshkian-Iran-s-missile-defense-capabilities-built-on-foundations,2026-10-18 01:46:56
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Second supertanker strikes sea mine in Strait of Hormuz: IRGC Navy,Second supertanker strikes sea mine in Strait of Hormuz: IRGC Navy,"Second supertanker strikes sea mine in Strait of Hormuz: IRGC Navy TEHRAN— A second supertanker carrying more than 2 million barrels of crude oil caught fire after striking a sea mine in the Strait of Hormuz, the Islamic Revolution Guard Corps (IRGC) Navy announced, reporting a second such incident within 24 hours. TEHRAN— A second supertanker carrying more than 2 million barrels of crude oil caught fire after striking a sea mine in the Strait of Hormuz, the Islamic Revolution Guard Corps (IRGC) Navy announced, reporting a second such incident within 24 hours. In a statement, the IRGC Navy said the vessel had attempted to navigate an unauthorized route after switching off its positioning and radar systems. According to the statement, the ship had been misled by the “aggressor US military” into attempting the unauthorized passage. It subsequently struck a sea mine, triggering a powerful explosion in the engine room and bringing the vessel to a halt. The announcement followed an earlier report by the IRGC Navy of a similar incident on Friday evening involving another supertanker carrying more than 2 million barrels of crude oil. The force said that the vessel had also disabled its positioning and radar systems while attempting to transit the strait via an unauthorized route. The IRGC Navy reiterated that the Strait of Hormuz was closed and warned vessels against violating Iran’s regulations governing passage through the strategic waterway. It cautioned that ships disregarding the restrictions would “burn in the fire of trust in the US terrorist army.”","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:22:34 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531175/Second-supertanker-strikes-sea-mine-in-Strait-of-Hormuz-IRGC,2026-10-18 01:46:57
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran calls on UNSC to hold Israel accountable,Iran calls on UNSC to hold Israel accountable,"Iran calls on UNSC to hold Israel accountable TEHRAN— Iran has called on the United Nations Security Council to take decisive action to compel Israel to fulfill its obligations under international law, end its military aggression across West Asia, and face accountability for serious violations of international law. TEHRAN— Iran has called on the United Nations Security Council to take decisive action to compel Israel to fulfill its obligations under international law, end its military aggression across West Asia, and face accountability for serious violations of international law. Gholamhossein Darzi, Iran’s ambassador and chargé d’affaires to the United Nations in New York, made the appeal on Friday during the Security Council’s open debate on the situation in the Middle East, warning that Israel’s continued aggression, occupation, and destabilizing activities pose a grave threat to regional and international peace and security. Darzi said the Israeli regime had repeatedly demonstrated disregard for international law and the principles enshrined in the UN Charter, while continuing its military operations and violations despite the announcement of a ceasefire in Gaza. He pointed to Israel’s actions in the Gaza Strip, the occupied West Bank, Lebanon, and Syria, as well as the two wars launched against Iran by Israel and the United States over the past year, as evidence of the urgent need for international accountability. “The Security Council must act decisively to address the root causes of this tragedy, end impunity, compel Israel to fully comply with its obligations under international law and relevant UN resolutions, and bring an end to the decades-long injustice inflicted upon the Palestinian people,” Darzi said. Gaza and Palestine at the center of the crisis Addressing the humanita","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:16:58 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531172/Iran-calls-on-UNSC-to-hold-Israel-accountable,2026-10-18 01:46:57
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iranians rally at Persepolis in defense of national identity after Rubio remarks,Iranians rally at Persepolis in defense of national identity after Rubio remarks,"Iranians rally at Persepolis in defense of national identity after Rubio remarks TEHRAN – Hundreds of people from Fars Province gathered at the UNESCO-registered Persepolis complex on Wednesday afternoon in a rally dubbed “Devotees of Civilization” to protest recent anti-Iran remarks by U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio.
The gathering, held from 15 at Takht-e Jamshid, was aimed at showcasing Iran’s ancient civilization and national identity and conveying a message of resilience to the world.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:14:10 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/photo/531174/Iranians-rally-at-Persepolis-in-defense-of-national-identity,2026-10-18 01:46:58
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Either Security Together or Insecurity Together,Either Security Together or Insecurity Together,"Either Security Together or Insecurity Together TEHRAN – Iranian Foreign Minister Seyed Abbas Araghchi told the 52nd Council of Foreign Ministers of the Organization of Islamic Cooperation in Baghdad that lasting security in the region is indivisible: either states build security together, or they will endure insecurity together. TEHRAN – Iranian Foreign Minister Seyed Abbas Araghchi told the 52nd Council of Foreign Ministers of the Organization of Islamic Cooperation in Baghdad that lasting security in the region is indivisible: either states build security together, or they will endure insecurity together. Speaking on Saturday at the OIC ministerial meeting hosted by Iraq under the theme ""Dialogue and solidarity, two fundamental pillars for promoting peace and sustainable development,"" Araghchi laid out Iran's position on the ongoing war in the Persian Gulf, the Strait of Hormuz, Palestine and Yemen. Araghchi arrived in Baghdad to attend the 52nd session, and was welcomed at the airport by Iraq's Deputy Foreign Minister. Upon arrival at Baghdad International Airport, he paid tribute at the memorial of resistance commanders Lieutenant General Qassem Soleimani and Abu Mahdi al-Muhandis. He opened his address by thanking the Government and people of Iraq, ""our neighbor and brother,"" for hosting the meeting, congratulating Secretary-General Ismail Ould Cheikh Ahmed on his appointment, and thanking Türkiye for its successful chairmanship of the OIC Council of Foreign Ministers. The OIC was founded to give the Islamic Ummah a common voice, he said, recalling that its Charter, like the UN Charter, rests on sovereign equality, territorial integrity, non-interference, peaceful settlement of disputes and refraining from threat or use of force. Those principles, he stressed, ""belong to no single country or gro","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:04:04 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531171/Either-Security-Together-or-Insecurity-Together,2026-10-18 01:46:58
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Tehran seeks rail link to Afghanistan via Uzbekistan as Iran-Kazakhstan freight grows,Tehran seeks rail link to Afghanistan via Uzbekistan as Iran-Kazakhstan freight grows,"Tehran seeks rail link to Afghanistan via Uzbekistan as Iran-Kazakhstan freight grows TEHRAN- The head of the Islamic Republic of Iran Railways, on the sidelines of the two-day summit of ministers from Economic Cooperation Organization (ECO) member states in Kazakhstan, announced a review of obstacles to Iran-Kazakhstan rail cooperation and the issue of connecting Iran’s rail network to Afghanistan via Uzbekistan. TEHRAN- The head of the Islamic Republic of Iran Railways, on the sidelines of the two-day summit of ministers from Economic Cooperation Organization (ECO) member states in Kazakhstan, announced a review of obstacles to Iran-Kazakhstan rail cooperation and the issue of connecting Iran’s rail network to Afghanistan via Uzbekistan. Jabbar-Ali Zakeri, at the two-day ECO ministers’ summit in Kazakhstan, referred to the development of rail infrastructure and the increase in regional transit capacity and emphasized the need to expand transport cooperation among regional countries. The head of the Islamic Republic of Iran Railways, referring to the annual holding of the “New Silk Road” conference by Kazakhstan Railways and the country’s Ministry of Transport, described the main goal of the event as developing transport in the region and strengthening international corridors. Zakeri, referring to the opening last year of the Dostyk route, the second border crossing between Kazakhstan and China, said: “Rail-laying operations are underway on the continuation of this route over a length of 150 kilometers, and the project is expected to become operational next year. This measure can increase the capacity of the East-West corridor.” The Deputy Minister of Transport and Urban Development, stating that Kazakhstan’s rail transit, despite existing restrictions in Russia’s and Belarus’s communications with Europe, has grown by 20 percent to about 30 million tons, described this trend as a sign","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:39:28 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531170/Tehran-seeks-rail-link-to-Afghanistan-via-Uzbekistan-as-Iran-Kazakhstan,2026-10-18 01:46:59
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Tehran, Astana eye expanded Caspian, rail cooperation","Tehran, Astana eye expanded Caspian, rail cooperation","Tehran, Astana eye expanded Caspian, rail cooperation TEHRAN- The transport ministers of Iran and Kazakhstan, while emphasizing the development of transport routes and the use of Caspian Sea capacities, stressed the expansion of trade exchanges and the drafting of a comprehensive document on logistics and infrastructure cooperation between the two countries. TEHRAN- The transport ministers of Iran and Kazakhstan, while emphasizing the development of transport routes and the use of Caspian Sea capacities, stressed the expansion of trade exchanges and the drafting of a comprehensive document on logistics and infrastructure cooperation between the two countries. Farzaneh Sadegh, in Kazakhstan, met with Nurlan Sauranbayev, the country’s Minister of Transport. While appreciating the holding of regional transport events and their proper hosting in Astana, she referred to the roadmap for the eastern route of the North-South Corridor, developed with the participation of Iran, Kazakhstan, Russia, and Turkmenistan, and described the follow-up of the implementation of agreements and the removal of existing obstacles as among the priorities of cooperation between the two countries. Activating the eastern branch of the North-South Corridor, increasing transit capacity, connecting Chabahar Port to the rail network, and developing the China-Kazakhstan-Iran-Europe corridor were among the proposals of the Minister of Transport and Urban Development for expanding transit cooperation. She said: “The roadmap for bilateral cooperation, with emphasis on Iran’s proposed corridors, has been drafted and sent to you, and I hope the ground for signing it will be provided at the earliest opportunity so that it can be implemented more quickly.” The Minister of Transport and Urban Development, at the meeting attended by Zakeri, Head of Iran Railways, and Akba","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:35:41 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531168/Tehran-Astana-eye-expanded-Caspian-rail-cooperation,2026-10-18 01:47:00
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Economy minister stresses accelerating finalization of projects supported by Islamic Development Ban,Economy minister stresses accelerating finalization of projects supported by Islamic Development Ban,"Economy minister stresses accelerating finalization of projects supported by Islamic Development Ban TEHRAN- The Minister of Economic Affairs and Finance emphasized the necessity of accelerating the finalization of approved projects, removing implementation obstacles, and using the Islamic Development Bank’s financing capacities to complete the country’s priority projects. TEHRAN- The Minister of Economic Affairs and Finance emphasized the necessity of accelerating the finalization of approved projects, removing implementation obstacles, and using the Islamic Development Bank’s financing capacities to complete the country’s priority projects. Seyyed Ali Madanizadeh, on the sidelines of the annual meetings of the International Monetary Fund and the World Bank Group in Bangkok, in a meeting with Muhammad Sulaiman Al Jasser, President of the Islamic Development Bank, added: “In this meeting, we exchanged views on the implementation process of projects supported by this bank and ways to strengthen financial and development cooperation.” The Minister of Economic Affairs and Finance stated: “Following up on approved projects and removing obstacles to their implementation, especially in the environmental, urban wastewater, and educational infrastructure development sectors, were among the main axes of these negotiations.” According to the report, the issue of extending the credit validity and re-approving some priority projects whose assessment stages had already been carried out was examined, and both sides emphasized the need to pursue the use of the remaining projected credits to complete projects under implementation. Strengthening banking coordination, finalizing payments related to installments, and facilitating the repayment process of financial obligations were among other issues raised at this meeting; issues whose follow-up can help prevent ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:32:05 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531165/Economy-minister-stresses-accelerating-finalization-of-projects,2026-10-18 01:47:00
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Leader congratulates U23 Greco-Roman team on world title,Leader congratulates U23 Greco-Roman team on world title,"Leader congratulates U23 Greco-Roman team on world title TEHRAN – Ayatollah Seyed Mojtaba Khamenei, Leader of the Islamic Revolution, congratulated Iran's U23 Greco-Roman wrestling team on winning the World Championship title in the United States. TEHRAN – Ayatollah Seyed Mojtaba Khamenei, Leader of the Islamic Revolution, congratulated Iran's U23 Greco-Roman wrestling team on winning the World Championship title in the United States. In a message issued Oct. 17, he extended congratulations to the pride-inspiring champions, their hard-working coaches and the entire Iranian nation, saying the shining of youth, hoisting of Iran's flag and echo of the national anthem reflect radiant hopes paving the way toward a bright and magnificent future.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:27:41 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531166/Leader-congratulates-U23-Greco-Roman-team-on-world-title,2026-10-18 01:47:01
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Vietnam embassy, Iran–Vietnam chamber of commerce chart a path for bilateral trade, investment co-op","Vietnam embassy, Iran–Vietnam chamber of commerce chart a path for bilateral trade, investment co-op","Vietnam embassy, Iran–Vietnam chamber of commerce chart a path for bilateral trade, investment co-op TEHRAN- Vietnamese Ambassador to Iran Nguyen Luong Ngoc and Mr. Seyed Mostafa Mousavi, President of the Iran–Vietnam Joint Chamber of Commerce, met at the Chamber’s headquarters in Tehran on Saturday, together with members of the visiting Vietnamese trade delegation and representatives of Iranian business associations and enterprises, to discuss ways to strengthen bilateral economic, trade and investment cooperation. TEHRAN- Vietnamese Ambassador to Iran Nguyen Luong Ngoc and Mr. Seyed Mostafa Mousavi, President of the Iran–Vietnam Joint Chamber of Commerce, met at the Chamber’s headquarters in Tehran on Saturday, together with members of the visiting Vietnamese trade delegation and representatives of Iranian business associations and enterprises, to discuss ways to strengthen bilateral economic, trade and investment cooperation. During the meeting, Mr. Mousavi highlighted Vietnam’s strong economic potential and expressed interest in expanding cooperation in agriculture, industry, oil and gas, logistics and tourism. He also emphasized the importance of strengthening business ties, promoting investment opportunities and facilitating exchanges of business delegations between the two countries. Ambassador Nguyen Luong Ngoc underscored the need to enhance the exchange of market information, establish connections between reliable business partners and address challenges related to international payments and goods transportation. He stressed the importance of translating cooperation proposals into concrete and practical initiatives. The Ambassador reaffirmed the Embassy of Vietnam’s commitment to working closely with the Iran–Vietnam Joint Chamber of Commerce, business associations and enterprises from both countries to promote substantive, effective and mutually beneficial economic, trade and investment cooperation. A Vietnamese trade delegation arrived in Tehran on Octob","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:10:56 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531164/Vietnam-embassy-Iran-Vietnam-chamber-of-commerce-chart-a-path,2026-10-18 01:47:02
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Students, farmers and the Yellow Jacket movement are taking to the street in France","Students, farmers and the Yellow Jacket movement are taking to the street in France","Students, farmers and the Yellow Jacket movement are taking to the street in France A wave of mass protests swept across France Saturday, with dozens of peaceful marches taking place alongside scenes of violent clashes between demonstrators and police forces, Politico reported. A wave of mass protests swept across France Saturday, with dozens of peaceful marches taking place alongside scenes of violent clashes between demonstrators and police forces, Politico reported. The demonstrations were also a battleground for candidates ahead of next year’s high-stakes presidential election: The far-right’s Marine Le Pen sided with law enforcement while the far-left’s Jean-Luc Mélenchon backed protesters. Throughout the day, media reported incidents in the country’s largest cities including Lyon, Bordeaux, Marseille and Paris. Dozens of rioters clashed with law enforcement on the capital’s Place de la République, next to a much larger number of demonstrators gathered for an authorized march that started from Paris’s central square. “A very large majority of people are protesting without violence,” Paris’s police prefecture said on Saturday afternoon. Students, farmers and members of the Yellow Jacket movement, among others, took to the streets on Saturday in a “convergence of struggles” to protest rising living costs, sluggish wages and deep disagreements with the government. About 500,000 protestors took to the streets across the country, according to the CGT union. France’s interior ministry has yet to release its figures, which are usually lower than counts issued by unions. Saturday’s demonstrations grew out of the student protests that began last month with school blockades and calls for better study conditions, more teachers and more funding. The moveme","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:05:23 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531163/Students-farmers-and-the-Yellow-Jacket-movement-are-taking-to,2026-10-18 01:47:02
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Azerbaijan reignites debate over secularism,Azerbaijan reignites debate over secularism,"Azerbaijan reignites debate over secularism MADRID - A decision by the Azerbaijani government that effectively bans students and teachers from wearing the hijab in educational institutions has sparked a wave of protests. MADRID - A decision by the Azerbaijani government that effectively bans students and teachers from wearing the hijab in educational institutions has sparked a wave of protests. The amendment, approved last month, does not directly ban the Islamic veil. Instead, it prohibits clothing that the government considers to violate the “principle of secularity.” From a Western perspective, secularism is often used to judge the hijab in a way that excludes certain views while supporting others. The hijab is often presented as a sign that women lack freedom and control over their own decisions. Women who wear it are sometimes portrayed as lacking independence and the ability to make their own choices. However, this view does not necessarily reflect the experiences of women who choose to wear the hijab. Instead, it follows a way of thinking that gives priority to values such as visibility and individual freedom as understood within a Western framework. By placing a barrier between the body of an Oriental woman and the Western gaze, the veil appears to put her beyond Western observation and desire. Its covering makes the woman seem mysterious and inaccessible, frustrating the desire to see and understand her. When a veiled woman refuses to be observed, the Western gaze may respond with disappointment and subject her to even greater scrutiny. The portrayal of the Orient and its women as an “enigma” that must be uncovered turns the veil into a central part of this process. The veil becomes ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:32:32 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531161/Azerbaijan-reignites-debate-over-secularism,2026-10-18 01:47:03
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Peace with Israel: A Lebanese illusion?,Peace with Israel: A Lebanese illusion?,"Peace with Israel: A Lebanese illusion? TEHRAN – The occupying Israeli regime continues to wage almost daily aggression against towns and villages in southern Lebanon. TEHRAN – The occupying Israeli regime continues to wage almost daily aggression against towns and villages in southern Lebanon. Israeli Occupation Forces (IOF) fired artillery shells in at least eight areas of southern Lebanon. In the town of Bayada, an IOF tank reportedly shelled Al-Mansouri in Tyre district with several rounds. IOF aggression was also reported in Zawtar al-Sharqiyah, which the regime has been trying to occupy over the past week. The developments have raised questions about the intentions behind the “framework agreement” signed between the Israeli and Lebanese governments on June 26. The Lebanese government has also faced criticism for reaching a direct agreement with Tel Aviv while southern Lebanon remains under the regime’s occupation forces. A recent study published by the Israeli Institute for National Security Studies (INSS) outlines a new security doctrine. While the doctrine has yet to be officially announced, it is already being put into practice, reflecting a broader shift in how the regime views its security mechanisms. The study argues that this new doctrine changes how Israelis understand the relationship between security, war, and peace. The regime no longer sees peace as a lasting strategic goal, but rather as a temporary arrangement. Conflict, by contrast, is increasingly viewed as a permanent condition to be managed rather than brought to an end. At the heart of this new doctrine is a shift in how the Zionist regime views war: no longer as an","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:14:47 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531160/Peace-with-Israel-A-Lebanese-illusion,2026-10-18 01:47:04
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Trump waves Russia sanctions passed by Congress amid deepening row with Ukraine,Trump waves Russia sanctions passed by Congress amid deepening row with Ukraine,"Trump waves Russia sanctions passed by Congress amid deepening row with Ukraine Donald Trump has put on hold a sweeping new sanctions package targeting the Russian economy, telling Congress the pause on the legislation passed by both chambers was in the national interest, the Guardian reported. Donald Trump has put on hold a sweeping new sanctions package targeting the Russian economy, telling Congress the pause on the legislation passed by both chambers was in the national interest, the Guardian reported. In an executive order on Friday, the president said he was waiving many ⁠sanctions, restrictions and duties ⁠on Russia, in a move that comes as he has been publicly criticizing ⁠Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy, including suggesting that Ukraine needs a ​new leader. The move was greeted by Russian presidential envoy Kirill Dmitriev, who wrote on social media: “The Trump administration’s suspension of the Graham Act is an important and truly historic moment.” Trump signed the legislation last month, after Congress passed the measure in an act of rare bipartisan agreement. It sought to clamp down more quickly on the flow of financial resources fueling Russia’s war in Ukraine. The legislation – whose ‌primary backer in ‌Congress was the late senator Lindsey Graham – sanctions Russian officials, banks and a shadow fleet of tankers that keeps Russian energy moving and was due to be implemented in two days. It also directs Trump to impose up to 100% tariffs on the top five importers of Russian oil or natural gas, with an exception for countries that import less than 15% of Russia’s natural gas exports and have taken significant steps to reduce those imports. Friday’s announcement comes a week after Trump said the U.S. had agreed to purchase diesel from Russia to ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:56:22 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531159/Trump-waves-Russia-sanctions-passed-by-Congress-amid-deepening,2026-10-18 01:47:04
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Bomb the Planet, Then Hold a Biodiversity Summit","Bomb the Planet, Then Hold a Biodiversity Summit","Bomb the Planet, Then Hold a Biodiversity Summit As wars continue to devastate ecosystems worldwide, Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has called for peace diplomacy to protect biodiversity, condemning environmental destruction caused by armed conflicts. As wars continue to devastate ecosystems worldwide, Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has called for peace diplomacy to protect biodiversity, condemning environmental destruction caused by armed conflicts.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:16:33 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531156/Bomb-the-Planet-Then-Hold-a-Biodiversity-Summit,2026-10-18 01:47:05
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Intl. Archaeology Day: A glimpse of Iran’s Paleolithic heritage and museums,Intl. Archaeology Day: A glimpse of Iran’s Paleolithic heritage and museums,"Intl. Archaeology Day: A glimpse of Iran’s Paleolithic heritage and museums TEHRAN - On 17 October, archaeologists and cultural institutions worldwide mark International Archaeology Day, highlighting archaeology’s contribution to our understanding of the human past. The occasion also invites reflection on the broader role of archaeology in reconstructing human history, investigating changing relationships between people and their environments, and communicating scientific knowledge to the public through museums and other cultural institutions. TEHRAN - On 17 October, archaeologists and cultural institutions worldwide mark International Archaeology Day, highlighting archaeology’s contribution to our understanding of the human past. The occasion also invites reflection on the broader role of archaeology in reconstructing human history, investigating changing relationships between people and their environments, and communicating scientific knowledge to the public through museums and other cultural institutions. In Iran, this day offers a valuable occasion to recognize a heritage that extends far beyond monumental architecture and written records. Long before the emergence of urban centers, human groups inhabited the Iranian Plateau and its mountain ranges, developed stone-tool technologies and other early technologies, adapted to changing climatic conditions, and exploited a wide range of environments. The Paleolithic represents the longest period of this history, and it places Iran at the center of important debates concerning human evolution, hominin dispersals across Eurasia, and adaptation during the Pleistocene. Situated between Southwest Asia, the Caucasus, Central Asia, and the Indian subcontinent, Iran encompasses a remarkable diversity of landscapes and ecological settings. These environments formed part of the geographical context in which prehistoric populations moved, settled, and adapted to changing conditions. Iran should therefore be understood not just ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:51:12 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531154/Intl-Archaeology-Day-A-glimpse-of-Iran-s-Paleolithic-heritage,2026-10-18 01:47:06
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"Iran proposes joint tourism packages, measurable targets to boost Chinese arrivals","Iran proposes joint tourism packages, measurable targets to boost Chinese arrivals","Iran proposes joint tourism packages, measurable targets to boost Chinese arrivals TEHRAN – Iran has proposed five practical measures to increase Chinese tourist arrivals, including joint travel packages, familiarization tours and direct cooperation between travel agencies, as it seeks to turn longstanding cultural ties with China into tangible tourism business. TEHRAN – Iran has proposed five practical measures to increase Chinese tourist arrivals, including joint travel packages, familiarization tours and direct cooperation between travel agencies, as it seeks to turn longstanding cultural ties with China into tangible tourism business. The proposals were outlined in a message from Iran’s Minister of Cultural Heritage, Tourism and Handicrafts, Seyyed Reza Salehi-Amiri, read at a specialized meeting on strengthening Iran-China tourism cooperation in Beijing on Friday. Salehi-Amiri said that Iran eyes China to be become one of its most important tourism partners, stressing that the success of bilateral cooperation would depend on moving beyond discussions to concrete agreements and actual tourist exchanges. The meeting, hosted by Iran’s embassy in Beijing, brought together officials and representatives of tourism companies from both countries to discuss barriers to bilateral travel, develop joint tourism products and expand cooperation between tour operators. Marking the 55th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Iran and China, Salehi-Amiri described the occasion as an opportunity to advance cooperation from dialogue to implementation. He proposed establishing a joint working group of Iranian and Chinese travel agencies and tour operators, developing at least three travel packages specifically tailored to the Chinese market, and organizing familiarization tours in Iran for Chinese travel agency executives and journalists. The ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:46:48 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531153/Iran-proposes-joint-tourism-packages-measurable-targets-to-boost,2026-10-18 01:47:07
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,"IRCS, ICRC hold workshops to strengthen readiness for CBRN incidents","IRCS, ICRC hold workshops to strengthen readiness for CBRN incidents","IRCS, ICRC hold workshops to strengthen readiness for CBRN incidents TEHRAN – The Iranian Red Crescent Society (IRCS) and the International Red Cross and Red Crescent (ICRC) have held the second and third training courses on Application of Personal Protective Equipment during Chemical, Biological, Radiological, and Nuclear (CBRN) incidents. TEHRAN – The Iranian Red Crescent Society (IRCS) and the International Red Cross and Red Crescent (ICRC) have held the second and third training courses on Application of Personal Protective Equipment during Chemical, Biological, Radiological, and Nuclear (CBRN) incidents. The first round of the course was held in Tehran from June 7 to 21. The second and third courses were held from October 4-8 and 11-15, separately. The courses aimed to improve preparedness and the operational capacity of relief teams and has been attended by a total number of 150 members of rapid response teams from different provinces in the country, ICRC website announced in a press release on October 15. During the closing ceremony, the attendees and instructors reviewed achievements, strengths, and ground for improvement. Stressing the need to repeat the exercises, organize the course in provincial levels, and to provide complementary equipment required, the attendees emphasized that the experience was different from previous maneuvers. The instructors also expressed gratitude for the participants’ active involvement, reiterating their positive performance during practical simulation exercises in applying the learning points and following the decontamination process suited to each type of contamination. Speaking on the sidelines of the ceremony, the head of ICRC’s Tehran Delegation, Marisela Silva Chau, highlighted the close collaboration between ICRC and the Iranian Red Crescent Society, citing the wor","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:51:14 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531148/IRCS-ICRC-hold-workshops-to-strengthen-readiness-for-CBRN-incidents,2026-10-18 01:47:07
Tehran Times,Iran (State),en,Iran puts forward six proposals to boost SCO anti-drug cooperation,Iran puts forward six proposals to boost SCO anti-drug cooperation,"Iran puts forward six proposals to boost SCO anti-drug cooperation TEHRAN – Iran’s Drug Control Headquarters (DCHQ) has put forward six proposals to strengthen cooperation among Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) member states in combating illicit drugs and related crimes. TEHRAN – Iran’s Drug Control Headquarters (DCHQ) has put forward six proposals to strengthen cooperation among Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) member states in combating illicit drugs and related crimes. Mohammad Narimani, an official with the DCHQ, presented the proposals at the opening ceremony of the SCO International Conference of Member States, titled “For a Drug-Free World,” held on October 13–14 in Bishkek, Kyrgyzstan. The event was attended by representatives of the competent authorities of the SCO member states, the SCO Secretariat, the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC), the Collective Security Treaty Organization (CSTO), the Central Asian Regional Information and Coordination Centre (CARICC) and other regional organizations, as well as government bodies, higher education institutions and civil society of the Kyrgyz Republic. Iran’s six proposals included strengthening the regional early warning system on synthetic drugs and new psychoactive substances, promoting cooperation in countering chemical precursors used in illicit manufacturing of narcotic drugs, establishing a SCO specialized network in prevention, treatment, harm reduction, and rehabilitation fields, developing joint capacity-building and educational programs, fostering operational and intelligence collaboration in countering transnational drug trafficking networks, and protecting health and humanitarian services, ISNA reported. Highlighting the need for strengthening regional and i","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:49:30 GMT",https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/531145/Iran-puts-forward-six-proposals-to-boost-SCO-anti-drug-cooperation,2026-10-18 01:47:08
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В Пентагоне предупредили о беспрецедентных за всю историю масштабах вооружения Китая,В Пентагоне предупредили о беспрецедентных за всю историю масштабах вооружения Китая,"В Пентагоне предупредили о беспрецедентных за всю историю масштабах вооружения Китая Реклама Китайстремительно наращивает военный потенциал, а масштабы его программы перевооружения могут оказаться беспрецедентными в мировой истории. Такое заявление сделал главаПентагонаПит Хегсет,передаетForbes. «Наиболее масштабное наращивание военной мощи за всю современную историю, а возможно, и за всю мировую историю, — это то, что Китай строит в Тихом океане. Каждый день мы работаем над тем, чтобы наш департамент был готов предотвратить любые изменения в существующем порядке, которые они могут захотеть внести в первую островную цепь, вторую островную цепь, Южно-Китайское море или в Тихом океане», — сказал глава военного ведомства. Ранее госсекретарьСШАМарко Рубиов интервью NBC Newsзаявил, что Китай обладает второй армией в мире по военной мощи. По его словам, невозможно игнорировать, ","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:36:21 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/v-pentagone-predupredili-o-bespretsedentnyh-za-vsyu-mirovuyu-istoriyu-masshtabah-vooruzheniya-knr/,2026-10-18 01:47:11
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Трамп взял два месяца на оценку последствий от возможных санкций против России,Трамп взял два месяца на оценку последствий от возможных санкций против России,"Трамп взял два месяца на оценку последствий от возможных санкций против России Реклама Госсекретарь Соединенных ШтатовМарко Рубиосообщил, что глава американской администрацииДональд Трампвзял два месяца на тщательную оценку потенциальных эффектов и последствий от введения антироссийских санкций и сопутствующих тарифных ограничений в отношении третьих стран. Его слова приводитТАСС. По словам дипломата, особое внимание в ходе этого анализа будет уделено влиянию подобных мер на национальную и глобальную экономику. Рубио пояснил, что сложность ситуации заключается в том, что ограничительные инициативы затрагивают не толькоМоскву, но и предполагают введение пошлин против ряда других государств, включаяИндию. В связи с этим администрации требуется указанное время для моделирования экономических последствий таких шагов. Необходимость проведения углубленного исследования, по","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:27:55 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/tramp-vzyal-dva-mesyatsa-na-otsenku-posledstviy-ot-vozmozhnyh-sanktsiy-protiv-rossii/,2026-10-18 01:47:13
