Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Премьера Польши раскритиковали после встречи с Зеленским,Премьера Польши раскритиковали после встречи с Зеленским,"Премьера Польши раскритиковали после встречи с Зеленским Реклама ДепутатЕвропарламентаотПольшиЕва Зайончковская-Герник раскритиковала польского премьер-министра Дональда Туска после его заявления о дружбе междуВаршавойиКиевомна встрече с президентомУкраиныВладимиром Зеленским. Она разместила соответствующую публикацию в социальной сетиX. «Туск подчеркивает, что ""никто никогда не изменит эту так называемую дружбу"" — то есть, даже если украинские власти предпримут действия, которые будут противоречить нашим интересам, даже если они будут оскорблять поляков на каждом шагу и громче всех восхвалять убийц польских граждан, он останется привержен этой ""дружбе""», — написала евродепутат. Она подчеркнула, что именно из-за такого отношения Украина превратила Польшу в банкомат, который отдает Киеву все и не требует ничего взамен. Ранее Зайончковская-Герникв","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:43:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/premiera-polshi-raskritikovali-posle-vstrechi-s-zelenskim/,2026-10-18 01:47:29
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Политолог связал дизельную сделку с надеждой Трампа улучшить настроение американцев,Политолог связал дизельную сделку с надеждой Трампа улучшить настроение американцев,"Политолог связал дизельную сделку с надеждой Трампа улучшить настроение американцев Реклама Американский журналист и политолог Джон Вароли в беседе сKP.RUсвязал дизельную сделку с надеждой президентаСШАДональда Трампаулучшить настроение американцев. Вароли отметил, что американский лидер рассчитывал на положительный психологический эффект от сделки для энергетического рынка и биржи, однако пока снижения цен на дизельное топливо не наблюдается. Эксперт констатировал наличие глубокого экономического кризиса в США, из-за чего администрация была вынуждена обратиться к России за помощью. Эксперт прокомментировал внутреннюю политическую ситуацию в США, отметив, что поддержкуКиевуоказывает влиятельная группа либеральных глобалистов. По его словам, на фоне снижения рейтинга Трампа (который, по оценке политолога, составляет около 30 процентов) и риска потери контроля республиканце","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:41:06 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/politolog-svyazal-dizelnuyu-sdelku-s-nadezhdoy-trampa-uluchshit-nastroenie-amerikantsev/,2026-10-18 01:47:31
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Российских школьников начнут учить применять искусственный интеллект,Российских школьников начнут учить применять искусственный интеллект,"Российских школьников начнут учить применять искусственный интеллект Реклама С 1 сентября 2027 года все учащиеся 10-11-х классов будут изучать способы применения технологий искусственного интеллекта (ИИ) в учебном процессе и повседневной жизни. Об этом рассказал экспертМинпросвещения России, директор Института содержания и методов обучения имени В. С. Леднева Максим Костенко, его цитируетРИА Новости. Как пишет агентство, ранее Минпросвещения утвердило федеральный государственный образовательный стандарт для учеников старших классов. Переход на обучение в соответствии с новыми требованиями начнется с 1 сентября 2027 года. «Изменения коснулись и метапредметных результатов. В них теперь включено умение применять технологии искусственного интеллекта», — сказал Костенко. По его словам, это означает, что школы должны будут обеспечить условия, при которых выпускни","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:31:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/rossiyskih-shkolnikov-nachnut-uchit-primenyat-iskusstvennyy-intellekt/,2026-10-18 01:47:33
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Россиянам рассказали о пользе зефира,Россиянам рассказали о пользе зефира,"Россиянам рассказали о пользе зефира Реклама Натуральный зефир на основе желатина содержит природные хондропротекторы, а яблочный пектин в составе десерта обладает антиоксидантной активностью. Об этомRTрассказали в Роскачестве. В состав классического зефира входят сахар, патока, яблочное пюре, яичный белок и натуральные загустители — пектин или агар. При этом яблочное пюре считается обязательным ингредиентом десерта: без него продукт не может называться зефиром, объяснили специалисты Роскачества. В ведомстве отметили, что зефир без глазури содержит 300–330 килокалорий на 100 граммов и не содержит жиров, что позволяет называть его «легкой сладостью» на фоне других десертов. Однако в нем много сахара, поэтому людям с диабетом зефир противопоказан, а при заболеваниях поджелудочной железы его следует употреблять с осторожностью, ","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:12:32 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/rossiyanam-rasskazali-o-polze-zefira/,2026-10-18 01:47:34
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,«Наши дипломаты всегда придут на помощь». Захарова прокомментировала направление ноты в МИД Казахстана из-за ареста рэпера Navai,«Наши дипломаты всегда придут на помощь». Захарова прокомментировала направление ноты в МИД Казахстана из-за ареста рэпера Navai,"«Наши дипломаты всегда придут на помощь». Захарова прокомментировала направление ноты в МИД Казахстана из-за ареста рэпера Navai Реклама Официальный представительМИД РоссииМария Захаровапрокомментировалаобщественную дискуссию, возникшую вокруг действий российских дипломатов в связи с задержанием вКазахстанерэпера Navai (Наваи Бакирова). Ранее стало известно, что Генеральное консульствоРФв Алматынаправилоофициальную ноту в МИД Казахстана после ареста артиста по делу о контрабанде наркотиков. Наши консульские сотрудники — не адвокаты и не следователи, чтобы квалифицировать поступки наших соотечественников за рубежом или заниматься расследованиями, они — всегда и везде — обязаны защищать граждан России во всех без исключения сложных ситуациях за рубежом Их прямая обязанность, закрепленная в Конституции России и Консульском уставе, — обеспечивать защиту прав российских граждан в любых сложных обстоятельствах за пределам","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:12:29 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/long-nashi-diplomaty-vsegda-pridut-na-pomosch-zaharova-prokommentirovala-napravlenie-noty-v-mid-kazahstana-iz-za-aresta-repera-navai/,2026-10-18 01:47:36
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Стало известно о попытке ВСУ стабилизировать фронт на глуховском участке,Стало известно о попытке ВСУ стабилизировать фронт на глуховском участке,"Стало известно о попытке ВСУ стабилизировать фронт на глуховском участке Реклама КомандованиеВооруженных силУкраины(ВСУ) попыталось стабилизировать фронт на глуховском участке в Сумской области. Об этом в беседе сТАССзаявил подполковник Народной милиции Луганской Народной Республики в отставкеАндрей Марочко. «На глуховский участок украинское преступное военно-политическое руководство отправило несколько спецподразделений, которые должны были, по их мнению, стабилизировать ситуацию», — рассказал военный эксперт. Он подчеркнул, что ситуация не изменилась и, следовательно,Киевуне удалось реализовать замысел. Ранее Марочкосообщил, что ВСУ проводят контратаки на двух участках у населенного пункта Омельник в Запорожской области, при этом российские военные отражают все попытки наступления.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:04:59 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/stalo-izvestno-o-popytke-vsu-stabilizirovat-front-na-gluhovskom-uchastke/,2026-10-18 01:47:38
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Посол России оценил готовность Молдавии расследовать инциденты с БПЛА,Посол России оценил готовность Молдавии расследовать инциденты с БПЛА,"Посол России оценил готовность Молдавии расследовать инциденты с БПЛА Реклама Молдавияготова расследовать инциденты с пролетом беспилотных летательных аппаратов (БПЛА) в стране. Об этом в эфиреRTсообщил российский посол вКишиневеОлег Озеров. Как указал дипломат, пролеты дронов могли быть инсценированы украинскими спецслужбами. По его словам, всплеск подобных инцидентов в странахНАТОобычно происходит тогда, когда Запад согласует антироссийские меры. «Сейчас такие форумы по всей Европе проводятся, особенно в странах Восточного блока, примыкающих к российской территории. И совершенно очевидно, что вся эта антидроновая истерия привязана к разжиганию агрессивных настроений в отношении нашей страны», — заявил Озеров. Ранее пресс-секретарь президента РФВладимира ПутинаДмитрий Песковзаявил, что Молдавии для возобновления диалога с Россией необходимо отказаться от ли","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:35:20 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/posol-rossii-otsenil-gotovnost-moldavii-rassledovat-intsidenty-s-bpla/,2026-10-18 01:47:39
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Иван Золо раскрыл причину своего задержания,Иван Золо раскрыл причину своего задержания,"Иван Золо раскрыл причину своего задержания Реклама Блогер Иван Золо (настоящее имя —Иван Золочевский) прокомментировал инцидент на концерте вДонецке. В своемTelegram-канале он рассказал, что был задержан за видеозапись, где он был запечатлен в футболке с запрещенной символикой. По словам Золо, еще в 2022 году он купил футболку, а потом снял в ней видео. На ней была изображена символика сатанизма (международное движение сатанизма признано экстремистским и запрещено вРФ). «Я лично об этом не знал. Теперь же мне сказали, что было нарушение. Незнание закона не освобождает от ответственности, поэтому я полностью признал свою вину за эту ситуацию, обязуюсь удалить все видео, связанные с данной атрибутикой», — написал блогер. Он также пообещал утилизировать футболку с запрещенной символикой и рассказал, что сейчас с ним все в порядке. Кро","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:29:01 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/ivan-zolo-raskryl-prichinu-svoego-zaderzhaniya/,2026-10-18 01:47:41
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Экс-советник Трампа призвал прекратить выделять деньги Зеленскому,Экс-советник Трампа призвал прекратить выделять деньги Зеленскому,"Экс-советник Трампа призвал прекратить выделять деньги Зеленскому Реклама ПрезидентУкраиныВладимир Зеленскийбольше не должен получить ни цента из средств американских налогоплательщиков. Об этом на своей странице в соцсетиХнаписал экс-советник президентаСШАДональда Трампапо нацбезопасностиМайкл Флинн. Он возмутился поведением украинского лидера и обвинил его в неуважении к американскому президенту. По мнению Флинна, Зеленский ведет себя так, будто поддержка со стороны США ему полагается по праву. «Этот мелкий неблагодарный мерзавец не должен больше получить ни цента из средств американских налогоплательщиков. Хватит это терпеть. У нас самих здесь, дома, полно проблем, чтобы еще тратить силы на поддержку этого скользкого типа», — написал экс-советник. Флинн также заявил, что американцы устали поддерживать украинского лидера. «На самом деле он — кто угодно","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:26:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/eks-sovetnik-trampa-prizval-prekratit-vydelyat-dengi-zelenskomu/,2026-10-18 01:47:43
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Депутат Рады назвал преемника Зеленского,Депутат Рады назвал преемника Зеленского,"Депутат Рады назвал преемника Зеленского Реклама Выборы наУкраинепроводиться не будут, после действующего лидераВладимира Зеленскогострану возглавить может только спикер парламента. Об этом заявил депутатВерховной радыАртем ДмитруквTelegram-канале. «Никаких назначений глав Украины не будет ... Мы не можем назначить никого президентом вместо Зеленского. Им может стать только глава парламента — все, других вариантов нет», — написал Дмитрук. Он пояснил, что слова американского лидераДональда Трампао необходимости проведения выборов на Украине направлены лишь на отстранение Зеленского, а не на избрание нового лидера. Ранее пресс-секретарь президента РоссииВладимира ПутинаДмитрий Песковзаявил, чтоМоскваготова приостановить удары по Украине в день выборов, еслиКиевна них решится.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:19:10 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/deputat-rady-nazval-preemnika-zelenskogo/,2026-10-18 01:47:44
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Рыбалка во Флориде закончилась смертельной схваткой с аллигатором,Рыбалка во Флориде закончилась смертельной схваткой с аллигатором,"Рыбалка во Флориде закончилась смертельной схваткой с аллигатором Реклама Во Флориде (штат США) 71-летний мужчина погиб после нападения почти четырехметрового аллигатора. Это второй смертельный случай с участием этого вида хищников в штате с начала 2026 года. Об этом сообщаетABC News. По данным полиции, Стивен Хэмилтон рыбачил недалеко от озера Апопка, примерно в 24 километрах отОрландо. Нападение произошло в пятницу, 16 октября, около 17:00 по местному времени. Аллигатор схватил мужчину и утащил в воду. Спасательная операция осложнилась присутствием других аллигаторов. Тело погибшего удалось извлечь примерно через два часа после происшествия. Предполагаемого нападавшего — аллигатора длиной около 3,6 метра — поймали и усыпили специалисты. Ранее в этом же штате ребенок чудомвырвалсяиз пасти аллигатора после того, как заплыл в зону, где купание запрещено. ","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:16:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/rybalka-vo-floride-zakonchilas-smertelnoy-shvatkoy-s-alligatorom/,2026-10-18 01:47:46
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Политолог связал миграционные проблемы Франции с последствиями колониальной политики,Политолог связал миграционные проблемы Франции с последствиями колониальной политики,"Политолог связал миграционные проблемы Франции с последствиями колониальной политики Реклама Член правления Российской ассоциации политической наукиВладимир Шаповаловв беседе с RTвысказалмнение, что текущие миграционные проблемы во Франции являются прямым следствием исторической колониальной политики Парижа. По словам эксперта, одним из основных источников миграционных потоков в страну являетсяАлжир. Шаповалов напомнил, что в XIX веке Франция вела кровопролитную войну за установление контроля над территориями в Северной Африке. В результате коренное население было насильственно вытеснено с наиболее плодородных земель для размещения французских переселенцев. В период колониальной зависимости права алжирцев подвергались жестким ограничениям, что к началу XX века спровоцировало формирование национально-освободительного движения. Политолог отметил, что во время Второй мировой ","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:07:51 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/politolog-svyazal-migratsionnye-problemy-frantsii-s-posledstviyami-kolonialnoy-politiki/,2026-10-18 01:47:48
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Появились подробности задержания блогера Ивана Золо,Появились подробности задержания блогера Ивана Золо,"Появились подробности задержания блогера Ивана Золо Реклама Силовики вошли в клуб вДонецке, где проходил концерт российского блогера Ивана Золо (настоящее имя —Иван Золочевский), примерно через 20 минут после того, как он вышел на сцену. Об этом сообщаетTelegram-канал Baza. По его информации, блогера задержали прямо на сцене во время исполнения одной из песен. Сперва посетители концерта подумали, что происходящее является частью шоу, однако позднее им сообщили, что концерт отменяется. «Силовики также проверяли документы и соблюдение возрастных ограничений», — говорится в сообщении. Причина задержания пока не раскрывается. Уточняется, что 18 октября Золо должен был выступить вМариуполе, однако теперь неизвестно, состоится ли концерт. О задержании блогерастало известнов ночь на 18 октября.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:57:49 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/poyavilis-podrobnosti-zaderzhaniya-blogera-ivana-zolo/,2026-10-18 01:47:49
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Захарова прокомментировала направление ноты в МИД Казахстана из-за ареста рэпера Navai,Захарова прокомментировала направление ноты в МИД Казахстана из-за ареста рэпера Navai,"Захарова прокомментировала направление ноты в МИД Казахстана из-за ареста рэпера Navai Реклама Официальный представительМИД РоссииМария ЗахаровавTelegram-канале прокомментировала общественную дискуссию, возникшую вокруг действий российских дипломатов в связи с задержанием вКазахстанерэпера Navai (Наваи Бакирова). Ранее стало известно, что Генеральное консульствоРФв Алматынаправилоофициальную ноту в МИД Казахстана после ареста артиста по делу о контрабанде наркотиков. Захарова подчеркнула, что консульские работники не являются адвокатами или следователями, чья задача заключается в правовой квалификации действий соотечественников или проведении собственных расследований. Их прямая обязанность, закрепленная в Конституции России и Консульском уставе, — обеспечивать защиту прав российских граждан в любых сложных обстоятельствах за пределами страны, независимо от характера произош","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:53:40 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/zaharova-prokommentirovala-napravlenie-noty-v-mid-kazahstana-iz-za-aresta-repera-navai/,2026-10-18 01:47:51
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Три летевших из Турции в Москву самолета развернулись из-за ограничений,Три летевших из Турции в Москву самолета развернулись из-за ограничений,"Три летевших из Турции в Москву самолета развернулись из-за ограничений Реклама Из-за ограничений, действующих в московском аэропорту Внуково, три самолета, летевших изТурциив столицу России, развернулись надПольшейиЛитвой. Об этом сообщаетТАССсо ссылкой на источник. «Три летевших в московский аэропорт Внуково самолета изАнтальи,Стамбулаи Измира развернулись обратно, находясь в воздушном пространстве Польши и Литвы», — говорится в сообщении. По данным собеседника агентства, все рейсы сейчас направляются в сторону стамбульского аэропорта имени Сабихи Гекчен, где будет решаться вопрос о повторном вылете вМосквуили пересадке пассажиров на другие рейсы. Вечером 17 октября мэр МосквыСергей Собянинсообщалоб уничтожении 12 украинских беспилотников, летевших на столицу.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:51:04 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/tri-letevshih-iz-turtsii-v-moskvu-samoleta-razvernulis-iz-za-ogranicheniy/,2026-10-18 01:47:53
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,«Будет продолжаться». Зеленский сделал заявление о снятии санкций США с России,«Будет продолжаться». Зеленский сделал заявление о снятии санкций США с России,"«Будет продолжаться». Зеленский сделал заявление о снятии санкций США с России Реклама Отмена американских ограничений против России не остановится на дизельной сделке. Об этомзаявилукраинский лидерВладимир Зеленский. Снятие санкций будет продолжаться По словам президентаУкраины, договоренностьМосквыиВашингтонапо дизелю является лишь первым шагом в этом процессе. 9 октября президент РоссииВладимир Путини его американский коллегаДональд Трампдоговорилисьо поставках российского дизельного топлива на американский и мировой рынки. Как отметил Путин, эта договоренность поможет стабилизировать ситуацию в мировой экономике. Зеленскийвозмутилсярешением президентаСШАДональда Трампа не использовать законЛиндси Грэма(внесен в перечень террористов и экстремистовРосфинмониторинга)против России. К сожалению, принято решение полностью проигнорировать закон Линдси Грэма По его слова","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:42:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/17/budet-prodolzhatsya-zelenskiy-sdelal-zayavlenie-o-prodolzhenii-snyatiya-ssha-sanktsiy-s-rossii/,2026-10-18 01:47:55
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Спецпредставитель Путина объяснил упадок Запада неспособностью исправлять ошибки,Спецпредставитель Путина объяснил упадок Запада неспособностью исправлять ошибки,"Спецпредставитель Путина объяснил упадок Запада неспособностью исправлять ошибки Реклама Запад столкнулся с упадком из-за неспособности обсуждать и исправлять просчеты в миграционной и энергетической политике. Об этом спецпредставитель президента России Владимира Путина по инвестиционно-экономическому сотрудничеству с зарубежными странами и глава РФПИ Кирилл Дмитриев написал на своей странице в соцсетиX. «Запад пришел в упадок из-за неспособности обсудить и исправить серьезные ошибки в сферах миграции, энергетики и разжигания войн», — объяснил Дмитриев. Так он ответил на публикацию пользователя, в которой, судя по описанию, показаны кадры протестов во французском Марселе. Ранеесообщалось, что более полумиллиона человек приняли участие в субботу в манифестациях по всей Франции против роста стоимости жизни и повышения цен. Позже стало известно, что протестующиеподожглизд","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:41:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/spetspredstavitel-putina-ob-yasnil-upadok-zapada-nesposobnostyu-ispravlyat-oshibki/,2026-10-18 01:47:56
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Блогера Ивана Золо задержали во время концерта в Донецке,Блогера Ивана Золо задержали во время концерта в Донецке,"Блогера Ивана Золо задержали во время концерта в Донецке Реклама Российского блогера и музыканта Ивана Золо (настоящее имя —Иван Золочевский) задержали во время его концерта вДонецке. Об этом сообщаетРЕН ТВ. Как пояснили в администрации клуба, где проходило выступление, Золо, а также его команду и посетителей концерта подвергли проверке. Другие подробности не приводятся. Блогер или его представители пока не комментировали ситуацию. В феврале 2026 года вСевастополезапретилипроведение концерта Ивана Золо. Решение было принято из нравственных соображений и ради безопасности потенциальных посетителей мероприятия.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:41:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/blogera-ivana-zolo-zaderzhali-vo-vremya-kontserta-v-donetske/,2026-10-18 01:47:57
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,В США назвали два шага для завершения конфликта на Украине,В США назвали два шага для завершения конфликта на Украине,"В США назвали два шага для завершения конфликта на Украине Реклама Бывший глава Национального центраСШАпо борьбе с терроризмом Джо Кент назвал условия, которые, по его мнению, необходимы для завершения конфликта наУкраине. Он высказался об этом в эфиреYouTube-каналаГленна Диесена. Как указал аналитик, чтобы прекратить украинский конфликт, Соединенные Штаты должны предпринять два шага. «Во-первых, существенно сократить поддержку, которую мы оказываем украинцам. Во-вторых, изменить наши отношения с другими странамиНАТОи утвердить свою роль доминирующей силы в альянсе», — сказал Кент. По его словам, если какая-нибудь из стран-участниц НАТО решит в одностороннем порядке проводить иную политику по отношению кКиеву, ей следует заниматься этим «вне рамок альянса». Ранее американский лидерДональд Трампвыступилс критикой в адрес своего предшественникаДжо Б","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:20:46 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/v-ssha-nazvali-dva-shaga-dlya-zaversheniya-konflikta-na-ukraine/,2026-10-18 01:47:59
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,США предложили Европе возобновить закупку российского газа,США предложили Европе возобновить закупку российского газа,"США предложили Европе возобновить закупку российского газа Реклама Администрация президента СШАДональда Трампапредложила Европе возобновить закупку российского газа. Как сообщаетThe New York Times(NYT) со ссылкой на источники,Вашингтонпредлагает пойти на это в рамках мирного соглашения по завершению украинского конфликта. По данным издания, с таким предложением к европейским и украинским чиновникам выступили американские переговорщики Стив Уиткофф иДжаред Кушнер. Уточняется, чтоКиевупредложили возобновить экспорт газа из России по газопроводам, которые ранее использовались для его поставки в Европу. По мнению американской стороны, благодаря этому Европа сможет получать более дешевые энергоресурсы, аУкраина, в свою очередь, будет получать доход от транзита газа. Кроме того, убеждены представителиСША, такой шаг поспособствует достижению мирного урег","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:18:11 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/ssha-predlozhili-evrope-vozobnovit-zakupku-rossiyskogo-gaza/,2026-10-18 01:48:01
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Стало известно о системе подземных туннелей ВСУ в Доброполье,Стало известно о системе подземных туннелей ВСУ в Доброполье,"Стало известно о системе подземных туннелей ВСУ в Доброполье Реклама Украинские подразделения оборудовали в Доброполье в Донецкой Народной Республике (ДНР) около 12 подземных туннелей для скрытого перемещения, их обнаружили военные Вооруженных сил (ВС) России. Об этом рассказал начальник разведки 110-й гвардейской бригады 51-й гвардейской общевойсковой армии группировки войск «Центр» с позывным Удав, его цитирует агентствоРИА Новости. По его словам, подземные ходы появились еще до начала продвижения российских подразделений. Они соединяли частные дома и позволяли военным перемещаться между берегами реки по скрытым маршрутам. Боец также сообщил, что украинские военнослужащие использовали высотные здания для наблюдения за передвижениями российских подразделений. Кроме того, они занимали подвалы и укрывались на территориях промышленных объектов. Ранее ","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:13:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/stalo-izvestno-o-sisteme-podzemnyh-tunneley-vsu-v-dobropolie/,2026-10-18 01:48:02
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Протесты в Париже обернулись погромом штаб-квартиры киберспортивного клуба,Протесты в Париже обернулись погромом штаб-квартиры киберспортивного клуба,"Протесты в Париже обернулись погромом штаб-квартиры киберспортивного клуба Реклама Во время беспорядков в Париже протестующие разгромили штаб-квартиру киберспортивного клуба Team Vitality. Об этом сообщило киберспортивное изданиеDust2.dk. Участники беспорядков разбили окна здания, вынесли оборудование и игровые кресла. Часть вещей затем подожгли прямо на улице. По данным издания, из офиса также забрали чемпионские трофеи клуба. Обстоятельства произошедшего и полный размер ущерба пока не установлены. Инцидент произошел 17 октября на фоне массовых протестов во Франции, сопровождавшихся столкновениями с полицией, поджогами и разграблением магазинов. Team Vitality пока не комментировали произошедшее. Число протестующих во Франциипревысилополмиллиона. Столкновения демонстрантов с полицией, беспорядки и погромы произошли в нескольких городах Франции, в том числе в Пари","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:11:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/17/protesty-v-parizhe-obernulis-pogromom-shtab-kvartiry-kibersportivnogo-kluba/,2026-10-18 01:48:04
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,"День отца в России в 2026 году: суть, история, традиции, идеи для подарков","День отца в России в 2026 году: суть, история, традиции, идеи для подарков","День отца в России в 2026 году: суть, история, традиции, идеи для подарков Указом президента Владимира Путина в 2021 году День отца был учрежден для укрепления статуса отца в семье и обществе. С тех пор его ежегодно празднуют в третье воскресенье октября. Подробности об истории и традициях Дня отца в России, а также идеи подарков папе — в материале «Ленты.ру». Реклама 18 октября 2026 года россияне отмечают День отца. Указом президентаВладимира Путинав 2021 году праздник был учрежден для укрепления статуса отца в семье и обществе. С тех пор его ежегодно празднуют в третье воскресенье октября. Подробности об истории и традициях Дня отца в России, а также идеи подарков папе — в материале «Ленты.ру». Традиционно День отца в России отмечают в третье воскресенье октября. В 2026 году День отца в России отмечают в воскресенье, 18 октября Считается, чтоДень отцав начале XX векапридумалаамериканка Сонора Луиза Смарт Додд. Потеряв мать в 16 лет, она осталась на попечении отца, ветерана гражданской войны Уильяма Джексона Смарта. Кроме Соноры, Уильям в одиночку воспитал еще пятерых детей, так и не женившись повторно. Однажды, уже будучи взрослой, Сонора посе","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:10:15 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/den-ottsa-v-rossii-2026-godu-sut-istoriya-traditsii-idei-dlya-podarkov/,2026-10-18 01:48:06
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,18 октября: какой праздник отмечают в России и мире,18 октября: какой праздник отмечают в России и мире,"18 октября: какой праздник отмечают в России и мире 18 октября в России отмечают День памяти войсковой казачьей славы, в мире — Международный день галстука и Всемирный день менопаузы. Православные вспоминают святителя Петра Московского. Подробнее о торжествах, приметах и знаменитых именинниках, родившихся 18 октября, — в материале «Ленты.ру». Реклама 18 октября в России отмечают День памяти войсковой казачьей славы, в мире — Международный день галстука и Всемирный день менопаузы. Православные вспоминают святителя Петра Московского. Подробнее о торжествах, приметах и знаменитых именинниках, родившихся 18 октября, — в материале «Ленты.ру». В состав российского войска казакивошлив 1570 году. С тех пор они принимали участие во многих судьбоносных сражениях, в том числе на полях Отечественной войны 1812 года и в ключевых битвах Великой Отечественной. 18 октября стал праздником казачьего войска еще при императоре Николае I, в 1813 году. Позже, в СССР, торжество перестали официально отмечать. Возродили праздник уже в современной России — в 2000 году, по инициативе войскового казачьего общества «Всевеликое войско Донское». Первые упоми","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:05:02 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/18-oktyabrya-kakoy-prazdnik-otmechayut-v-rossii-i-mire/,2026-10-18 01:48:08
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Африканские Мальдивы. Спрос россиян на Маврикий вырос в разы. Сколько стоит тур на самый безопасный остров в мире?,Африканские Мальдивы. Спрос россиян на Маврикий вырос в разы. Сколько стоит тур на самый безопасный остров в мире?,"Африканские Мальдивы. Спрос россиян на Маврикий вырос в разы. Сколько стоит тур на самый безопасный остров в мире? Реклама Маврикий— островное государство в юго-западной части Индийского океана — в 2026 году стал притягивать в разы больше россиян. Несмотря на высокий чек за отдых и ограниченность в выборе досуга, путешественники мечтают попасть на этот курортный африканский остров, а туроператоры уженареклиего новой альтернативой Мальдивам. Что так привлекает россиян и сколько сегодня стоят туры на один из самых безопасных островов мира — выяснила «Лента.ру». Как сообщил «Интерфаксу» глава управления по туризму страны (MPTA) Бенуа Хартер, только с января по май Маврикий посетили 16 тысяч туристов из России. Для сравнения: за весь 2025 год на острове отдохнули 25 тысяч соотечественников. Особенно активно курортоминтересуютсясостоятельные путешественники. В издании «Турдом» считают, что ВИП-туристы в пос","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:01:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/long-mauritus/,2026-10-18 01:48:09
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Белый дом объяснил отказ Трампа от новых санкций против России,Белый дом объяснил отказ Трампа от новых санкций против России,"Белый дом объяснил отказ Трампа от новых санкций против России Реклама Американский лидерДональд Трампотказался применять ограничения в отношении России, которые были предусмотрены принятым в сентябре законом, так как это бы препятствовало усилиям Соединенных Штатов по урегулированию конфликта наУкраине. Об этом заявила представитель Белого дома Тейлор Роджерс, передает порталAxios. «Применение санкционных положений сейчас будет препятствовать текущим усилиямСШАпо заключению прочного и всеобъемлющего мирного соглашения между Украиной и Россией», — сказала Роджерс. Президент США, подчеркнула она, ясно дал понять, что желает завершить украинский конфликт, а также оставляет за собой право воспользоваться полномочиями в любое время, если это необходимо для продвижения национальных интересов. Ранее Трампотказалсяввести несколько положений из «адских санкци","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:55:38 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/belyy-dom-ob-yasnil-otkaz-trampa-ot-novyh-sanktsiy-protiv-rossii/,2026-10-18 01:48:11
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Макрон выступил с заявлением о протестах,Макрон выступил с заявлением о протестах,"Макрон выступил с заявлением о протестах Реклама ПрезидентФранцииЭммануэль Макронзаявил, что устроившие погромы на протестах будут привлечены к ответственности. Он написал об этом в социальной сетиX. Макрон подчеркнул, что во Франции «нет места насилию». «Те, кто крушил все вокруг, нападал на префектуры и магазины, грабил — вплоть до зданий мэрий, — будут привлечены к ответственности и наказаны», — говорится в заявлении. Французский лидер также выразил поддержку правоохранителям и отметил, что все будут «едины в борьбе с сеятелями хаоса, которые стремятся разрушить наши институты и помешать мирным протестующим выражать свои требования». Ранеесообщалось, что в Париже из-за предстоящих протестов закрыли несколько станций метро. 17 октября — первый день школьных каникул во Франции, из-за чего в нескольких регионах страны наблюдаются","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:44:00 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/18/makron-vystupil-s-zayavleniem-o-protestah/,2026-10-18 01:48:12
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Лидеры ЕС обсудили возможность предоставления Украине нового кредита на 70 миллиардов евро,Лидеры ЕС обсудили возможность предоставления Украине нового кредита на 70 миллиардов евро,"Лидеры ЕС обсудили возможность предоставления Украине нового кредита на 70 миллиардов евро Реклама ЛидерыЕвросоюза(ЕС) не смогли договориться об источнике дополнительного финансированияУкраинына 2027 год в размере 70 миллиардов евро. Вопрос обсуждался на саммите ЕС вБрюсселе. Об этомсообщаетPolitico. Во время саммита президент УкраиныВладимир Зеленскийзаявил, что военные расходы страны в следующем году достигнут 155 миллиардов евро, и попросил европейские государства выделить дополнительные средства. По данным издания, среди рассматриваемых вариантов — новый совместный кредит, привлечение средств от стран за пределами ЕС и использование средств европейского бюджета. Также участники саммита вновь обсуждали возможность задействовать замороженные российские активы, общий объем которых оценивается примерно в 300 миллиардов евро. Однако согласовать конкретную схему финансирования не ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:34:08 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/17/lidery-es-obsudili/,2026-10-18 01:48:14
Lenta (RU),Russia,ru,Овечкин приблизился к еще одному рекорду НХЛ,Овечкин приблизился к еще одному рекорду НХЛ,"Овечкин приблизился к еще одному рекорду НХЛ Реклама Передача российского нападающегоАлександра Овечкинапомогла «Вашингтон Кэпиталс» обыграть «Нью-Джерси» в матче регулярного чемпионата Национальной хоккейной лиги (НХЛ). Об этом сообщаетРИА Новости. Встреча завершилась со счетом 4:2 (1:1, 3:0, 0:1) в пользу «Вашингтона». Российский нападающий провел на льду 13 минут 57 секунд, нанес один бросок в створ ворот и записал в актив голевую передачу. Для 41-летнего Овечкина она стала 761-й в карьере в НХЛ. До клубного рекорда по результативным передачам, который принадлежит Никласу Бэкстрему остается одна передача. На счету последнего 762 передачи. Ранее Овечкинзаявил, что нынешний сезон станет последним в его карьере в НХЛ. Контракт 41-летнего нападающего с «Вашингтоном» заканчивается 30 июня 2027 года.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:29:40 +0300",https://lenta.ru/news/2026/10/17/ovechkin-priblizilsya-k-esche-odnomu-rekordu-nhl/,2026-10-18 01:48:16
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Protesters clash with police in downtown Milan (VIDEOS),Protesters clash with police in downtown Milan (VIDEOS),"Protesters clash with police in downtown Milan (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad40d7d203027188f0f8d08.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Police clashed with protesters in Milan and Bologna during nationwide rallies over rising living costs <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647343-protesters-clash-with-police-milan/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Italian police have deployed tear gas and water cannons during clashes with protesters in Bologna and Milan amid nationwide demonstrations against the rising cost of living. Organized by Italia in Piazza, a movement of students and young workers, the rallies began across Italy on Saturday to protest high fuel and energy prices, soaring rents, low wages, and deteriorating healthcare and education. Demonstrators also voiced opposition to military spending. In Milan, where more than 5,000 people joined the march, participants carried a banner demanding“more money for families, less for wars.”In Genoa, crowds waved Palestinian flags and carried anti-war placards, calling for more funding for schools and housing rather than weapons. While initially peaceful, the rally in Milan turned violent when demonstrators reached police cordons in the city center. Masked protesters threw stones and homemade explosive devices at officers, who responded with charges that split up the march. Camionette dei carabinieri e della polizia costrette a indietreggiare. La situazione in Piazza Duomo va fuori controllo https://t.co/WR4MaWZJLt Clashes spread to the area outside Milan’s iconic Duomo Cathedral, where protesters hurled metal barriers and trash bins and set barricades made from cafe tables on fire. Make sure to inform everyone you know that the migrant gangs and their Antifa allies are also rioting in Milan, Italy tonight Building are vandalized and fires are set in front of Milan Cathedral (t","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:21:40 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647343-protesters-clash-with-police-milan/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:19
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Iran offers US deal to reopen Hormuz within a week,Iran offers US deal to reopen Hormuz within a week,"Iran offers US deal to reopen Hormuz within a week <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad3e75685f540707d6c7d57.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Tehran says it could reopen the Strait of Hormuz within a week if Washington accepts its peace plan, which Trump previously rejected <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647342-iran-double-down-hormuz-deal/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Iran could restore normal shipping through the Strait of Hormuz within a week if Washington accepts a peace plan proposed by Tehran last month, Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi has said. The terms were previously rejected by US President Donald Trump. The Islamic Republic remains“committed to safe and secure navigation in the Strait of Hormuz,”Araghchi told a ministerial meeting of the Organization of Islamic Cooperation on Saturday, blaming disruptions to shipping through the key waterway on the“aggressive actions”of the US and Israel. ”Through Qatar, we have conveyed a concrete seven-day plan: if the necessary conditions are met, the Strait can be reopened and normal maritime passage restored within seven days,” the minister said.“The choice now rests with the United States.” “This issue will not be resolved on the battlefield. Peace cannot be built through threats of annihilation,”Araghchi added. Tehran has offered to restore navigation through the crucial oil shipping route in exchange for Washington lifting its naval blockade, easing restrictions on Iranian oil exports and releasing some frozen Iranian assets. Iran is also demanding an end to hostilities“on all fronts,”including Israel’s military operations in Gaza and Lebanon. Last month, Trump rejected Iran’s terms as“unacceptable.”He argued that the US retained full control over the strait and held a stronger negotiating position, while Iran was desperate to reach an agreement because it was“losing so badly.” The US pr","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:36:54 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647342-iran-double-down-hormuz-deal/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:19
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Two supertankers hit mines in Strait of Hormuz – IRGC (VIDEO),Two supertankers hit mines in Strait of Hormuz – IRGC (VIDEO),"Two supertankers hit mines in Strait of Hormuz – IRGC (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad3c52485f5405c1c50eb98.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Two oil supertankers hit naval mines in the Strait of Hormuz on Saturday, Iran’s IRGC has told RT <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647340-two-tankers-hormuz-mines-irgc/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Two oil supertankers struck naval mines and caught fire in the Strait of Hormuz on Saturday, Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) has told RT. Both vessels were carrying about two million barrels of crude oil, Iranian state media reported. The incidents come amid a wave of attacks on tankers and cargo ships in the region in recent weeks, as talks between the US and Iran remain stalled and tensions persist. One tanker was reportedly struck by a mine on Saturday morning. The second vessel was immobilized when the mine strike triggered an explosion in its engine room, the IRGC Public Relations Office said. Both tankers had switched off their positioning and radar systems before attempting to transit the Strait of Hormuz via routes unauthorized by Tehran, it said. The news comes just days after a container ship sank in the key waterway following what Tehran described as a mine strike. All 21 crew members escaped unharmed. Iran has demanded that all ships using the Strait of Hormuz first obtain permits from its newly established maritime authority, which was formed in May to formalize control over the waterway. The US has also struck commercial shipping as part of its naval blockade of Iranian ports, which it imposed in July following the breakdown of talks with Iran. Last week, US forces disabled the Panama-flagged bulker Ocean Molica in the Gulf of Oman after accusing it of attempting to breach the blockade. US forces have destroyed ten tankers allegedly linked to the","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:55:44 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647340-two-tankers-hormuz-mines-irgc/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:20
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Zelensky treating Europe as his ‘personal ATM’ – MEP,Zelensky treating Europe as his ‘personal ATM’ – MEP,"Zelensky treating Europe as his ‘personal ATM’ – MEP <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad39cb285f5406ca94b451b.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Vladimir Zelensky treats Europe like a personal ATM, Italian MEP Roberto Vannacci has said after Kiev’s latest €70 billion request <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647339-zelensky-europe-personal-atm-vannacci/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Italian far-right MEP Roberto Vannacci has accused Vladimir Zelensky of treating Europe like an“ATM”after the Ukrainian leader requested another €70 billion ($79 billion) in aid. Zelenskydemandedmore money on Friday, just months after the EU approved a massive €90 billion loan to support Ukraine through 2027.“The war will cost 155 billion euros next year. And we need at least 70 billion euros more from you – for defense, for weapons, and for our resilience. This is a realistic amount,”he said at an EU summit in Brussels. Vannacci said Italian taxpayers should not have to foot the bill for further aid to Kiev. “Zelensky has found some suckers who give him all the billions he asks for, so he just keeps on asking for more,”the MEP said in a video on social media on Friday. He argued that Zelensky’s demands have continued to mount, citing Kiev’s alleged budget shortfalls of €27 billion in 2026 and €32 billion in 2027, followed by a fresh €70 billion demand on top of the €90 billion loan approved in April. He’s come to view us as Ukraine’s personal ATM. Slovak Prime Minister Robert Fico has also rejected the proposed funding, stressing that Bratislava would not participate in another EU financial mechanism for Ukraine. Hungary has adopted a similar position, Fico said, according to Slovakia’s TASR news agency on Friday. Slovakia, Hungary, and the Czech Republic secured exemptions from the financial obligations of the previous €90 billion loan, which EU leaders agreed late las","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:27:34 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647339-zelensky-europe-personal-atm-vannacci/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:21
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,French city hall goes up in flames amid nationwide unrest (VIDEOS),French city hall goes up in flames amid nationwide unrest (VIDEOS),"French city hall goes up in flames amid nationwide unrest (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad3ed4d85f5406f2c415a82.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Police fired tear gas as tens of thousands rally across France over living costs and education funding <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647334-france-tear-gas-nationwide-protests/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The bell tower of the 143-year-old town hall in the French city of Limoges collapsed on Saturday evening after the building was set ablaze amid nationwide protests over the rising cost of living. The incident came as clashes between police and demonstrators escalated across France, with officers firing tear gas as tens of thousands took to the streets demanding economic relief and education reform. The unrest followed weeks of student-led protests that began last month at a high school in Creteil, near Paris, over teacher shortages and deteriorating school facilities. Initially focused on education reform, improved learning conditions and increased funding, the movement has since converged with broader demonstrations against inequality and the rising cost of living. Labor unions have also joined the protests amid opposition to the government’s proposed 2027 budget and concerns over public spending cuts. In Limoges, a city in west-central France, masked protesters set fire to the 19th-century town hall, AFP reported, citing a regional official. Videos circulating on social media show the building’s bell tower giving way and collapsing as flames engulf its supports. The fire caused extensive damage, with the roof collapsing onto the lower floors and much of the facade destroyed. Local officials described the historic building as largely destroyed. No injuries were reported among those who had been inside. 🔴🇫🇷🔥 ALERTE INFO | Le clocher de la mairie de Limoges s’est effondré. htt","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:46:59 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647334-france-tear-gas-nationwide-protests/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:21
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Wired for War: Israeli firm ran global surveillance operation through online ads, investigation finds","Wired for War: Israeli firm ran global surveillance operation through online ads, investigation finds","Wired for War: Israeli firm ran global surveillance operation through online ads, investigation finds <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad386d585f5407b961c30ca.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Discover-Tech exploited digital advertising infrastructure to track targets and deliver spyware, according to two research teams <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647337-israel-spy-online-ads/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Israeli ad tech company Discover-Tech exploited online advertising infrastructure to track targets and help deliver spyware to dozens of devices belonging to Al Jazeera staff and members of other entities, according to investigations by the Canadian cybersecurity watchdog Citizen Lab and New York-based ad security firm Confiant. The researchers said Discover-Tech used a sprawling network of online ads to identify potential targets, monitor their activity and facilitate the compromise of their devices. “The core finding is the weaponization of ad infrastructure for advanced staging, preliminary targeting, and payload delivery, characterized by exceptional technical sophistication, robust anti-interception measures, and surgical micro-targeting,”Confiant said in its findings. Devices belonging to staff at the international news network Al Jazeera were among those infected through malicious ad placements, which operated silently, without visible pop-ups or suspicious links. The Qatar-based media network condemned“the spyware attacks targeting a number of its staff,”describing them as an“assault on press freedom,”and called for those responsible to be held accountable. The investigation also linked the malicious activity to Israeli spyware developer Candiru, which has been blacklisted by the US and rebranded as Integrity Labs, and Israeli surveillance technology provider Intelos. The companies allegedly exploited ad inventory on major platforms","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:45:53 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647337-israel-spy-online-ads/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:22
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,What if NATO’s ‘Theory of Victory’ is a recipe for disaster?,What if NATO’s ‘Theory of Victory’ is a recipe for disaster?,"What if NATO’s ‘Theory of Victory’ is a recipe for disaster? <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad37f6d85f5407985415db9.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> NATO’s ‘Theory of Victory’ aims to deter Russia. Could its 2029 readiness target turn defense preparations into a case for war? <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647336-natos-theory-of-victory/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByDmitry Kornev, military expert, founder and author of the MilitaryRussia project ByDmitry Kornev, military expert, founder and author of the MilitaryRussia project On October 5, 2026, at the Warsaw Security Forum, NATO’s Supreme Allied Commander Europe (SACEUR) Alexus Grynkewich unveiled a military strategy titled ‘Theory of Victory’. The strategy covers the next few years and outlines NATO’s preparations to counter a potential“Russian attack.”While the details are likely classified, the main points have been made public. Here are the key publicly disclosed aspects of NATO’s ‘victory’ plan: That’s the ‘theory of victory’; now, it has to be put into practice. Certain types of political documents don’t present any interest as long as they’re stored in bureaucratic folders – no one cares about numbers, timelines, logistics, and readiness levels. But once they enter the public domain, they quickly acquire symbolic meaning. A“defense plan”becomes a“war plan,”“deterrence”turns into“targeting,”and a simple date on a calendar becomes a prophecy. This is precisely the case with this strategy. Formally, NATO’s plan doesn’t contain anything sensational: it talks about strengthening the eastern flank, preparing equipment and resources, expanding exercises, aligning industrial capabilities with evolving needs, setting readiness targets, integrating air and missile defense systems, creating logistical routes, and developing crisis response scenarios. All of this has been part of NATO’s a","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:27:47 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647336-natos-theory-of-victory/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:23
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,China urges Israel to rethink its policies,China urges Israel to rethink its policies,"China urges Israel to rethink its policies <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad36de385f540707d6c7d39.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> China has called on Israel to halt settlement expansion in the occupied West Bank, warning of a worsening humanitarian crisis in Gaza <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647333-china-urges-israel-to-rethink-west-bank/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi has urged Israel to halt and reverse the establishment of settlements in the occupied West Bank, describing the Palestinian issue as the“greatest historical injustice of this century,”according to a ⁠statementreleased by Beijing following his meeting with Israeli President Isaac Herzog.The two officials met on Thursday on the sidelines of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia (CICA) summit in Baku, Azerbaijan.Wang said achieving peace and reconciliation in the Middle East remained a cornerstone of Chinese foreign policy, stressing that a two-state solution was the only viable path toward resolving the Israeli-Palestinian conflict. The Chinese diplomat also warned that the humanitarian situation in Gaza remained critical despite the ceasefire reached a year ago.“The immediate priority is to fully open access to Gaza,”Wang said, arguing that two million civilians must not be left struggling to survive or exposed to a worsening humanitarian catastrophe.He added that Israel should“stop and reverse”its efforts to forcibly establish settlements in the West Bank.Herzog, meanwhile, said Israel wanted peace but continued to face“security threats.”In aposton X, he claimed Iran and its regional allies were the primary dangers.The meeting comes amid continued Israeli settlement expansion in the West Bank, which Israel occupied during the 1967 Six-Day War. Most countries consider the settlements illegal under international ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:03:26 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647333-china-urges-israel-to-rethink-west-bank/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:23
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump weighs in on Ukraine’s Starlink access,Trump weighs in on Ukraine’s Starlink access,"Trump weighs in on Ukraine’s Starlink access <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad36e362030276c4f42b4b5.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US President Donald Trump has denied that he or Elon Musk was involved in restricting Ukraine’s access to Starlink satellite services <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647327-trump-musk-ukraine-starlink/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump claimed on Friday that he did not order restrictions on Ukraine’s military access to Starlink satellite services, adding that he did not believe SpaceX CEO Elon Musk had done so either. Ukrainian state and military officials earlier this week accused SpaceX of abruptly restricting access to Starlink satellite communications services and Starshield, its military-grade version, which Kiev relies on for frontline drone operations. Musk responded that Starshield is owned and controlled by the US government. The billionaire stressed that Starlink should be used only for civilian and defensive purposes, arguing that employing its systems for offensive operations would be“inappropriate for a commercial company.” The development followed US President Donald Trump stepping up pressure on Ukraine’s Vladimir Zelensky to halt strikes on Russian oil refineries, which he blames for surging global energy prices. Trump has also repeatedly urged the Ukrainian leader to hold a long-overdue presidential election. At the same time, Washington lifted sanctions on Russian diesel exports following talks with the Kremlin, prompting criticism from Zelensky. On Friday, the US President stated that he waived penalties aimed to target Moscow’s economy and countries purchasing Russian energy, which had been signed into law just a month ago. “Well, I don’t know if it was anybody because it wasn’t me, and I don’t think it was Elon,”Trump said when asked who had been behind the all","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:55:41 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647327-trump-musk-ukraine-starlink/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:24
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Italy launches probe against Israeli defense minister,Italy launches probe against Israeli defense minister,"Italy launches probe against Israeli defense minister <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad32fe72030275fa6203f3a.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Italy has launched a probe against Israeli Defense Minister Israel Katz over alleged abuse of Gaza-bound aid flotilla activists <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647328-italy-israel-katz-gaza/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Italy has expended its probe into the alleged torture and sexual abuse of activists from the Gaza-bound aid flotilla by Israel’s security forces to include Israeli Defense Minister Israel Katz and twelve other high-ranking military, police and prison officials, the Rome Public Prosecutor’s Office has said. Israel intercepted dozens of yachts in international waters and arrested more than 800 volunteers from various countries in October 2025 and May 2026, who were attempting to break West Jerusalem’s naval blockade of the Palestinian enclave. They were held for days before being deported. The investigation was launched by Rome earlier this year after some 50 Italian nationals, who were part of the Global Sumud Flotilla missions, complained about being mistreated in Israeli detention, among other things reporting at least 15 cases of sexual abuse and rape. The probe had initially beeen centered on the country’s far-right national security minister Itamar Ben-Gvir. A similar inquiry was initiated by France. The Rome prosecutor's office said in a statement on Friday that the case against the Israeli officials concerns suspected torture, kidnapping, personal injury, robbery and damage. The activists detained after the 2025 mission reported beatings, injuries, death threats, insults and accusations of terrorism, the statement read. The participants of the second mission claimed to have been subject to even harsher treatment by Israeli security forces, including beatings in the dark","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:24:44 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647328-italy-israel-katz-gaza/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:25
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump waives ‘bone-crushing’ Russia sanctions,Trump waives ‘bone-crushing’ Russia sanctions,"Trump waives ‘bone-crushing’ Russia sanctions <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad2e7dc203027365f79e391.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump has waived sweeping new sanctions against Russia under a law named after Senator Lindsey Graham, citing US national interests. <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647324-trump-waives-graham-sanctions-russia/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has suspended sweeping new sanctions against Russia that he signed into law just a month ago, invoking a national-interest exemption to waive penalties targeting Moscow’s economy and countries purchasing Russian energy. In an executive order issued on Friday, Trump waived sanctions and tariffs mandated by the Lindsey O. Graham Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act, including proposed 500% tariffs on imports from Russia and 100% tariffs on major buyers of Russian oil and gas. “I have submitted to the Congress a certification that the issuance of such a waiver is in the national interests of the United States and a report explaining the basis for the certification,”Trump wrote. China and India, the two largest buyers of Russian crude oil, were expected to be among the countries hardest hit by the legislation. The bill, championed by the late Senator Lindsey Graham, has been described by supporters as a“bone-crushing”measure aimed at driving Russian energy exports out of the global market. Hawkish US lawmakers argued that existing restrictions had allowed Moscow to circumvent economic pressure. Trump lifted sanctions on Russian diesel exports earlier this month in an effort to curb rising energy prices ahead of the US midterm elections. The move sparked outrage in Ukraine and among America’s European allies, prompting a bipartisan group of US senators to accuse Trump of betraying Kiev. According to US media reports, Trump decided to ease sanctions after Ukrai","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:48:49 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647324-trump-waives-graham-sanctions-russia/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:26
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump defies Western critics over Putin’s G20 invitation,Trump defies Western critics over Putin’s G20 invitation,"Trump defies Western critics over Putin’s G20 invitation <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad2d43285f5407985415d7d.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Trump says he would welcome Putin at the G20 summit in Miami despite criticism of his outreach to Moscow from European allies <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647323-trump-welcomes-putin-g20/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has said he would welcome Russian President Vladimir Putin at the upcoming G20 summit in Florida, despite efforts by Ukraine and other European countries to isolate Moscow. After returning to office in early 2025, Trump broke ranks with many of his Western allies, who had suspended high-level meetings with Russia over the Ukraine conflict. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio confirmed last month that Putin had been invited to the summit, scheduled for December 14–15 in Miami. “I don’t know if he’s coming. I would certainly love to have him,”Trump told reporters on Friday when asked whether the Russian leader would attend. Putin’s spokesman, Dmitry Peskov, said last month that the Kremlin was grateful for the invitation but had yet to decide whether Putin would attend. He added that Russia would“actively participate in the work of the G20.” The invitation drew criticism from EU officials and a bipartisan group of US senators.“It’s clearly, I think, the wrong path to normalize people who are starting wars,”said Kaja Kallas, the EU’s top diplomat. Trump: I would certainly love to have Putin at the G20. I don’t know if he’s coming. https://t.co/nc7NJMRESQ Trump has defended his engagement with Moscow as part of his efforts to end the Ukraine conflict. Following a phone call with Putin earlier this month, Trump lifted sanctions on Russian diesel exports in an effort to curb rising energy prices ahead of the US midterm elections. The move drew further critic","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:51:12 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647323-trump-welcomes-putin-g20/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:26
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,October 7 becomes Netanyahu’s ‘political kryptonite’ – RT reports (VIDEO),October 7 becomes Netanyahu’s ‘political kryptonite’ – RT reports (VIDEO),"October 7 becomes Netanyahu’s ‘political kryptonite’ – RT reports (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad27e6085f5407985415d69.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israeli PM Benjamin Netanyahu is facing mounting allegations over ignored warnings before the October 7 Hamas attack, RT reports <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647288-israel-netanyahu-elections-hamas/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is facing mounting accusations that he ignored warnings ahead of the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack, as a bitter blame game over one of Israel’s worst security failures emerges in the final weeks of the election campaign. Former Shin Bet chief Ronen Bar has filed a defamation suit against Netanyahu, accusing him of falsely blaming intelligence officials for the attack despite receiving repeated alerts about security threats. The Hamas-led assault killed around 1,200 people in southern Israel, with another 251 taken hostage. Israel’s subsequent military offensive in Gaza has killed more than 74,000 Palestinians, according to the local health authorities. Bar is seeking nearly $1 million in damages, claiming he warned the prime minister of growing danger in the months preceding the assault. He says a long trail of documents will expose Netanyahu’s account of events as false. “Israel’s worst disaster has become political kryptonite,”RT correspondent Charlotte Dubenskij reported from Jerusalem on Friday, as the country prepares to vote on October 27. Netanyahu, however, maintains that Bar failed to alert him to the imminent threat on the morning of the attack, despite discussing warning signs with senior military officials. He has accused the former intelligence chief of failing to take measures that could have prevented the bloodshed. Further questions have been raised by Netanyahu’s former military secretary, Avi Gil, w","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:23:47 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647288-israel-netanyahu-elections-hamas/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:27
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump’s press secretary out after just five days,Trump’s press secretary out after just five days,"Trump’s press secretary out after just five days <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad2b1d685f540707d6c7d24.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Katie Zacharia is leaving as White House press secretary after just five days amid criticism of her debut briefing and legal credentials <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647321-trump-press-secretarey-leaves/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Katie Zacharia is stepping down as US President Donald Trump’s press secretary after just five days on the job, the White House confirmed on Friday. A conservative political commentator, Zacharia has faced widespread criticism over her handling of her debut press briefing and allegations that she misrepresented her legal credentials. Trump cast doubt on Zacharia’s future in the role while speaking to reporters outside the White House.“Honestly, if I were you, I’d reconsider,”he said, adding that he had spoken to her shortly beforehand.“Katie, do you need this? I don’t think you need this.” Several hours later, White House communications director Steven Cheung said Zacharia would be“transitioning into a new role that will be announced at a later date.” Zacharia posted a photo of herself with Trump in the Oval Office on X, saying that“it was an honor to work for him.” President Trump is a kind, wonderful, gracious, thoughtful, enthusiastic, and hardworking man. I wish more Americans appreciated him. No one will ever make America great the way he has and continues to. It was an honor to work for him. https://t.co/Tp4NizrhE2 According to the New York Times, Zacharia largely read from a script during her first and only press briefing on Tuesday and ended the Q&A session after just five and a half minutes. Critics also accused her of misrepresenting herself as a lawyer after she failed to confirm whether she had passed a US bar exam. Zacharia later claimed to have passed a bar exam","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:36:04 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647321-trump-press-secretarey-leaves/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:28
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"Zelensky’s diesel burnout, Nord Stream on trial, Russiagate revived: RT stories that shaped the week","Zelensky’s diesel burnout, Nord Stream on trial, Russiagate revived: RT stories that shaped the week","Zelensky’s diesel burnout, Nord Stream on trial, Russiagate revived: RT stories that shaped the week <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad311b12030272fbf13cc8d.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> RT looks at this week’s top stories, including the rift between Donald Trump and Vladimir Zelensky, and the return of the ‘Russiagate’ hoax <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647296-rt-top-stories-zelensky-trump-nord-stream/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> This week did not start well for Ukrainian leader Vladimir Zelensky, who was apparently blindsided by US President Donald Trump’s decision to suspend sanctions on Russian diesel supplies after talks with the Kremlin. The deal won’t alleviate the global diesel shortage, but it’salready cooling speculative marketsand easing pressure on Trump ahead of next month’s midterm elections. For Zelensky, it’s a“diplomatic nightmare,”asRussian analyst Sergey Poletaev wrote for RT. Trump rubbed salt in the wound on Saturday when he openly suggested that Ukrainians“get a new leader who can make a deal”and halt attacks on Russian oil refineries. Russian President Vladimir Putin,Trump went on to claim,“wants to make a deal more than Zelensky.” Backed into a corner, Zelenskybegan throwing haymakers. Accusing the American president of empathizing with dictators, Zelensky demanded air defense missiles from the US before vowing to continue his drone campaign against Russia’s refineries – with or without American support. The US apparently sent a warning signal to Zelensky bythrottling the Ukrainian military’s accessto SpaceX’s high-speed Starlink and Starshield satellite communications services, which are vital tools in guiding attack drones used against Russia, and in detecting incoming retaliatory strikes.Neither Trump nor SpaceX CEO Elon Muskwould take responsibility for the communications drop-off, but even if they had, their ","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:19:32 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647296-rt-top-stories-zelensky-trump-nord-stream/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:28
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Israeli settlers beat up and rob WaPo journalist in West Bank (VIDEOS),Israeli settlers beat up and rob WaPo journalist in West Bank (VIDEOS),"Israeli settlers beat up and rob WaPo journalist in West Bank (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad293e8203027365f79e38c.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> WaPo photo journalist Heidi Levine has been attacked by violent Israeli settlers in the West Bank <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647319-israeli-settlers-wapo-journalist/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Washington Post photographer Heidi Levine has been badly beaten by Israeli settlers and stripped of her equipment while covering attacks on Palestinians harvesting olives in the occupied West Bank. The assault occurred on Friday near the village of Abu Falah, the latest in an ongoing string of attacks staged by organized settler groups. Masked settlers have repeatedly attacked Palestinian villages, hurling stones and setting orchards on fire in an apparent effort to disrupt the autumn harvest. The Israeli military, which is usually present, has taken little to no action against the settlers. Levine, a veteran photographer who has covered conflicts across the Middle East and elsewhere for decades, was caught in a settler charge on the Palestinians. The mob threw the journalist, who was wearing a blue protective vest clearly marked ‘PRESS,’ to the ground, repeatedly kicking her while stealing her cameras and phone. “They just kept kicking me and kicking me, like probably 50 times,”Levine told reporters after the incident. Footage from the scene shows the immediate aftermath, with Levine seen prone on the ground after the settlers were repelled by the villagers. The journalist was badly shaken but apparently spared more serious injuries thanks to her protective vest and helmet. Severe settler + soldier attack on olive harvesters in Abu Falah. American WaPo journalist Heidi Levine badly wounded. Machine gunfire—at least one Palestinian shot. Tear gas. Soldiers assaulting journali","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:15:32 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647319-israeli-settlers-wapo-journalist/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:29
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump’s first attorney general pick accused of sex trafficking,Trump’s first attorney general pick accused of sex trafficking,"Trump’s first attorney general pick accused of sex trafficking <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad24d7c85f5406ca94b44e8.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Two women have sued former US Representative Matt Gaetz, accusing him and other defendants of running a sex trafficking ring <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647315-trump-first-attorney-general-pick-accused-sex-trafficking/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Two women have filed a federal lawsuit accusing former US Representative Matt Gaetz, President Donald Trump’s first pick for attorney general, of participating in a sex trafficking ring while serving in Congress. Gaetz has faced similar allegations for years, and has denied any wrongdoing. The lawsuit,filed in Florida on Thursday, alleges that Gaetz and several other men, including former Seminole County Tax Collector Joel Greenberg and former Florida legislator Christopher Dorworth, sexually exploited the plaintiffs between 2017 and 2019. The women, identified as Jane Doe 1 and Jane Doe 2, are seeking unspecified damages under the federal Trafficking Victims Protection Act. According to the complaint, Greenberg recruited financially vulnerable young women through the dating website SeekingArrangement.com and introduced them to Gaetz. The lawsuit alleges that Gaetz had sex with Jane Doe 1 and a 17-year-old girl at a July 2017 party where narcotics were distributed. He allegedly paid the minor $400 in cash and transferred $500 to Jane Doe 1 three days later. Gaetz and Greenberg subsequently made at least 19 payments to Jane Doe 1, ranging from $150 to $1,000, the complaint claims. Jane Doe 2 alleged that she first had sex with Gaetz in exchange for money in October 2017. The plaintiffs also accused the defendants of providing drugs and financing trips to Miami, Las Vegas, the Bahamas and other destinations in exchange for sex. The men allegedly use","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:42:35 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647315-trump-first-attorney-general-pick-accused-sex-trafficking/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:30
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Saudi Arabia’s biggest problem may be its enemy’s smallest weapons,Saudi Arabia’s biggest problem may be its enemy’s smallest weapons,"Saudi Arabia’s biggest problem may be its enemy’s smallest weapons <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad24e972030272aa063ff02.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Saudi Arabia spends over $82 billion on defense, yet Houthi drones and missiles keep threatening its oil facilities and airports <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647309-saudi-arabia-ansar-allah/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByFarhad Ibragimov– lecturer at the Faculty of Economics at RUDN University, expert and lecturer at the Department of Political Science, Faculty of Social Sciences and Mass Communications, Financial University under the Government of the Russian Federation ByFarhad Ibragimov– lecturer at the Faculty of Economics at RUDN University, expert and lecturer at the Department of Political Science, Faculty of Social Sciences and Mass Communications, Financial University under the Government of the Russian Federation The Houthis continue to strike Saudi Arabia despite Riyadh’s threats of a forceful response and promises to enlist outside partners to defend the kingdom. By targeting airports and oil infrastructure, Ansar Allah is seeking to raise the cost of Saudi involvement in Yemen’s conflict and force the kingdom’s leadership to reconsider the terms of a settlement. The latest wave of Houthi attacks has targeted facilities of particular importance to Saudi Arabia. On the evening of October 13, a strike hit Saudi Aramco’s headquarters in Dhahran, home to the company’s key management operations. The Saudi Energy Ministry reported a fire, though miraculously no one was killed. Ansar Allah also claimed strikes on an oil refinery in Riyadh and King Khalid International Airport. The choice of targets suggests the Houthis want to put virtually all of the kingdom’s oil revenue at risk and disrupt its international air connections. These targets also suggest that the movement is trying ","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:03:43 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647309-saudi-arabia-ansar-allah/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:30
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump-Putin diesel deal fractures West on Russia – ex-Austrian FM,Trump-Putin diesel deal fractures West on Russia – ex-Austrian FM,"Trump-Putin diesel deal fractures West on Russia – ex-Austrian FM <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad25ac820302777762dfc71.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US diesel deal with Moscow has exposed divisions in the West’s anti-Russian stance, ex-Austrian Foreign Minister Karin Kneissl says <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647317-trump-putin-diesel-deal-west/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Washington’s diesel deal with Moscow has exposed divisions within the West over its anti-Russian stance, as the US shifts toward a more pragmatic approach, former Austrian Foreign Minister Karin Kneissl has said. US President Donald Trump announced the agreement with Russian President Vladimir Putin last week, easing sanctions on Russian diesel imports until April 2027 in an effort to bring down soaring fuel prices. The move marks a departure from the Western sanctions policy imposed on Moscow since the escalation of the Ukraine conflict in February 2022. Speaking to TASS on Friday, Kneissl described the agreement as more than a“symbolic breakthrough,”pointing to the 300,000 tons of Russian diesel expected to reach the US and global markets by November. “The EU says that this undermines the West’s united position. However, one could also say that this marks a shift by the US toward a more pragmatic approach, while the EU continues to pursue a purely ideological line,”she stated. The agreement has drawn criticism from European leaders attending a two-day EU summit in Brussels this week. Czech Prime Minister Andrej Babis accused Trump of sidelining the bloc, telling reporters that“Trump, by doing that business with Putin, stabbed us in the back. We have to do something.” Bulgarian Prime Minister Rumen Radev, however, welcomed the agreement, arguing that lower fuel prices were essential to Europe’s economic competitiveness.“Any step in reducing fuel prices and to g","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:52:42 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647317-trump-putin-diesel-deal-west/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:31
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,From Russian oil to Starlink: How the US is redrawing its Ukraine playbook,From Russian oil to Starlink: How the US is redrawing its Ukraine playbook,"From Russian oil to Starlink: How the US is redrawing its Ukraine playbook <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad22de72030276d9570949a.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Donald Trump is ramping up pressure on Ukraine after Zelensky ignored his warnings on striking Russian oil refineries <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647287-russian-oil-starlink-trump-pressure-zelensky/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The administration of US President Donald Trump has ramped up pressure on Ukraine to halt strikes on Russian oil refineries while pursuing landmark diplomacy with Moscow in a bid to bring down soaring fuel prices at home and revive stalled peace negotiations. The overtures have left Vladimir Zelensky fuming, reigniting the bitterest public confrontation between the two since their explosive Oval Office showdown in 2025. Zelensky has fiercely criticized Trump’s Russian diesel deal and defied his demands to stop attacking Russian refineries, saying he feels“betrayed”by Washington. In response, the US president branded the Ukrainian leader“not a good guy for us to deal with,”while suggesting that Ukraine needs a“new president,”referring to Zelensky’s long-expired presidential term. As the dispute escalated, American officials reportedly threatened to restrict intelligence sharing and weapons supplies to Kiev, while Ukrainian commanders sounded the alarm about serious disruptions to the Starlink network, which the military heavily relies on for logistics, reconnaissance, and drone control. Trump’s peace push has also put him on a collision course with Zelensky’s EU backers. US negotiators reportedly proposed unfreezing some Russian sovereign assets – an idea categorically rebuffed in Brussels. Zelensky then attempted to drum up support at a slightly farcical summit in Brussels where he demanded EU and NATO membership; both of which have been rejected outright","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:32:49 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647287-russian-oil-starlink-trump-pressure-zelensky/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:32
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Zelensky imposes refinery deal demand – WSJ,Zelensky imposes refinery deal demand – WSJ,"Zelensky imposes refinery deal demand – WSJ <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad2225d85f5405c1c50eb39.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Ukraine is open to stopping attacks on Russian oil refineries in exchange for extended Starlink coverage, the Wall Street Journal has said <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647299-ukraine-starlink-zelensky-refineries/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Vladimir Zelensky is open to stopping attacks on Russian oil refineries for 100 days in exchange for a 300 km extension of Starlink satellite internet service coverage for the Ukrainian military, the Wall Street Journal has said. The report comes as US President Donald Trump has ramped pressure on Zelensky to end the strikes, which he blames for surging global energy prices. In his interview with Newsmax on Thursday, Trump called Ukraine’s actions“a disgrace.” In an article published the same day, the WSJ said that Republican Senators Roger Wicker and Kevin Cramer brought the deal to the Ukrainian leader during their visit to Kiev last Friday. The outlet claimed that it was told by unnamed sources that Zelensky had agreed to the proposal. The extended Starlink coverage should help Ukraine target missile launchers inside Russia, according to the report. Kiev, which is experiencing an acute shortage of US-supplied Patriot air defense missiles, has been struggling to contain Russia’s large-scale missile and drone strikes against military-related infrastructure across Ukraine. Moscow says the raids are being carried out in response to Ukrainian terrorist attacks on civilian targets in Russia, including energy facilities. The Ukrainians, who have relied heavily on Starlink during the conflict with Russia for battlefield communications and controlling drones, have been“terrified”by the slowdown of satellite internet provided by Elon Musk’s SpaceX company this week, the WSJ said.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:13:00 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647299-ukraine-starlink-zelensky-refineries/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:33
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Nuremberg at 80: How do you put a death machine on trial?,Nuremberg at 80: How do you put a death machine on trial?,"Nuremberg at 80: How do you put a death machine on trial? <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad203b22030277188123150.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Inside the Nuremberg trials: the legal battles, defense strategies and evidence that brought down Hitler’s men <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647265-nuremberg-at-80-nazis-hanged/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> On the night of October 16, 1946, 10 individuals were hanged in the Nuremberg prison. These were the main Nazi criminals who had been captured and brought to trial. Despite the horrifying scale and brutality of the crimes, the Nuremberg Trials remain one of the most controversial proceedings in world history. The idea of an international tribunal to address Nazi atrocities had been considered for some time. In 1942, the Soviet Union established a special Extraordinary Commission that gathered information about these crimes. Tragically, it had a lot of work to do. The USSR became the primary battleground for the bloodiest and most brutal war in Europe. The range and nature of the crimes committed on Soviet soil were staggering: genocide against multiple peoples, mass killings on various grounds, all sorts of war crimes, deliberate attacks on medical facilities and civilian infrastructure, arbitrary executions, economic exploitation, and sexual violence. Essentially, every town liberated from the Nazis had enough evidence to warrant its own tribunal. When the concentration camps were liberated, it became clear that Allied propaganda had not exaggerated but rather understated the extent of Nazi atrocities. In addition to the Soviet government, the exiled governments of occupied countries – Belgium, Czechoslovakia, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Poland, Norway, France, and Yugoslavia – also wanted to hold the Nazis legally accountable for their crimes. The outlines of the future tr","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:29:28 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647265-nuremberg-at-80-nazis-hanged/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:33
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,EU summit: Zelensky gets promises but no money – As it happened,EU summit: Zelensky gets promises but no money – As it happened,"EU summit: Zelensky gets promises but no money – As it happened <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad212db85f540561e1ac11e.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> EU leaders have pledged continued support but failed to reach a new funding deal with Ukraine’s Vladimir Zelensky at the Brussels summit <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647286-zelensky-begging-bowl-eu-summit/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Vladimir Zelensky has emerged from the EU summit in Brussels with fresh promises of support but no deal on the additional €70 billion ($79 billion) he is demanding for Ukraine. Instead, European leaders tasked the European Commission with finding ways to meet Kiev’s growing financial needs, leaving the question of who will foot the bill unanswered.The Ukrainian leader arrived in Brussels following a bitter public falling-out with US President Donald Trump over Washington’s decision to ease sanctions on Russian diesel supplies. His demands have put further pressure on Kiev’s European backers, who are already struggling with soaring energy costs, strained budgets and the prospect of a difficult winter. The summit also failed to break the deadlock over frozen Russian sovereign assets held in Belgium. German Chancellor Friedrich Merz continued to push for the funds to be used to support Kiev, despite his unpopularity at home, while flatly rejecting aUS proposalto include them in a peace settlement. After the talks, Merz acknowledged that“there were no decisions, but there was an exchange of views,”warning that the €90 billion loan already agreed for Ukraine“will not be enough.”This live feed has now ended. 16 October 2026 Merz’s insistence on continuing to bankroll Ukraine drew a sharp response in Germany, where AfD co-leader Alice Weidel contrasted his appetite for further funding with skyrocketing costs at home. “Diesel €2.25 [per liter], drinks 30 cents more ex","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:08:51 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647286-zelensky-begging-bowl-eu-summit/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:34
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,ICC serves Europe’s ‘colonialist interests’ – analyst (VIDEO),ICC serves Europe’s ‘colonialist interests’ – analyst (VIDEO),"ICC serves Europe’s ‘colonialist interests’ – analyst (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad1f5f22030275c28705db6.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> ICC targets Global South nations while ignoring crimes in Ukraine to serve Western interests, legal analyst Alexandre Guerreiro says <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647281-icc-europe-colonialist-interests/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The International Criminal Court (ICC) has become a tool of Western influence that selectively targets countries of the Global South while shielding European interests and ignoring crimes in Ukraine, international legal analyst and academic Alexandre Guerreiro has said. He accused the tribunal of applying double standards rather than delivering universal justice. Criticism of the ICC has intensified in recent months amid growing accusations of political bias and selective justice. Venezuela, Chad, Burkina Faso, Mali and Niger have moved to withdraw, accusing the court of serving Western interests and engaging in“neocolonial repression.” In an interview with RT on Thursday, Guerreiro argued that the court had abandoned its original purpose as an independent institution capable of holding perpetrators accountable regardless of nationality, and has become increasingly politicized and dominated by European powers. “In practice, what we have is a court that serves European interests, colonialist interests,”he said, arguing that the tribunal is used to pressure Global South nations while avoiding similar scrutiny of European countries. Guerreiro pointed to the court’s handling of cases involving Afghanistan, Iraq and Kenya, arguing that political interference had repeatedly undermined the principles of impartial justice. He also accused the ICC of ignoring alleged crimes in Ukraine, including the deadly May 2014 Odessa clashes between Ukrainian nationalists and opponents","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:14:27 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647281-icc-europe-colonialist-interests/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:35
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Israel unlikely to attack Iran before elections – media,Israel unlikely to attack Iran before elections – media,"Israel unlikely to attack Iran before elections – media <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad1a303203027672a40f602.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Israeli officials reportedly see a strike on Iran as unlikely before the October 27 vote, despite claims Netanyahu wants to resume the war <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647268-israeli-unlikely-attack-iran-elections/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> There is a widespread belief within Israel’s political and security establishment that the country will not attack Iran ahead of the October 27 parliamentary elections, Ynet News reported on Thursday. The report comes after Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu told Army Radio on Wednesday that it would be“inconvenient”to launch preemptive strikes against Iran at this time. He claimed, however, that“Iran’s proxies”were planning to fire rockets at Israel. “Even if Iran fires missiles at us, they will blame me,”he said, adding that Israel would retaliate against any attack. Netanyahu sought to dispel speculation following a Channel 12 report claiming that he had urged Washington to strike Iran before the Israeli elections and the US midterms scheduled for November 3. Axios cited a US official earlier this week as saying that Netanyahu“seems to want to go in again”against Iran. Netanyahu’s office denied the claims. US President Donald Trump has repeatedly hinted in recent weeks that he could resume the bombing campaign if Iran does not accept his terms. American media outlets have reported that the Pentagon prepared plans to use a massive conventional explosive nicknamed the“mother of all bombs.”The White House, however, denied that Trump and Netanyahu had discussed resuming the war. Diplomatic efforts to end the conflict have stalled, with Washington and Tehran accusing each other of making unacceptable demands. Iranian officials have warned that the countr","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:08:36 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647268-israeli-unlikely-attack-iran-elections/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:36
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Missiles supplied to Ukraine sold on ‘open market’ – Trump,Missiles supplied to Ukraine sold on ‘open market’ – Trump,"Missiles supplied to Ukraine sold on ‘open market’ – Trump <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad1ec1d85f5405ae3007cd2.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US President Donald Trump has questioned the whereabouts of military aid provided to Ukraine under his predecessor, Joe Biden <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647267-trump-blasts-zelensky-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump has accused Ukraine of selling American-supplied missiles on the black market, questioning the whereabouts of billions of dollars in military and financial aid provided to Kiev under his predecessor, Joe Biden. In an interview with Newsmax aired on Thursday, Trump lashed out at Ukrainian leader Vladimir Zelensky, accusing him of exploiting Washington’s generosity, while refusing to negotiate an end to the conflict with Russia. “Where is the cash that we gave to Ukraine? Where is all the equipment? Biden was giving them missiles, and they were being sold on the open market,”Trump said. Russian officials have repeatedly warned that unchecked deliveries of Western weapons to Ukraine and rampant corruption in the country have resulted in a large amount of these arms ending up in the hands of organized criminal groups and extremist organizations in Europe, Africa, the Middle East, and Latin America, including Mexican drug cartels. An RT investigation in 2022 found a variety of Western-supplied weapons such as anti-tank rockets, drones, and small arms for sale on the“dark web.” According to a report by Small Arms Survey, the Ukrainian authorities intercepted a vehicle carrying 18 US-made Javelin anti-tank missiles and other hardware in Kiev-controlled part of Russia’s Donetsk People’s Republic in 2024. The driver lacked the proper paperwork to transport the weapons, which suggested that they could have been intended for sale, it said. Ukraine has also been","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:09:24 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647267-trump-blasts-zelensky-ukraine/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:37
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Teen gunman kills four at US elementary school,Teen gunman kills four at US elementary school,"Teen gunman kills four at US elementary school <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad15558203027361a643fc9.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> A teenage gunman killed three children and a teacher at an elementary school in Bend, Oregon, before being shot dead by a bystander <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647264-us-active-shooter-alert-school/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> A teenage gunman killed three students and a teacher at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday, police said. The shooter was himself shot dead by a bystander. The culprit was identified as a 16-year-old Bend resident, the city’s police chief, Mike Krantz, said at a news conference. He did not reveal the suspect’s name or say whether he knew anyone at the school. The three children killed were aged five, eight and 11. A seven-year-old child and a 54-year-old teacher were hospitalized in critical condition. Krantz said the gunman was shot by a“community member who had seen the suspect enter the school and pursued him into the school and engaged him.” The school has been placed on lockdown, and the Bend Police Department has urged the public to avoid the area. According to The Source Weekly, parents received alerts that nearby schools, including Caldera High School and Jewell Elementary School, had also been placed on lockdown following a police alert at around 1:20 PM on Thursday. The lockdowns were lifted about 40 minutes later. Video from the scene shows multiple police cars and ambulances near the school. Paramedics seen staging at Silver Rail Elementary School in Bend, Oregon amid reported active shooter situation. https://t.co/9KnGY4LIEv FBI Director Kash Patel said the bureau’s local office was working with investigators.“We will make every resource they need available,”he wrote on X. “Today is an awful day for our community,”Bend Mayor Melanie Kebler ","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:16:54 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647264-us-active-shooter-alert-school/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:37
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Russia could make Olympic return under national flag – Trump envoy,Russia could make Olympic return under national flag – Trump envoy,"Russia could make Olympic return under national flag – Trump envoy <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad12b1685f540449e50b96f.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Russia could make a major Olympic return under its national flag in 2028, US President Donald Trump’s envoy Paolo Zampolli has told TASS <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647262-russia-olympics-national-flag/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Russia could make a major return to the Olympics in 2028 under its national flag for the first time in years, US President Donald Trump’s special envoy, Paolo Zampolli, has said. Russian athletes were barred from numerous international competitions following the escalation of the Ukraine conflict in February 2022. Some were later allowed to compete under neutral status, without their national flag or anthem. Speaking to TASS on Thursday, Zampolli expressed optimism about broader Russian participation in the Los Angeles Games, arguing that sporting bans should not become a permanent substitute for political dialogue. ”I am optimistic about further progress that would establish a reliable mechanism for fuller participation by Russian athletes at the 2028 Los Angeles Olympics,”he said.“The US must host Games that are safe, fair, and open to every eligible athlete.” The International Olympic Committee (IOC) provisionally lifted its suspension of the Russian Olympic Committee in July, paving the way for broader participation at LA 2028. However, it has yet to decide whether Russian athletes will be able to compete under their national flag and anthem. Several international federations, including World Aquatics, World Gymnastics and the International Fencing Federation, have also eased restrictions on Russian competitors. Zampolli called the return of the Russian flag and anthem at the 2026 Winter Paralympics in Italy an“important step,”arguing that excluding top a","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:54:24 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647262-russia-olympics-national-flag/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:38
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump calls off firing squad livestream,Trump calls off firing squad livestream,"Trump calls off firing squad livestream <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad11fce20302735017a7f00.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The execution of Nidal Malik Hasan, who killed 13 US service members, will not be public, US President Donald Trump has said <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647261-trump-calls-off-firing-squad-livestream/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The execution of Nidal Malik Hasan, who killed 13 US service members in a 2009 shooting rampage at Fort Hood, will not be public, US President Donald Trump has announced. Days earlier, Secretary of War Pete Hegseth promised it would be webcast, drawing criticism from lawmakers across party lines. In a post on Truth Social on Thursday, Trump wrote that the former US Army major“will die, as scheduled, by firing squad, but this event will not be streamed.”The US president explained that while webcasting Hasan’s execution“might have been a strong deterrent… many very good and well meaning people would rather not watch him die, through streaming, or through any other visual device.” Trump noted that the relatives of the victims would still have the right to view Hasan’s death in person. According to Axios, citing an anonymous administration official, the US president has grown increasingly skeptical of the idea in recent days, not least because of all the“negative input”he supposedly received. Speaking to reporters late last Friday, Trump said he“wasn’t involved in that decision.” Hegseth told conservative commentator Jack Posobiec last Thursday that Hasan is scheduled to be shot at 1 PM on December 3 – the approximate time of day of the original attack – at the same installation where he carried out the massacre. “We’ll make sure that people are able to watch it, that it’s public, because people need to understand there’s serious consequences for these types of things,” the secre","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:27:45 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647261-trump-calls-off-firing-squad-livestream/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:39
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Netanyahu survived his enemies. Can he survive his own voters?,Netanyahu survived his enemies. Can he survive his own voters?,"Netanyahu survived his enemies. Can he survive his own voters? <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0fbee85f54065b529af40.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Ahead of Israel’s election, Netanyahu loyalists defend his wartime record while former Likud voters seek alternatives on the left and right <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647250-netanyahu-voters-israel-elections/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> As Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu fights to retain power, loyalists are crediting him with strengthening the country and defeating its enemies, while former supporters blame his leadership for October 7 and are seeking alternatives on both the left and the right. With less than a month to go before Israel’s elections, Netanyahu faces an uphill battle to retain power. But polls show it won’t be an easy task.A recent surveyconducted by Maariv, one of Israel’s leading newspapers, estimates that his party, Likud, will only win 20 seats out of 120 total in the Knesset, Israel’s parliament, a drop of 12 compared with its performance in the 2022 elections. The decline in Likud’s ratings is hardly surprising. Netanyahu and his government have been blamed for failing to prevent the October 7, 2023 attacks, in which more than 1,200 Israelis were killed and 251 people were taken to Gaza as hostages. He has also faced criticism for pursuing a series of controversial policies concerning the judiciary and the media; remaining in power amid graft probes that led to charges of bribery, fraud and breach of trust; and contributing to Israel’s growing isolation on the international stage. Surprisingly, however, the Maariv poll shows that around 40 percent of respondents still want Netanyahu to remain Prime Minister of Israel.Loyalists offer a long list of Netanyahu’s achievements. For them he is the man who subdued Israel’s enemies, confronted Iran’s nuclear ambit","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:04:11 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647250-netanyahu-voters-israel-elections/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:40
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Trump could have Zelensky arrested – Galloway,Trump could have Zelensky arrested – Galloway,"Trump could have Zelensky arrested – Galloway <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad10c862030272ada6aefdf.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> US President Donald Trump could have Vladimir Zelensky arrested over corruption in Ukraine, former British MP George Galloway has told RT <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647229-zelensky-us-trump-confrontation/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> US President Donald Trump could have Ukraine’s Vladimir Zelensky arrested on corruption charges, former British MP George Galloway has predicted. Tensions between the two men escalated after Zelensky challenged Trump’s deal with Moscow to ease restrictions on Russian diesel exports. Washington has repeatedly demanded that Kiev stop striking Russian oil refineries, warning that continued attacks could jeopardize US intelligence sharing and Starlink support. Kiev has pressed ahead with the strikes, while Zelensky has accused Trump of“betrayal”and“weakness.” Speaking to RT on Thursday, Galloway, who alsohostsThe Mother of All Talk Shows, suggested that Zelensky’s defiance of Trump could cost him his position. “I’m going to predict to you that Trump will organize the anti-corruption units that he arguably controls in Kiev to march into Zelensky’s office at some point soon and place him under arrest for grand larceny, for corruption on a scale that we have never seen in politics ever before,”he said. “This is a regime in the process of collapse,”Galloway added. He cautioned, however, that a change of leadership would not necessarily end the Ukraine conflict, arguing that Kiev would also have to abandon its NATO ambitions and adopt a policy of neutrality. Galloway also argued that Ukraine had no viable replacement for Starlink and that losing access to the satellite service could severely hamper its military operations. The former lawmaker criticized London’s continued financial su","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:57:26 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647229-zelensky-us-trump-confrontation/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:41
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Western Europe is giving its spies teeth,Western Europe is giving its spies teeth,"Western Europe is giving its spies teeth <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad10145203027313119ab08.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Intelligence agencies are gaining new powers and the freedom to use them, gradually turning the EU into a security state <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647259-europe-gives-spies-teeth/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByLadislav Zemánek, non-resident research fellow at China-CEE Institute and expert of the Valdai Discussion Club ByLadislav Zemánek, non-resident research fellow at China-CEE Institute and expert of the Valdai Discussion Club Something fundamental has changed in Europe over the past months. Governments across the continent have begun expanding the powers of intelligence agencies at a pace that would have been difficult to imagine only a few years ago. Germany is preparing to give its foreign intelligence service a far more operational role. The Netherlands is expanding the ability of its intelligence agencies to act proactively against hostile actors. Austria is broadening its definition of espionage. Sweden is rebuilding its foreign intelligence architecture. Taken together, these amount to a European securitization drive: more activities are being redefined as security problems, more institutions are being brought inside the security apparatus, and intelligence services are being transformed from organizations that primarily collect information into agencies which are increasingly expected to act. Western Europe’s security establishment has been shaken by two developments: the continuing perception of a more assertive and dangerous international environment, and growing political uncertainty surrounding America’s role in European security under President Donald Trump. The psychological shock came in March 2025, when the Trump administration temporarily halted US military an","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:02:37 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647259-europe-gives-spies-teeth/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:41
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Houthis strike presidential compound in Aden (VIDEO),Houthis strike presidential compound in Aden (VIDEO),"Houthis strike presidential compound in Aden (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad103fe20302738f3738312.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Yemen’s Houthis have conducted a missile strike on the presidential compound in Aden used by the Saudi-backed government <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647260-houthis-aden-presidential-compound/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Yemen’s Houthis have conducted a missile strike on the presidential palace in the southern city of Aden, where the internationally recognized, Saudi-backed government is located. The group claimed the strike killed several Saudi officials and mercenaries, while the government acknowledged only two fatalities among security guards. Later in the day, the figure was revised to five dead and at least 16 wounded. The Al-Maashiq presidential palace was hit by at least five missiles on Thursday, with footage circulating online showing black smoke and a large plume of dust emitting from the compound. Yemeni Information Minister Moammar al-Eryani said the country’s prime minister and cabinet members were at the compound during the strike yet escaped the attack unharmed. The militant group, known officially as the Ansar Allah movement, said that the compound served as military operations headquarters run by Saudi officers and was being used as a weapons depot. There were multiple casualties at the site, the Houthis claimed. “The strike on the Saudi enemy’s military operations headquarters in Aden falls within the framework of the previously announced policy: targeting Saudi military concentrations wherever they may be and considering any military presence of the Saudi enemy a legitimate target for our forces, wherever it is located,”the group’s military spokesman, Yahya Saree, has said. Yemen has remained locked in a civil war since 2014, with the situation further aggravated by a Saud","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:04:35 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647260-houthis-aden-presidential-compound/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:42
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Leakers should be shot – Trump,Leakers should be shot – Trump,"Leakers should be shot – Trump <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0f3c085f54062d97f9ca2.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Officials leaking sensitive government information to the media “should be shot,” US President Donald Trump has said <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647254-leakers-should-be-shot-trump/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Government employees sharing confidential information with journalists should face the death penalty, US President Donald Trump has said. Addressing supporters during a midterm rally in Bullhead City, Arizona on Wednesday, Trump cited an occasion when the Pentagon allegedly had to put off an air raid against Iran after the bombers’ departure and arrival times were leaked to the press, including the New York Times and CNN. It was not immediately clear which military operation Trump was referring to, although several media outlets conjectured that he was speaking about last year’s bombing campaign targeting Iran’s underground nuclear facilities. “Somebody leaked – some sleazebag,”Trump said, adding that“they ought to go to jail and be shot.” He argued that“in the old days we used to shoot leakers…[especially]when they leak what time you’re going to attack a country.” “The leakers are the scum of the earth,”Trump concluded. Since the start of the US-Israeli military campaign against Iran in late February, the Republican leader has repeatedly lashed out at government officials leaking information to the press as well as media outlets publishing such materials. “Keep on leaking you dirty dogs! When we find you, you will pay a big price,”Trump wrote in a Truth Social post last month in response to media reports claiming that some of his aides had advised him against attacking Tehran. In August, the US president similarly accused leakers of making“treasonous statements,”saying that ","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:22:53 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647254-leakers-should-be-shot-trump/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:42
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,"American bombs, European pilots: Who does what in NATO’s nuclear club?","American bombs, European pilots: Who does what in NATO’s nuclear club?","American bombs, European pilots: Who does what in NATO’s nuclear club? <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0f34385f540561e1ac0e3.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Steadfast Noon 2026 has brought NATO nuclear drills to Italy, raising questions about Europe’s expanding nuclear role and security <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647253-american-bombs-european-pilots/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> ByDmitry Kornev, military expert, founder and author of the MilitaryRussia project ByDmitry Kornev, military expert, founder and author of the MilitaryRussia project From October 13 to 23, 2026, Italy is hosting NATO’s annual nuclear deterrence exercise Steadfast Noon. The exercise will take place at air bases in Aviano and Ghedi in northern Italy. Flight operations and training involving mock nuclear weapons will take place in designated airspace over the Tyrrhenian Sea and other areas under NATO jurisdiction in Southern and Western Europe. The purpose of these exercises is to prepare NATO aircraft for the potential deployment of US nuclear weapons stationed at European airbases. This year’s exercise boasts a record number of participants – 17 NATO countries, compared to 14 in 2025 and 13 in 2024. While the complete list of participating nations hasn’t been disclosed, it is confirmed that the US, Italy, Germany, the Netherlands, and Türkiye will take part. Romania and Poland will likely provide fighter support and ensure integration along NATO’s eastern flank. New NATO members – Sweden and Finland – are fully engaged in the training missions. Finland may host US nuclear weapons in the future and has already started acquiring F-35 carrier aircraft. Notably, France does not participate in NATO’s nuclear planning group and is not involved in these exercises, likely due to its own air-delivered nuclear capabilities. The exercise involves around 70 military aircra","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:14:35 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647253-american-bombs-european-pilots/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:43
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Eight US states accuse OpenAI of harming children,Eight US states accuse OpenAI of harming children,"Eight US states accuse OpenAI of harming children <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0f4662030272e31554f9b.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Eight US states have accused ChatGPT of encouraging children to harm themselves as the FTC subpoenas OpenAI and Anthropic <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647257-us-ai-harms-children-lawsuits/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> Eight US states have sued OpenAI, accusing its ChatGPT chatbot of encouraging self-harm and violence, including among children, and misleading the public about its safety. The states allege that ChatGPT is designed to be excessively agreeable and engaging, gaining users’ trust while reinforcing delusions, encouraging dangerous behavior, and even helping plan mass shootings. “OpenAI claims ChatGPT is safe while it’s giving dangerous medical advice, encouraging people to hurt others, and coaching people to commit suicide – all while pretending to be their fake friend,”Iowa Attorney General Brenna Bird said. Iowa, Kansas, Nebraska, West Virginia, Arkansas, Arizona, Idaho, and Montana filed separate lawsuits in state courts on Wednesday. The complaints accuse the company of violating consumer protection laws and creating a public nuisance. The states seek financial penalties, damages, and changes to ChatGPT. They also want OpenAI barred from developing self-improving AI models unless it can demonstrate that those systems are aligned with human values. OpenAI spokesman Drew Pusateri defended the company’s age-specific protections, parental controls, and break reminders, saying that“while no system can be perfect, we’ll continue to work with experts to inform our work and build additional safeguards.” Separately, the Federal Trade Commission (FTC) sent civil subpoenas to OpenAI and Anthropic on Wednesday seeking documents about safety incidents and possible consumer protection viol","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:03:42 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647257-us-ai-harms-children-lawsuits/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:44
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Albania’s Education Ministry torched as violent unrest grips country (VIDEOS),Albania’s Education Ministry torched as violent unrest grips country (VIDEOS),"Albania’s Education Ministry torched as violent unrest grips country (VIDEOS) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0f2a785f540640f3fabb8.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Albania is enduring a third consecutive day of student-led protests, with widespread rioting and a heavy-handed police response <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647255-albania-student-protests-violent/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The Ministry of Education building has been set ablaze in Tirana. The Albanian capital is reeling from a third consecutive day of student-led mass protests. The protests which began in the country this week were reportedly sparked by the ongoing unrest in France and were initially aimed at rising education costs, the poor condition of educational facilities, and widespread corruption. The unrest promptly grew political and violent, and the protesters are now demanding the departure of socialist Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama as well as the leader of the country’s democratic opposition, Sali Berisha. The two have dominated Albania’s political landscape for about four decades, and both have repeatedly faced allegations of corruption. The unrest comes on top of months of anti-government protests in Albania, which have mainly revolved around a major luxury tourism development project linked to US President Donald Trump’s son-in-law, Jared Kushner. The movement, which has become known as the ‘Flamingo Revolution,’ has been condemned by the prime minister as part of a“hybrid war”waged by the“enemies of Israel and Albania.” On Wednesday, a large crowd of protesters breached the premises of the Education Ministry, setting the building on fire. Footage from the scene shows the fence of the compound damaged, with a large group of protesters watching black smoke billowing out of the windows. Violent protests continue in Tirana, while the Ministry of Education bui","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:39:39 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647255-albania-student-protests-violent/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:44
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US proposes unfreezing Russian assets for Ukraine peace – FT,US proposes unfreezing Russian assets for Ukraine peace – FT,"US proposes unfreezing Russian assets for Ukraine peace – FT <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0e3a12030272233172752.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The US has proposed unfreezing Russian assets for Ukraine peace talks, but the EU has rejected the initiative, the FT reports <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647252-us-proposes-unfreezing-russian-assets/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The US has proposed unfreezing billions of euros in Russian assets held in the EU to give impetus to Ukraine peace talks, the Financial Times reported on Wednesday, citing sources. Moscow has long described the freezing of its assets as“theft”while warning of significant retaliation if the funds are seized. The proposal was raised last week during negotiations in Miami involving President Donald Trump’s envoy Steve Witkoff, his son-in-law Jared Kushner, and officials from Ukraine, France, Germany, Britain, the EU, and NATO, four people familiar with the matter told the paper. Washington reportedly floated several mechanisms for releasing the frozen funds as part of a comprehensive peace deal, including transferring some of them into a special-purpose vehicle overseen by the US. However, the exact arrangements have not been finalized, with numerous ideas about how the funds could be used being discussed, the FT said. During the talks, Washington asked Kiev to present proposals for spending potential reconstruction funds and to work with the World Bank on tackling rampant corruption and introducing financial accountability measures, a US official told the paper. Kiev’s European backers, however, rejected the American initiative, refusing to surrender control over the assets, with the move requiring the unanimous approval of all 27 EU members, according to the newspaper. The proposal also reportedly“startled”European delegations and Kiev, with some wondering about Washin","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:34:21 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647252-us-proposes-unfreezing-russian-assets/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:45
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,Deadly floods devastate Istanbul (VIDEO),Deadly floods devastate Istanbul (VIDEO),"Deadly floods devastate Istanbul (VIDEO) <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0b98085f540421b77b4ae.png"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> Record rainfall has triggered deadly floods across Istanbul, killing at least three people and forcing thousands to evacuate <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647242-istanbul-deadly-floods/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> At least three people have been killed as torrential rains unleashed devastating floods across Istanbul, submerging streets, sweeping away vehicles and bringing much of Türkiye’s largest city to a standstill. The storm battered the city overnight on Wednesday, flooding residential neighborhoods, businesses, and major roads on both the European and Asian sides. Schools were closed, public transport was disrupted, and authorities urged residents to remain indoors as further rainfall was forecast. The downpour, described by local officials as the worst in decades, has triggered a massive emergency response, with thousands evacuated and dozens of flights diverted. Reporting from the flooded streets of Istanbul on Thursday, RT correspondent Yasin Ekin said the scale of destruction was still being assessed, with emergency crews working to rescue stranded residents and clear debris. İstanbul Sarıyer Ayazağa mahallesi korkunç görüntüler.. #yağmur https://t.co/zeCuRDGX4Q Istanbul Governor Davut Gul described the rainfall as the heaviest in 84 years, according to Ekin, with some areas receiving up to 270 millimeters of precipitation. The correspondent illustrated the extraordinary volume of water, explaining that such rainfall would amount to roughly 27 metric tons of water falling on an area of 100 square meters. The flooding also reportedly forced a tanker carrying liquefied natural gas (LNG) aground near the Sariyer district along the Bosphorus Strait. The death toll rose to three o","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:23:15 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647242-istanbul-deadly-floods/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:46
RT (EN),Russia (English),en,US could drop ‘mother of all bombs’ on Iran – CNN,US could drop ‘mother of all bombs’ on Iran – CNN,"US could drop ‘mother of all bombs’ on Iran – CNN <img align=""left"" alt=""Preview"" src=""https://mf.b37mrtl.ru/files/2026.10/thumbnail/6ad0af7a85f54040a05ae776.jpg"" style=""margin-right: 10px;"" /> The Pentagon is developing plans to use a GBU-43/B MOAB against Iran, CNN has reported, citing US officials <br /><a href=""https://rt-english.com/news/647237-trump-moab-iran-cnn/?utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=RSS"">Read Full Article at RT.com</a> The Pentagon is developing plans to use the largest conventional bomb in the US arsenal in its war on Iran, CNN has reported, citing multiple sources in US President Donald Trump’s administration. If approved, the strike would mark only the second combat use of the GBU-43/B Massive Ordnance Air Blast bomb, or MOAB, following its deployment in Afghanistan in 2017 during Trump’s first term. According to CNN, such an operation would primarily serve as“psychological warfare”against Iranian forces while potentially boosting domestic support for the Trump administration. Sources suggested the weapon, nicknamed the“mother of all bombs,”could be dropped ahead of the US midterm elections in early November. The MOAB is a massive 9,800 kg (21,600-pound) airburst munition designed to devastate a large area and intimidate enemy forces witnessing the explosion. While capable of destroying relatively unfortified targets, it is not a penetrating“bunker-buster”designed to destroy deeply buried installations, such as those used by Iran for critical military infrastructure. The“bunker-buster”GBU-57 Massive Ordnance Penetrator weighs approximately 14,000 kg (30,000 pounds). However, the MOAB carries at least four times as much explosive material. “The MOAB is a massive information operation type weapon that is great for huge area clearance but not much else,”one of CNN’s sources said. “POTUS has unfortunately put himself in a situation where he is almost compelled to do something,”the official a","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:44:17 +0000",https://rt-english.com/news/647237-trump-moab-iran-cnn/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=RSS,2026-10-18 01:48:46
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Trump vows ‘very good decision’ on anti-Russian sanctions,Trump vows ‘very good decision’ on anti-Russian sanctions,"Trump vows ‘very good decision’ on anti-Russian sanctions According to the US president, the decision will benefit the entire world WASHINGTON, October 18. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump has stated that he intends to make a ""very good decision"" regarding anti-Russian sanctions, one that will benefit the entire world. ""A lot of you don't know what my decision is yet, but we'll figure it out, and you'll figure it out. It's a very good decision, and it's going to be a decision that's good for the country, and I think good for the world because we're really at a world stage,"" Trump told reporters at his Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida, according to the White House press pool. Earlier on Saturday, U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio stated that Trump set a 60-day window to evaluate the potential consequences of imposing sanctions on Russia, as well as the associated tariffs on other nations, including the impact on both the U.S. and global economies. According to Rubio, this additional analysis is prompted by the current volatility in global energy markets. Previously, Trump signed an executive order suspending the application of the anti-Russian measures stipulated by the new law, pending further instructions from the president or the secretary of state. On September 18, Trump signed a bill passed by Congress that mandates tougher sanctions against Russia’s top political and military leadership, as well as state-owned enterprises. The legislation includes provisions for a 500% increase in tariffs on imports from Russia, and a 100% increase on imports from countries that are major purchasers of Russian energy.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:08:33 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203635,2026-10-18 01:48:48
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Trump takes 60 days to assess impact of potential sanctions against Russia — Rubio,Trump takes 60 days to assess impact of potential sanctions against Russia — Rubio,"Trump takes 60 days to assess impact of potential sanctions against Russia — Rubio The US secretary of state noted that the additional analysis is prompted by tensions in global energy markets WASHINGTON, October 18. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump intends to use a 60-day window to evaluate how potential sanctions against Russia and related tariffs on other nations could affect the US and global economies, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio told reporters. ""The problem is these sanctions were not just sanctions on Russia. They include tariffs on a number of countries, India, for example, and others. And so, I think the president wants to take the 60-day period of time to sort of analyze what imposing both sanctions and tariffs will mean to the global economy and even to the U.S. economy,"" Rubio said. The secretary of state noted that the additional analysis is prompted by tensions in global energy markets. He highlighted that energy supplies are facing pressures from the situation involving Iran and the Strait of Hormuz, Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia, and strikes on energy infrastructure during the Russia-Ukraine conflict, all of which drive global energy prices. Rubio also pointed to India, which, he said, is ""voluntarily diversifying their energy portfolio"" but still imports ""substantial amount of energy from Russia because it is hard to pivot everything from one day to the next."" ""But they [India] are also an important ally and partner of the United States,"" he remarked, emphasizing that Washington must weigh these factors to find the optimal mix of sanctions and tariffs.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:46:35 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203633,2026-10-18 01:48:48
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Russia's Battlegroup Center destroys Ukrainian unit of about 2,000 troops in Dobropolye","Russia's Battlegroup Center destroys Ukrainian unit of about 2,000 troops in Dobropolye","Russia's Battlegroup Center destroys Ukrainian unit of about 2,000 troops in Dobropolye According to the reconnaissance chief of the 110th Brigade of the battlegroup, the initial Ukrainian force in the city did not exceed 1,300 troops DONETSK, October 18. /TASS/. A Ukrainian military unit numbering around 2,000 troops has been destroyed in Dobropolye after the entire force became trapped in the city, TASS reported on Sunday, citing the reconnaissance chief of the 110th Brigade of Russia's Battlegroup Center, who goes by the call sign ""Udav"" (Boa). ""The unit consisted of about 2,000 personnel. As of now, it has been completely destroyed,"" the reconnaissance chief said. According to the serviceman, the initial Ukrainian force in Dobropolye did not exceed 1,300 troops. The Ukrainian command later reinforced the unit, only to effectively abandon them after they were encircled.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:35:40 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2203631,2026-10-18 01:48:49
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukraine currently lacks access to Starshield military communications system — Rubio,Ukraine currently lacks access to Starshield military communications system — Rubio,"Ukraine currently lacks access to Starshield military communications system — Rubio According to the US secretary of state, the matter is ""under conversation"" WASHINGTON, October 18. /TASS/. Ukraine does not currently have access to the Starshield satellite communications system, and the matter is under discussion, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said on Saturday. ""Starlink is a commercial product and it's regulated and handled as a commercial product. Starshield is a defense product, a military product, and as I said, I mean that that is something that we have and the United States military uses. It's not at this moment available to Ukraine, and that's under conversation. It's under discussion right now of how they would want to use it,"" he told reporters before flying to Uzbekistan. According to the secretary of state, Ukraine ""asked for access to it in order to conduct deep strikes inside Russia."" ""They do not have access to it at this moment,"" he emphasized.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:27:35 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203629,2026-10-18 01:48:50
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia sees Europe’s need for Russian fuel — deputy premier,Russia sees Europe’s need for Russian fuel — deputy premier,"Russia sees Europe’s need for Russian fuel — deputy premier Alexander Novak cited calls in Germany to resume purchases of Russian gas as an example MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Russia sees continued interest in Russian fuel from European consumers, including amid calls in Germany to resume purchases of Russian gas, Russian Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak said in an interview to Marina Kim on the Soloviev Live television. ""Recently, we have seen more and more politicians and countries saying that it was a mistake to stop purchases of Russian gas or Russian oil, or petroleum products,"" he said. ""The countries that still benefit from exemptions are calling for these exemptions to be extended. In other words, we see interest in Russian energy resources.""","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:56:39 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2203589,2026-10-18 01:48:51
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Air defense forces destroy 11 UAVs heading toward Moscow — city mayor,Air defense forces destroy 11 UAVs heading toward Moscow — city mayor,"Air defense forces destroy 11 UAVs heading toward Moscow — city mayor Sergey Sobyanin reported that emergency services personnel are working at the site where the debris fell MOSCOW, October 18. /TASS/. Air defense systems have destroyed 11 unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) that were heading toward Moscow, Mayor Sergey Sobyanin announced. ""The Defense Ministry’s air defense system has destroyed eleven UAVs that were heading toward Moscow. Emergency services personnel are working at the site where the debris fell,"" he wrote on his Telegram channel.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:43:35 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2203623,2026-10-18 01:48:52
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Bell tower of Limoges town hall collapses after arson during riots,Bell tower of Limoges town hall collapses after arson during riots,"Bell tower of Limoges town hall collapses after arson during riots Firefighting operations are still underway PARIS, October 18. /TASS/. A bell tower has collapsed onto the roof of the town hall in Limoges, central France, after a fire broke out during riots, according to footage broadcast by the France 3 television channel. The fire started after several groups of radicals broke into the building and set fire to rooms on the ground floor. They then torched several vehicles parked nearby, which later exploded. Despite firefighters battling the blaze for an hour, the fire spread to the roof. An hour later, the flames engulfed the bell tower. Footage shows the burning structure toppling sideways and crashing through the central section of the roof. Firefighting operations are still underway. ""There are no words to condemn what happened - it is so vile. This is chaos for the country,"" Limoges Mayor Guillaume Guerin said. He claimed the rioters ""came to kill,"" adding that this was ""visible on security camera footage."" The mayor pledged to file a formal complaint and ensure that all those responsible for destroying the historic building are punished. The Limoges town hall, built in 1883 by architect Charles Alfred Leclerc, is a protected historic landmark.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:26:11 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2203621,2026-10-18 01:48:53
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"World Bank recognizes Russia’s achievements, provides platform for cooperation — Deputy PM","World Bank recognizes Russia’s achievements, provides platform for cooperation — Deputy PM","World Bank recognizes Russia’s achievements, provides platform for cooperation — Deputy PM Alexey Overchuk noted that Russia ""possesses vast experience and knowledge and has much to offer countries of the Global South"" BANGKOK, October 18. /TASS/. The World Bank recognizes Russia’s digital achievements and provides a platform to share this expertise with developing economies, Russian Deputy Prime Minister Alexey Overchuk told TASS, following the autumn meetings of the IMF and World Bank. Overchuk noted that ""Russia possesses vast experience and knowledge and has much to offer countries of the Global South,"" particularly regarding ""digital transformation in public administration."" ""The World Bank acknowledges Russia’s achievements in this area, understands how vital Russian expertise is for developing economies, and provides us with an international platform to work directly with these nations,"" he emphasized. On the sidelines of the meetings in Bangkok, Russia organized two packed working seminars with World Bank support. ""One seminar focused on digital transformation in land and real estate administration and geospatial data systems. The other addressed digital public services and digital transformation in tax administration,"" Overchuk said. He noted that these areas crucially impact the business climate, investment attractiveness, and socio-economic development in the Global South. ""The World Bank prioritizes these issues, and Russia is a global leader in digital governance,"" Overchuk said, adding that Russia ranks eighth in the World Bank’s GovTech Maturity Index. ""By learning from our experience, developing nations are seeking closer cooperation with Russia, which aligns with our intere","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:40:44 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2203619,2026-10-18 01:48:53
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Ukrainian forces shell DPR settlements 13 times over past day,Ukrainian forces shell DPR settlements 13 times over past day,"Ukrainian forces shell DPR settlements 13 times over past day No civilian casualties were reported DONETSK, October 18. /TASS/. Ukrainian forces have attacked the territory of the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) 13 times over the past 24 hours, the department for documenting Ukraine’s war crimes at the DPR head’s office and government reported on Friday. ""Thirteen armed attacks by Ukrainian formations have been recorded. No civilian casualties were reported today,"" the statement says. Meanwhile it became known that two civilians had been injured in Konstantinovka and Donetsk on October 12 and 15, respectively. The shelling damaged three residential buildings, two civilian infrastructure facilities, a truck, and several cars. In total, Ukrainian troops fired 15 rounds of various ammunition into the DPR, the office added.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:25:46 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2203617,2026-10-18 01:48:54
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Over 500,000 people took to streets across France on October 17 — trade union","Over 500,000 people took to streets across France on October 17 — trade union","Over 500,000 people took to streets across France on October 17 — trade union The authorities have not yet published any official numbers PARIS, October 17. /TASS/. CGT, one of France’s largest trade unions, said that more than 500,000 people took to the streets across the country to protest against price growth and declining purchasing power. ""Over 500,000 people took part,"" BFMTV quoted the trade union as saying in a statement. The figure was later officially confirmed by French Interior Minister Laurent Nunez. He said 100 rallies were held all across the country, with 550,000 people participating, including 110,000 in Paris. In turn, student organization L'Union Etudiante estimates the number of participants at 800,000. In all, 1,700 rallies and marches were held all across France, the organization said. The authorities have not yet published any official numbers. French President Emmanuel Macron condemned the unrest and pledged to bring those responsible to justice. ""There is no place for violence in our republic. Those who took part in looting, attacked prefectures and shops, ransacked public facilities, including our mayor’s offices, will be prosecuted and punished,"" he wrote on the X social network. The president also expressed his support to police forces. A series of mass protests against rising fuel prices and the declining purchasing power of the population has been taking place all over France on October 17. In a number of cities, the protests have escalated into riots and clashes with police. By 1:00 p.m. GMT, some 400 people have been detained all over France, including over 160 in the capital. Ac","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:06:04 +0300",https://tass.com/society/2203615,2026-10-18 01:48:55
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Yemeni government forces report killing 800 Houthis in past day,Yemeni government forces report killing 800 Houthis in past day,"Yemeni government forces report killing 800 Houthis in past day Spokesman Majid al-Nuzaili added that on the eastern front, government forces continued to clear enemy positions, establishing control over new tactical areas DOHA, October 17. /TASS/. Armed forces of the internationally recognized Yemeni government have neutralized over 800 members of the country’s rebel Ansar Allah (Houthi) movement over the past 24 hours, delivering over 1,400 strikes on their positions, Yemeni Armed Forces Spokesman Majid al-Nuzaili said. ""Over the past 24 hours, 1,417 precision and direct strikes were conducted using combat aircraft, drones, field artillery, and multiple launch rocket systems,"" he said in a statement. In his words, ""approximately 800 [enemy] elements were neutralized, including killed and wounded, and more than 190 pieces of armored vehicles were destroyed or disabled"" as a result of the ongoing Operation Dawn of Yemen. Al-Nuzaili said the strikes targeted Houthi manpower clusters, their fortified positions, firing points and drone launch sites. The spokesman added that on the eastern front, government forces continued to clear enemy positions, establishing control over new tactical areas. Besides, in the Taiz Governorate in the country’s southwest, troops repelled continuous waves of Houthi attacks, while the Air Force delivered strikes on enemy positions and reinforcements, thus inflicting significant losses in terms of personnel and equipment. The armed confrontation between the Houthis and government forces has been going on since August 2014. In September of that year, the Ansar Allah movement established control over the country’s capital Sana’a, and advanced southward. In March 2015, at","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:52:29 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203613,2026-10-18 01:48:56
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Number of Ebola cases in Kenya rises to seven — agency,Number of Ebola cases in Kenya rises to seven — agency,"Number of Ebola cases in Kenya rises to seven — agency According to the Health Ministry, cited by Reuters, one person has died NAIROBI, October 17. /TASS/. The number of confirmed Ebola cases in Kenya has risen to seven, including one fatality,Reutersreported, citing the country’s Health Ministry. Four new cases have been detected over the past 24 hours. Three of the patients are medical workers who provided medical aid to the country’s first Ebola patient. Another infected was his relative. All four were under quarantine when the symptoms manifested. Two patients previously diagnosed with Ebola are in stable condition. The ministry said the first patient contacted with 130 people, and 128 of them have been identified and placed in quarantine. So far, there have been no signs that the infection has begun to spread beyond the identified transmission patterns. No restrictions on travel, trade and mass gatherings have been introduced. The first Ebola case was detected in Kenya on October 5, in a citizen who arrived from the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) via Uganda. The man died. The Ebola outbreak in DRC continues, with no vaccine against it approved to date.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:34:37 +0300",https://tass.com/society/2203609,2026-10-18 01:48:57
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,School students clash with police in Brussels,School students clash with police in Brussels,"School students clash with police in Brussels The unrest began after police blocked a column of several hundred school and university students because their march was not authorized BRUSSELS, October 17. /TASS/. A new wave of student protests, accompanied by sporadic clashes with police, swept through Brussels on Saturday, a TASS correspondent reported. The unrest began after police blocked a column of several hundred school and university students because their march was not authorized. Protestors refused to disperse and started throwing firecrackers and bottles at police, as well as launching fireworks in their direction. Police immediately responded with water cannons and tear gas. Following the arrival of police reinforcements, the column scattered into small groups that moved in all directions, leaving behind overturned trash bins, broken bicycles and smashed scooters.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:23:42 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2203607,2026-10-18 01:48:57
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Oil prices may grow even further if Hormuz issue not settled — Russian deputy premier,Oil prices may grow even further if Hormuz issue not settled — Russian deputy premier,"Oil prices may grow even further if Hormuz issue not settled — Russian deputy premier Alexander Novak pointed out that the capacity to use oil stockpiles to stabilize the global market was nearly exhausted MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Global oil prices may grow even further if attempts to stabilize the situation in the Strait of Hormuz are unsuccessful, Russian Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak said in an interview to Marina Kim on the Soloviev Live television. He recalled that the closure of the strait dealt a serious blow to the global energy and oil market. Earlier, this waterway accounted for approximately 18-20 million barrels per day, or 20% of the total global oil production and consumption. ""We see that the global oil market is currently facing a shortfall of around 4-6 billion barrels per day. That is why the price has risen; it is reacting to the deficit. Volatility is high,"" he said. ""While the market expects things to stabilize there, prices remain high nonetheless."" ""However, if this situation persists, in my view, it will drive prices up even further, because stockpiles are currently being drawn from various reserves,"" the Russian deputy premier added. In his words, the capacity to use oil stockpiles to stabilize the global market has nearly been exhausted. ""Based on our assessments and those of experts, in fact, the potential to draw from reserves is effectively running out,"" the official said.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:14:31 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2203605,2026-10-18 01:48:58
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Houthis report downing Saudi Arabia’s Apache helicopter,Houthis report downing Saudi Arabia’s Apache helicopter,"Houthis report downing Saudi Arabia’s Apache helicopter Military Spokesman Yahya Saree said that the aircraft ""engaged in hostile actions targeting our forces on the border"" DOHA, October 17. /TASS/. Members of Yemen’s rebel Ansar Allah (Houthi) movement downed an Apache helicopter of Saudi Arabia’s air force, Houthi Military Spokesman Yahya Saree was quoted as saying by theSABAnews agency. ""The [Houthi] armed forces managed to take down an Apache helicopter of the Saudi enemy,"" he said. The spokesman added that the aircraft was downed when it ""engaged in hostile actions targeting our forces on the border.""","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:09:29 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203603,2026-10-18 01:48:59
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Europe has difficulties with supplying more air defense systems to Riyadh — newspaper,Europe has difficulties with supplying more air defense systems to Riyadh — newspaper,"Europe has difficulties with supplying more air defense systems to Riyadh — newspaper Military analysts told The National that the UK and France have no opportunity to transfer these systems without harming their own defense potential in the Baltic countries DOHA, October 17. /TASS/. Saudi Arabia’s European allies are experiencing difficulties with supplying additional air defense systems to Saudi Arabia because they need them for their own defense purposes,The Nationalnewspaper wrote, citing military analysts. Riyadh insists on additional deliveries of military equipment to repel attacks by Yemen’s radical Ansar Allah (Houthi) movement. However, according to the newspaper’s defense sources, the United Kingdom and France have no opportunity to transfer these systems without harming their own defense potential in the Baltic countries. Besides, London has been delivering weapons to Ukraine in significant amounts, including Storm Shadow cruise missiles. ""We have very little left in the locker to give,"" the newspaper quoted a UK defense source as saying. ""We really have nothing to send over to them."" According to The National, many Western countries have depleted their arsenals because of their commitments to Eastern European countries and Kiev. ""They [Saudi Arabia] need it because they are a big country,"" Lynette Nusbacher, a former military intelligence officer, was quoted as saying. ""They've got a lot of big targets that are easily spottable on Google Earth and they're up against people who have got sufficient ballistic missiles."" In her words, Saudi Arabia is in the urgent need of aid from the United Kingdom, France, Italy and the United States. Britain already has a battery of Sky Sabre air defence systems at King Fahd Air Base,","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:04:06 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203601,2026-10-18 01:49:00
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,German chancellor points to major political division in Germany,German chancellor points to major political division in Germany,"German chancellor points to major political division in Germany Friedrich Merz also urged the Christian Democratic Union (CDU) to redefine its purpose BERLIN, October 17. /TASS/. German Chancellor Friedrich Merz admitted a profound political division in the country and urged the Christian Democratic Union (CDU) to redefine its purpose. ""Let’s be honest with one another: we are going through a severe political polarization, and we are experiencing it internally as well,"" he told an annual conference of the CDU/CSU coalition’s youth conference in Bonn, aired by Phoenix TV. ""Germany needs us in the future as well, but we need to justify our existence anew,"" Merz added. In September, the conservative union suffered disastrous results in state elections in Berlin, Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, and Saxony-Anhalt. In Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, the CDU failed to pass even the 5% threshold to the local parliament. In Berlin, they lost to the Left Party, and in Saxony-Anhalt - to Alternative for Germany (AfD).","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:52:02 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203599,2026-10-18 01:49:01
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Indian experts describe Trump’s waiver of Russian oil tariffs as economic relief for India,Indian experts describe Trump’s waiver of Russian oil tariffs as economic relief for India,"Indian experts describe Trump’s waiver of Russian oil tariffs as economic relief for India Continued access to competitively priced Russian crude oil will allow bringing down raw material costs, easing inflationary pressure and supporting economic growth, Indian experts say NEW DELHI, October 17. /TASS/. US President Donald Trump’s decision to lift tariffs and restrictions in accordance with the Russia and Iran sanctions act, came as an economic relief for India and its exporters, Indian experts say. ""While the waiver of additional duties under the US Russia-related sanctions law provides temporary relief, it is a welcome development for India's energy security,"" the PTI news agency quoted industry chamber FICCI's Secretary General Anant Swarup as saying. In his words, continued access to competitively priced Russian crude oil will allow bringing down raw material costs, easing inflationary pressure and supporting economic growth. ""At the same time, a waiver that can be modified or withdrawn at short notice does not provide the durable predictability that businesses need for long-term planning,"" the expert continued. In his words, FICCI hopes that both India and the United States will ensure that such measures to do not complicate the ongoing trade negotiations, and that bilateral economic partnership is based on stability, transparency, mutual benefit and trust. In turn, Federation of Indian Export Organisations (FIEO) Director General Ajay Sahai said that this step will prevent serious risks for Indian exports and is designed to strengthen buyer confidence and order flows, particularly in employment-intensive sectors such as textiles, leather, gems and jewelry, and machine building. ""It also creates a positive environment for advancing India-U","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:39:23 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2203597,2026-10-18 01:49:01
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Many countries want to buy Russian oil — deputy premier,Many countries want to buy Russian oil — deputy premier,"Many countries want to buy Russian oil — deputy premier The first tanker has already been loaded in the port of Dikson, Russian Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak said MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Russia has no problems selling its oil as many countries are willing to buy, Russian Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak said. ""You know, as far as oil sales are confirmed, and many countries are willing to buy,"" he said. ""I already know that the first tanker has already been loaded in the port of Dikson,"" Novak added.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:20:27 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2203595,2026-10-18 01:49:02
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Top Russian diplomat arrives in Bahrain to participate in Russia-GCC strategic dialogue,Top Russian diplomat arrives in Bahrain to participate in Russia-GCC strategic dialogue,"Top Russian diplomat arrives in Bahrain to participate in Russia-GCC strategic dialogue Bahrain will become the first stop on Sergey Lavrov's Middle East tour MANAMA /Bahrain/, October 17. /TASS/. Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov has arrived in Manama to participate in the ninth strategic dialogue between Russia and the Gulf Cooperation Council, a TASS correspondent reported. Bahrain will become the first stop on the top Russian diplomat’s Middle East tour. Later, Lavrov is expected to travel to Tehran for consultations with Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi. Russian Foreign Ministry’s Spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said Lavrov is expected to hold a number of bilateral meetings on the sidelines of the Russia-GCC dialogue. The previous GCC meeting in this format at the level of foreign ministers was held in Russia’s Black Sea resort city of Sochi in September 2025. The GCC comprises Bahrain, Qatar, Kuwait, the UAE, Oman and Saudi Arabia.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:11:22 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2203593,2026-10-18 01:49:02
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia to deliver 39 billion cubic meters of gas to China via Power of Siberia,Russia to deliver 39 billion cubic meters of gas to China via Power of Siberia,"Russia to deliver 39 billion cubic meters of gas to China via Power of Siberia There is also an agreement to expand deliveries to 44 billion cubic meters of gas, Russian Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak said MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. This year, Russia will deliver 39 billion cubic meters of gas via the Power of Siberia pipeline, exceeding the volume stipulated by the main contract, Russian Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Novak said. ""First of all, I’d like to say that our first project, Power of Siberia, has been implemented very successfully. Its capacity is 38 billion cubic meters of gas, but we expect to deliver 39 billion cubic meters this year, which is even more than under the main contract,"" he said in an interview to Marina Kim on the Soloviev Live television. ""There is also an agreement to expand deliveries to 44 billion cubic meters of gas,"" Novak added.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:09:42 +0300",https://tass.com/economy/2203583,2026-10-18 01:49:03
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Pakistani military uses heavy weaponry in response to Afghan attack,Pakistani military uses heavy weaponry in response to Afghan attack,"Pakistani military uses heavy weaponry in response to Afghan attack The report says a number of fortifications were destroyed on the Afghan side ISLAMABAD, October 17. /TASS/. The armed forces of Pakistan used heavy weaponry in response to fire from the Afghan side of the border, the Islamic republic’s state-run RTV television reported. ""The armed forces of Pakistan gave an efficient response with the use of heavy weaponry, responding to an unprovoked fire that Afghan Taliban members opened in the Kurram sector,"" the television wrote on the X social network. The report says a number of fortifications were destroyed on the Afghan side. Afghanistan’s TOLO News television channel reported earlier in the day, citing a security source, that armed clashes had broken out on the border between Afghanistan and Pakistan with at least seven Pakistani servicemen killed and six wounded.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:30:01 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203579,2026-10-18 01:49:04
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,At least 400 people detained across France during unrest on October 17,At least 400 people detained across France during unrest on October 17,"At least 400 people detained across France during unrest on October 17 Most of the detainees were grown-ups and pledged to hold responsible those involved in looting, violence and vandalism PARIS, October 17. /TASS/. France’s law enforcement agencies detained at least 400 people while dispersing rallies organized as part of nationwide protests against price growth, French Interior Minister Laurent Nunez told reporters. ""By now, 400 people have been detained, but these are only preliminary figures,"" he said. He added that most of the detainees were grown-ups and pledged to hold responsible those involved in looting, violence and vandalism.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:15:00 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203577,2026-10-18 01:49:04
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Nuclear reactor in northeast Japan stopped after radiation water leak,Nuclear reactor in northeast Japan stopped after radiation water leak,"Nuclear reactor in northeast Japan stopped after radiation water leak The power unit will be shut down for ten days to inspect and replace the malfunctioning components TOKYO, October 17. /TASS/. Unit two of Japan’s Onagawa nuclear power plant in the northeastern Japanese Miyagi prefecture has been shut down following a leak of technical water containing an insignificant amount of radioactive substances, the NPP’s owner Tohoku Electric Power said. The company notified that the leak originates from a faulty valve. Its workers are collecting the radioactive wastewater, and no containment breach beyond the facility’s perimeter has been detected. The incident poses no threat to the environment, the company added. The power unit will be shut down for ten days to inspect and replace the malfunctioning components. Technical water is currently leaking at a rate of approximately 0.2 metric tons per hour. The Onagawa NPP previously suspended its operations in May, following a minor release of radioactive steam. The facility was shut down following the 2011 Fukushima NPP accident, but was put back on stream in 2024. The accident at the Fukushima-1 nuclear power plant prompted the government to shut down all the 54 nuclear power stations in the country, which dealt a huge blow to the energy supply. Until the spring of 2011, the nuclear reactors generated a third of the electricity the island consumes. Currently, the country is partially restarting nuclear power plants in compliance with new enhanced safety measures. Currently, there are 14 reactors in operation, and their number is gradually increasing. The government of the new Prime Minister Sanae Tak","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:13:01 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203571,2026-10-18 01:49:05
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Police use tear gas against protestors in Italy’s Milan — newspaper,Police use tear gas against protestors in Italy’s Milan — newspaper,"Police use tear gas against protestors in Italy’s Milan — newspaper The protest involved over 5,000 participants, mostly young people ROME, October 17. /TASS/. Italian police used tear gas against protestors in Milan, who gathered in protest of expensive petroleum and the war economy, the Corriere della Sera newspaper wrote. According to the report, tear gas was used when protestors started hurling stones and bottles at police officers. Some reports indicated that shop windows were smashed and property was vandalized in the area. The protest involved over 5,000 participants, mostly young people. Meanwhile, an anti-government protest was held in the capital Rome. The event was organized by the Italian General Confederation of Labor (CGIL). The union’s leader Maurizio Landini accused the government of investing exclusively in armaments, while keeping wages law amid the rising cost of living. He announced that a general strike will take place on November 20. Another general strike in Italy has already been scheduled for October 30, coinciding with a major international action by European port workers protesting the war economy and weapons shipments.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:10:01 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203575,2026-10-18 01:49:06
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Power outages reported in 23 LPR municipalities after Ukrainian attack — head,Power outages reported in 23 LPR municipalities after Ukrainian attack — head,"Power outages reported in 23 LPR municipalities after Ukrainian attack — head Social infrastructure sites have been connected to alternative power sources LUGANSK, October 17. /TASS/. The armed forces of Ukraine attacked power infrastructure in the Lugansk People’s Republic (LPR), triggering emergency power outages in 23 municipalities, LPR head Leonid Pasechnik said. ""Members of Ukrainian armed groups attacked the republic’s energy infrastructure. As a result, power outages were reported in 23 municipalities, including the region’s administrative center,"" he wrote on the Max messenger. In his words, social infrastructure sites have been connected to alternative power sources. ""At this point, the probability of another attack remains high. Power grid workers will organize repair works as soon as the opportunity arises. Some consumers will be switched to backup power lines,"" the official added. ""Social and medical facilities have been promptly connected to backup power sources,"" he added.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0300",https://tass.com/emergencies/2203573,2026-10-18 01:49:06
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,At least 30 Ukrainian drones downed over Russian regions in daytime,At least 30 Ukrainian drones downed over Russian regions in daytime,"At least 30 Ukrainian drones downed over Russian regions in daytime Оn-duty air defenses destroyed Ukrainian fixed-wing unmanned aerial vehicles over the regions of Belgorod, Bryansk, Vologda, Kursk, Oryol and Krasnodar, as well as over Black Sea waters MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Russian air defenses took down 30 Ukrainian drones over various Russian regions in daytime on Saturday, the Russian Defense Ministry said. ""In daytime, between 8:00 a.m. and 8:00 p.m. Moscow time (5:00 a.m. and 5:00 p.m. GMT), on-duty air defenses destroyed 30 Ukrainian fixed-wing unmanned aerial vehicles over the regions of Belgorod, Bryansk, Vologda, Kursk, Oryol and Krasnodar, as well as over Black Sea waters,"" the ministry said.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2203569,2026-10-18 01:49:07
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Clashes break out on Afghan-Pakistani border, casualties reported — TV","Clashes break out on Afghan-Pakistani border, casualties reported — TV","Clashes break out on Afghan-Pakistani border, casualties reported — TV Two towers and a CCTV camera were destroyed during the incident ISLAMABAD, October 17. /TASS/. Armed clashes broke out on the border between Afghanistan and Pakistan with at least seven Pakistani servicemen killed and six wounded, the TOLO News television channel reported citing a security source. The report says servicemen of the two countries clashed in the Dand-Patan district of Afghanistan’s Paktia province near the Durand Line, the border between the two states, which Kabul does not recognize. Two towers and a CCTV camera were destroyed during the incident. Shootouts in the area continue, but their intensity has already subsided, the source said.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:15:00 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203567,2026-10-18 01:49:07
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Albanian police use rubber bullets against protestors in Tirana — CNA,Albanian police use rubber bullets against protestors in Tirana — CNA,"Albanian police use rubber bullets against protestors in Tirana — CNA Protests in the city have entered their fifth consecutive day as demonstrators are trying to seize government buildings BELGRADE, October 17. /TASS/. Albanian police are using rubber bullets and other riot control equipment to disperse anti-government protests in Tirana city center, the CNA news portal said. Protests in the Albanian capital have entered their fifth consecutive day as demonstrators are trying to seize government buildings. Police use water cannons to quell the unrest. The unrest in Tirana broke out on October 13, during a student protest outside the Ministry of Education. Protests continued on the following day, and escalated when protestors, demanding the resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama, attempted to break through to his residence. When police dispersed the crowd, rioters broke into groups and began attacking government buildings in downtown Tirana, including the parliament, the Justice Ministry, the State Archives, and other agencies. Sali Berisha, the leader of Albania’s leading opposition force, the Democratic Party of Albania, has declared his support for the ongoing protests.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:57:38 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203565,2026-10-18 01:49:08
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,French police disperse unauthorized rally near Elysee Palace,French police disperse unauthorized rally near Elysee Palace,"French police disperse unauthorized rally near Elysee Palace Marching crowds were stopped around 200 meters from the building PARIS, October 17. /TASS/. French police dispersed an unauthorized rally near the French president’s official residence, Elysee Palace, where crowds gathered despite a ban from the authorities, the LCI television reported. Marching crowds were stopped around 200 meters from the building. The number of participants is unknown. A small group of protestors is now gathering near the Avenue des Champs-Elysees. A TASS correspondent reported that tear gas was used to disperse the crowd of around a hundred people, who carried banners that criticized the police and the government. A grenade with tear gas was hurled at them after they partially blocked traffic not far from the Elysee Palace. Earlier, the Franceinfo radio station reported citing the authorities that the Paris City Hall has prohibited public demonstrations in a number of areas in the French capital on Saturday, including streets adjacent to the presidential residence. Violators are facing a fine of 135 euro. However, numerous unauthorized rallies have been taking place in various locations in Paris since morning. A series of mass protests against rising fuel prices and the declining purchasing power of the population has been taking place all over France on October 17. In a number of cities, the protests have escalated into riots and clashes with police. By 1:00 p.m. GMT, a total of 272 people have been detained all over France, including over 160 in the capital. In a separate incident, a group of aggressive protestors b","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:33:10 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203563,2026-10-18 01:49:08
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Sounds of explosions heard in southern Iran, near Strait of Hormuz — Fars","Sounds of explosions heard in southern Iran, near Strait of Hormuz — Fars","Sounds of explosions heard in southern Iran, near Strait of Hormuz — Fars The report says locals informed of explosions in the Kuhestak coastal area and in several districts of Sirik TUNIS, October 17. /TASS/. Sounds of explosions were heard near the city of Sirik in the southern Iranian province of Hormozgan, the Fars news agency reported. The report says locals informed of explosions in the Kuhestak coastal area and in several districts of Sirik. Sirik is located on the Gulf of Oman coast, east of the Strait of Hormuz. The cause of the explosions, as well as potential damage or casualties, has not been reported at this point.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:02:38 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203559,2026-10-18 01:49:09
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,UKMTO reports attack on LNG ship off Yemen,UKMTO reports attack on LNG ship off Yemen,"UKMTO reports attack on LNG ship off Yemen The name of the ship and its port of registry were not specified LONDON, October 17. /TASS/. A tanker transporting liquefied natural gas (LNG) was attacked off the Yemeni coast, the United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO) center under the Royal Navy said. ""UKMTO has received a report of an incident 140NM southwest of Al Mukalla, Yemen,"" the organization said in a statement. ""A Master of an LNG Tanker has reported being approached by a small skiff with seven persons onboard. The skiff fired two shots at the tanker whose armed Security Team fired two warning shots at the small skiff which forced them to alter course."" The name of the ship and its port of registry were not specified.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:01:10 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203557,2026-10-18 01:49:10
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russia views idea of shortcut to ‘nuclear zero’ as counterproductive — diplomat Postnikov,Russia views idea of shortcut to ‘nuclear zero’ as counterproductive — diplomat Postnikov,"Russia views idea of shortcut to ‘nuclear zero’ as counterproductive — diplomat Postnikov Director of the Department for Non-Proliferation and Arms Control of the Russian Foreign Ministry underlined that real progress on this path may be achieved only through carefully balanced, step-by-step measures MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Russia believes that ideas of a shortcut to a ""nuclear zero,"" which implies an immediate abandonment of nuclear weapons and declaring them illegal, are counterproductive, Director of the Department for Non-Proliferation and Arms Control of the Russian Foreign Ministry Oleg Postnikov said. ""Russia remains committed to the ideals of nuclear disarmament in the comprehensive manner, as envisaged by provisions of the NPT [Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty]. It unconditionally remains our key legal benchmark and foundation for implementing efforts in this domain,"" he said in his October 16 address to the First Committee of the 81st UN General Assembly, published by the Russian foreign ministry. ""Real progress on this path may be achieved only through carefully balanced, step-by-step measures that do not jeopardize anyone’s security and help reinforce global stability,"" the Russian diplomat continued. ""Ideas of a shortcut to ‘nuclear zero,’ which imply an immediate and unconditional abandonment of nuclear weapons along with arbitrarily outlawing them, we view as unrealistic and counterproductive."" ""Attempts to artificially establish disarmament deadlines, especially in the current turbulent and unpredictable international situation, are equally unfeasible. We are firmly convinced that disarmament initiatives should correspond to the military, political and strategic context,"" Postnikov added. In his words, a serious obstacle to further reductions of nuclea","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:00:22 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2203555,2026-10-18 01:49:10
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,"Russian presidential envoy describes situation around Ukraine as ""checkmate""","Russian presidential envoy describes situation around Ukraine as ""checkmate""","Russian presidential envoy describes situation around Ukraine as ""checkmate"" Kirill Dmitriev gave a comment on a post where independent UK political observer David Vance suggested that US President Donald Trump will no longer ""allow Zelensky to play war games at a huge cost to the globe"" MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. The situation around Ukraine can be described as ""checkmate,"" said Kirill Dmitriev, special representative of the Russian president for investment and economic cooperation with foreign countries, head of the Russian Direct Investment Fund. He wrote ""checkmate,"" commenting on a post where independent UK political observer David Vance suggested that US President Donald Trump will no longer ""allow Zelensky to play war games at a huge cost to the globe."" Earlier, Vance wrote that Brussels and Kiev are growing increasingly worried by Trump’s approach to the Ukrainian conflict, adding that the situation seems to be moving towards peace.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:10:36 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2203539,2026-10-18 01:49:11
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Pope Leo XIV prepares to be discharged from hosptial after lung surgery — doctors,Pope Leo XIV prepares to be discharged from hosptial after lung surgery — doctors,"Pope Leo XIV prepares to be discharged from hosptial after lung surgery — doctors The Pope underwent blood tests and a chest X-ray in the morning, which confirm that his clinical condition allows for him to leave hospital VATICAN, October 17. /TASS/. Pope Leo XIV, who recently underwent a lung surgery, is now ready to be discharged from hospital, his doctors said. ""Dr. Luigi Carbone and Professor Stefano Margaritora said the Pope underwent blood tests and a chest X-ray in the morning, which confirm that his clinical condition allows for him to leave hospital,"" the statement says. On Tuesday, the 71-year-old Pontiff, elected about 18 months ago, underwent surgery to remove the lower lobe of his right lung. An intraoperative histological examination confirmed the diagnosis of lung adenocarcinoma (cancerous tumor), as suspected from the preoperative examinations. His further treatment was not specified, but it is presumed that surgery will be enough. On Friday, the Pontiff had a phone conversation with Russian President Vladimir Putin.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:52:49 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203537,2026-10-18 01:49:12
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Sanctions are Biden’s ineffective idea — Russian presidential envoy,Sanctions are Biden’s ineffective idea — Russian presidential envoy,"Sanctions are Biden’s ineffective idea — Russian presidential envoy Most countries have not joined sanctions against Russia and understand they harm the world economy and prosperity, special representative of the Russian president for investment and economic cooperation with foreign countries, head of the Russian Direct Investment Fund Kirill Dmitriev said MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Anti-Russian sanctions are an ineffective idea of former US President Joe Biden, said Kirill Dmitriev, special representative of the Russian president for investment and economic cooperation with foreign countries, head of the Russian Direct Investment Fund. ""Most countries have not joined sanctions against Russia and understand they harm the world economy and prosperity,"" he wrote on the X social network. ""Sanctions are ineffective Biden-think."" The post came as a response to a post by Mario Nawfal, who said that most countries in the world have not joined Western sanctions against Russia, because they realize how harmful they are for the global economy and prosperity.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:34:03 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2203535,2026-10-18 01:49:13
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Liberation of Dobropolye brings closer full liberation of Donbass — DPR head,Liberation of Dobropolye brings closer full liberation of Donbass — DPR head,"Liberation of Dobropolye brings closer full liberation of Donbass — DPR head This settlement of Dobropolye is actually one of the already outermost localities at the border of the Donetsk People’s Republic towards the Dnepropetrovsk Region, Denis Pushilin said DONETSK, October 17. /TASS/. Dobropolye is one of the outermost cities in the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) at the border with the Dnepropetrovsk Region and its liberation brings closer the full liberation of the Donbass region from Ukrainian troops, DPR Head Denis Pushilin told TASS. ""This settlement of Dobropolye is actually one of the already outermost localities at the border of the Donetsk People’s Republic towards the Dnepropetrovsk Region. <…> This [the liberation of Dobropolye] has brought us significantly closer to one of the main goals - the full liberation of Donbass,"" the DPR head said. On October 16, Chief of the General Staff of the Russian Armed Forces Valery Gerasimov reported to President Vladimir Putin that Russia’s Battlegroup Center had liberated Dobropolye in the Donetsk People’s Republic. Dobropolye was one of the last few major defensive areas of the Ukrainian army in the Donetsk region.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:37:59 +0300",https://tass.com/politics/2203533,2026-10-18 01:49:13
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Zelensky reports one of most massive strikes on country’s energy system,Zelensky reports one of most massive strikes on country’s energy system,"Zelensky reports one of most massive strikes on country’s energy system Over 15 major power generation and transmission facilities were attacked in various regions of Ukraine, Vladimir Zelensky said MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. The Ukrainian energy sector was confronted by one of the most massive strikes on its facilities on October 16 when over 15 major electric power generation and transmission sites were attacked, Vladimir Zelensky said on his Telegram channel. ""Over 15 major power generation and transmission facilities were attacked in various regions of Ukraine. <…> The most difficult situation has emerged in Lutsk, Rovno, Zhitomir, Vinnitsa, Shepetovka, Slavuta and Neteshin. The strikes were also delivered on energy sites in the Kharkov, Kiev, Dnepropetrovsk and other regions,"" he said. On October 16, Chief of the General Staff of the Russian Armed Forces Valery Gerasimov reported to President Vladimir Putin that Russian troops had begun delivering massive strikes on Ukrainian energy facilities.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:35:12 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203529,2026-10-18 01:49:14
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Record number of vessels attacked in Strait of Hormuz since early October,Record number of vessels attacked in Strait of Hormuz since early October,"Record number of vessels attacked in Strait of Hormuz since early October From October 1 to October 13, 22 vessels reported attacks MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Twenty-two vessels were attacked in the Strait of Hormuz in the first 13 days of October, as follows from TASS calculations. This figure has already exceeded the total number of incidents for the whole of March 2026 that previously held the record, the estimates show. From October 1 to October 13, 22 vessels reported attacks. As a result of all these incidents, 15 sailors sustained wounds, two went missing and one vessel sank, as follows from the data of the International Maritime Organization obtained by TASS. The largest number of vessels reported attacks on October 11. During that day, six vessels reported damage. On October 4 and 13, three damage reports were issued on each day. The United States and Israel launched a war against Iran on February 28. In June, Washington and Tehran signed a memorandum of understanding providing for an immediate cessation of hostilities on all fronts, including in Lebanon. However, overnight on July 8, the United States resumed large-scale strikes against Iran, accusing Tehran of violating the agreements regarding the Strait of Hormuz.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:31:12 +0300",https://tass.com/world/2203527,2026-10-18 01:49:14
TASS (EN),Russia (Wire),en,Russian forces strike Ukrainian army’s transport infrastructure in past day,Russian forces strike Ukrainian army’s transport infrastructure in past day,"Russian forces strike Ukrainian army’s transport infrastructure in past day Russia’s Black Sea Fleet destroyed a Ukrainian naval drone in Black Sea waters over the past 24 hours MOSCOW, October 17. /TASS/. Russian forces struck transport infrastructure facilities used by the Ukrainian army, UAV (unmanned aerial vehicle) assembly sites and enemy deployment areas over the past 24 hours, Russia’s Defense Ministry reported. ""Operational/tactical aircraft, attack unmanned aerial vehicles, missile troops and artillery of the Russian groups of forces struck transport infrastructure facilities used by the Ukrainian army, sites storing unmanned aerial vehicles, and also temporary deployment areas of Ukrainian armed formations and foreign mercenaries, in 142 locations"" the ministry said in a statement. Russia’s Black Sea Fleet destroyed a Ukrainian naval drone in Black Sea waters over the past 24 hours, the ministry reported. ""The Black Sea Fleet’s forces destroyed an uncrewed boat of the Ukrainian Navy in Black Sea waters,"" the ministry said. Russian forces are revealing and destroying scattered Ukrainian army groups in the Kharkov Region after destroying surrounded enemy formations in that area, Russia’s Defense Ministry reported. ""Battlegroup North units have completed the destruction of the surrounded enemy in the northeastern part of the Kharkov Region and are carrying out measures to reveal and eliminate scattered single Ukrainian army groups,"" the ministry said in a statement.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:12:51 +0300",https://tass.com/defense/2203521,2026-10-18 01:49:15
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese foreign minister meets with his Turkish counterpart,Chinese foreign minister meets with his Turkish counterpart,"Chinese foreign minister meets with his Turkish counterpart Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan on Thursday in Baku, the capital of Azerbaijan, on the sidelines of the Seventh Summit of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi (R) shakes hands with Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan in Baku, capital of Azerbaijan, October 15, 2026. /Chinese Foreign Ministry Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan on Thursday in Baku, capital of Azerbaijan, on the sidelines of the Seventh Summit of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia. Wang, also a member of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee, said China and Türkiye enjoy a traditional friendship, and deepening strategic cooperation between Beijing and Ankara serves the interests of both countries and their peoples and will also contribute to global economic recovery. China has always attached great importance to its relations with Türkiye and stands ready to work with Ankara to take the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries as an opportunity to implement the important consensus reached by the two heads of state and advance China-Türkiye strategic cooperation to a new level, Wang said. Wang said China appreciates Türkiye's repeated emphasis on attaching importance to China's security concerns and its efforts in curbing terrorist acts that endanger China's national ","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:25:38 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Chinese-foreign-minister-meets-with-his-Turkish-counterpart-1RibshSqDrG/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:16
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Medical supplies help Tigray hospitals in Ethiopia resume services: UN,Medical supplies help Tigray hospitals in Ethiopia resume services: UN,"Medical supplies help Tigray hospitals in Ethiopia resume services: UN Hospitals in Ethiopia’s Tigray region are gradually resuming services as medical supplies and equipment arrive following recent hostilities, the United Nations said Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Hospitals in Ethiopia's Tigray region are gradually resuming services as medical supplies and equipment arrive following recent hostilities, the United Nations said Thursday. The UN Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) said medical services were being restored at several facilities, including Ayder Hospital in the regional capital, Mekelle. A general view of a partially deserted main road in Mekelle, Tigray region, Ethiopia, September 23, 2026. /VCG The UN and its partners are also delivering food, nutrition and other essential supplies to Tigray, Afar and Amhara regions, although humanitarian needs remain significant. OCHA warned that insecurity in parts of Amhara, northern Afar and Tigray continues to threaten civilians and critical infrastructure, while hampering aid deliveries. Humanitarian agencies are assessing the impact of the violence and the needs of affected communities. The UN called for the protection of civilians and civilian infrastructure, urging all parties to ensure safe, rapid and unhindered access for humanitarian assistance.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:26:33 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Medical-supplies-help-Tigray-hospitals-in-Ethiopia-resume-services-UN-1RhSpbVNWOk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:16
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Cuba slams US pressure on UN vote against embargo,Cuba slams US pressure on UN vote against embargo,"Cuba slams US pressure on UN vote against embargo Cuba slams US pressure on UN vote against embargo Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Cuba on Wednesday denounced the United States for pressuring countries to reject a resolution on lifting the trade embargo against Cuba ahead of a United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) vote scheduled for the end of October. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is ""nervous and anxious about yet another defeat at the United Nations,"" and is ""pressuring and blackmailing heads of state and government from various countries"" to change their vote, Cuban Foreign Minister Bruno Rodriguez said in a post on social media platform X. ""Through his repeated lies and new actions, he is trying to keep quiet the act of collective punishment he is inflicting upon the Cuban people,"" Rodriguez said. According to the US State Department, Rubio spoke by phone on Tuesday with Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele, urging him to join the United States and its like-minded partners ""in advancing shared priorities at the United Nations."" The UNGA has voted in favor of the resolution some 30 times. It calls for an end to the economic, trade and financial blockade Washington has imposed on Cuba for over six decades. The resolution is non-binding. In 2025, the resolution received 165 votes in favor and seven against, with 12 abstentions.","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:18:16 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/Cuba-slams-US-pressure-on-UN-vote-against-embargo-1RfK2JP3iRG/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:17
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Mexican healthcare workers protest for better wages, conditions","Mexican healthcare workers protest for better wages, conditions","Mexican healthcare workers protest for better wages, conditions Mexican healthcare workers protest for better wages, conditions Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied Hundreds of Mexican healthcare workers marched through the capital, demanding higher wages, more staff, supplies and better working conditions. Demonstrators for the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) called for the resignation of union leader Rafael Olivos Hernandez, accusing him of failing workers' interests. The protests took place ahead of a crucial vote for a proposed 6.8% pay increase. Here's what protesters had to say. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:46:23 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/Mexican-healthcare-workers-protest-for-better-wages-conditions-1RfziGFwmYg/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:17
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,New China-DPRK border bridge over Yalu River opens to traffic,New China-DPRK border bridge over Yalu River opens to traffic,"New China-DPRK border bridge over Yalu River opens to traffic The new China-DPRK Yalu River bridge officially opened to traffic on Thursday, with both sides jointly holding an opening ceremony on this cross-border artery. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A view of the New Yalu River Bridge connecting China and the DPRK in Dandong, Liaoning Province, northeast China. /VCG The new China-DPRK Yalu River bridge officially opened to traffic on Thursday, with both sides jointly holding an opening ceremony for the cross-border artery. The cable-stayed bridge over the Yalu River serves as a cross-border transport link between the city of Dandong in northeast China's Liaoning Province and the city of Sinuiju in North Pyongan Province in the Democratic People's Republic of Korea. The double-pylon and double-cable-plane bridge features a 28.5-meter-wide deck designed with four lanes for two-way traffic, while its navigational clearance can accommodate vessels of up to the 3,000-tonne class. The new bridge will further facilitate trade and people-to-people exchanges between the two countries, Chinese foreign ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said on Wednesday. An opening ceremony is held for a new bridge across the Yalu River, the border river of China and the Democratic People's Republic of Korea, October 15, 2026. /Xinhua China and the DPRK are friendly neighbors connected by mountains and rivers, and the new bridge is an important facility for connectivity between the two countries, Mao noted at the press briefing. Dandong boa","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:31:16 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/Opening-ceremony-held-for-new-China-DPRK-border-bridge-over-Yalu-River-1RfSEPz7kuk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:17
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,African economies remain resilient despite Iran conflict shocks: IMF,African economies remain resilient despite Iran conflict shocks: IMF,"African economies remain resilient despite Iran conflict shocks: IMF African economies have remained resilient amid the energy crisis triggered by the Iran conflict, but declining foreign aid leaves the continent vulnerable to future shocks, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) said Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied African economies have weathered the energy crisis linked to the Iran conflict, but falling foreign aid could weaken their ability to withstand future economic shocks, the International Monetary Fund (IMF) said Thursday. The fund forecasts Africa's economy will grow by 4.5% this year and 5% in 2027. However, development assistance to the continent is expected to fall by 12% this year, following a sharp decline in 2025. Zeine Zeidane, head of the IMF's Africa department, warned that further energy disruptions, global financial uncertainty, extreme weather and ongoing conflicts could worsen economic pressures and threaten food security. FILE: A meeting of the World Bank Development Committee during the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and World Bank Spring meetings at the IMF headquarters in Washington, DC, US, on Thursday, April 16, 2026. /VCG Despite the risks, rising demand for critical minerals and economic reforms present opportunities for growth. African finance ministers at IMF and World Bank meetings in Bangkok emphasized the need to create jobs, diversify economies and expand local processing of natural resources. Guinea is counting on its Simandou iron ore project and a railway linking the mines to the coast to stimulate economic transformation. Meanwhile,","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:49:05 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/African-economies-remain-resilient-despite-Iran-conflict-shocks-IMF-1RhTuarGYwM/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:17
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Croatian president meets Chinese FM, pledges to strengthen cooperation","Croatian president meets Chinese FM, pledges to strengthen cooperation","Croatian president meets Chinese FM, pledges to strengthen cooperation Croatian President Zoran Milanovic met with visiting Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi in Zagreb on Friday, expressing Croatia's willingness to strengthen exchanges at all levels and advance mutually beneficial cooperation with China. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Croatian President Zoran Milanovic meets with visiting Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi, also a member of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee, in Zagreb, Croatia, October 16, 2026. /Xinhua Croatian President Zoran Milanovic met with visiting Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi in Zagreb on Friday, expressing Croatia's willingness to strengthen exchanges at all levels and advance mutually beneficial cooperation with China. During their meeting, Milanovic asked Wang, also a member of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee, to convey his sincere greetings to Chinese President Xi Jinping. China has undergone tremendous changes over the past few decades and made remarkable achievements in economic and social development, Milanovic said. China's peaceful development poses no threat to any country and should be viewed objectively and rationally by all parties. Each country has its own system and principles, and all countries should respect each other's development paths and ways of life and strengthen mutual understanding and trust through dialogue and communication, Milanovic said. Stressing that Croatia and China enjoy longstanding friendly relations and have achieved significant outcomes in cooperation acr","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:18:04 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/Croatian-president-meets-Chinese-FM-pledges-to-strengthen-cooperation-1Rj1dxTpLC8/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:18
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China calls for efforts to stop influx of illicit weapons into Haiti,China calls for efforts to stop influx of illicit weapons into Haiti,"China calls for efforts to stop influx of illicit weapons into Haiti A Chinese envoy to the United Nations on Wednesday called for efforts to stop the influx of illicit weapons into Haiti, after the Security Council adopted a resolution on renewing the sanctions regime against the country for one year. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A man sits in a shelter for families displaced by gang violence in Port-au-Prince, Haiti, August 12, 2026. /VCG A Chinese envoy to the United Nations on Wednesday called for efforts to stop the influx of illicit weapons into Haiti, after the Security Council adopted a resolution on renewing the sanctions regime against the country for one year. The situation in Haiti remains grave. Haitian gangs continue to obtain large quantities of weapons and ammunition from abroad, posing a serious threat to the security of both the Haitian people and international forces, said Sun Lei, China's deputy permanent representative to the UN. The sanctions regime itself cannot automatically improve the security situation in Haiti and UN member states must take concrete actions to ensure that the sanctions measures are effectively implemented, he said. ""We urge (UN) member states, especially the main source country of illicit weapons and ammunition entering Haiti, to take urgent and decisive measures to combat arms trafficking at its source."" Meanwhile, overcoming Haiti's predicament depends on the country's own political will and concrete efforts. All political parties and factions in Haiti must demonstrate a sense of responsibility, strengthen unity, and effectively advance a politi","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:22:57 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/China-calls-for-efforts-to-stop-influx-of-illicit-weapons-into-Haiti-1RfLmzBMzNC/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:18
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,IMF warns of rising global debt,IMF warns of rising global debt,"IMF warns of rising global debt IMF warns of rising global debt Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Walter Morris Copied International Monetary Fund (IMF) Managing Director Kristalina Georgieva is calling on the world’s largest economies to address growing fiscal and trade imbalances. Speaking at the IMF and World Bank annual meetings in Bangkok, Thailand, on Wednesday, Oct. 14, Georgieva warned of the need for urgent policy reforms as a new IMF report highlights the risks of delaying action on mounting debt. CGTN's Walter Morris reports. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:33:58 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/IMF-warns-of-rising-global-debt-1Rfz7TbrHgY/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:18
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Investment promotion: A bridge for China-Pakistan economic cooperation,Investment promotion: A bridge for China-Pakistan economic cooperation,"Investment promotion: A bridge for China-Pakistan economic cooperation Investment promotion: A bridge for China-Pakistan economic cooperation Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied On Thursday, more than 400 Chinese and Pakistani participants gathered in Shanghai for an investment conference focused on Sindh, Pakistan's most populous province. The event aimed to attract further Chinese investment to the province, with cooperation opportunities spanning key sectors including digital technology, artificial intelligence, manufacturing and electric vehicles, as well as the next phase of the China-Pakistan Economic Corridor.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:52:26 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Investment-promotion-A-bridge-for-China-Pakistan-economic-cooperation-1RhIzOW06fC/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:18
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China urges EU cooperation to promote trade ties,China urges EU cooperation to promote trade ties,"China urges EU cooperation to promote trade ties China hopes the EU will work with it on balanced, sustainable trade and keep global supply chains running smoothly, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said on Friday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A file photo of Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning. /VCG China hopes the European Union (EU) will jointly promote balanced growth and sustainable development in bilateral trade and maintain the stable and smooth operation of global industrial and supply chains, Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said on Friday. Mao made the remarks at a regular press briefing when asked to comment on the latest developments in China-EU trade ties. The second meeting of the China-EU trade and investment consultation mechanism has made positive progress recently, which shows that the two sides can properly handle differences through dialogue, Mao said. China hopes the EU side will honor its commitment to free trade and openness, abide by WTO rules and avoid introducing protectionist and discriminatory policies and measures, she said.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:17:48 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/China-urges-EU-cooperation-to-promote-trade-ties-1RiaU9PF7GM/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:19
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese military says will deter sabotaging moves in South China Sea,Chinese military says will deter sabotaging moves in South China Sea,"Chinese military says will deter sabotaging moves in South China Sea Chinese military says will deter sabotaging moves in South China Sea Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied China has reaffirmed its sovereignty over Huangyan Dao and Nansha Qundao, rejecting the Philippines' claims of safeguarding its rights in the region. The response follows recent incidents involving the Philippines and its military's claim that more than 100 Chinese vessels were present in nearby waters. Chinese Defense Ministry spokesperson Chen Xi said on Friday that the islands and reefs lie outside Philippine territory.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:26:23 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Chinese-military-says-will-deter-sabotaging-moves-in-South-China-Sea-1Ri2YqUXYI0/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:19
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Japanese PM sends ritual offering to war-linked Yasukuni Shrine,Japanese PM sends ritual offering to war-linked Yasukuni Shrine,"Japanese PM sends ritual offering to war-linked Yasukuni Shrine Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi on Saturday sent a ritual offering to the war-linked Yasukuni Shrine as its three-day autumn festival began, local media reported. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied File photo of protesters taking part in a rally on the 80th anniversary of Japan's unconditional surrender in World War II in Tokyo, Japan, August 15, 2025. /Xinhua Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi on Saturday sent a ritual offering to the war-linked Yasukuni Shrine as its three-day autumn festival began, local media reported. Takaichi sent a potted plant offering known as ""masakaki"" to the notorious shrine, a symbol of Japanese militarism and wartime aggression, under her title as prime minister, Kyodo News reported. Takaichi, a conservative politician who regularly visited the controversial shrine before becoming prime minister, is unlikely to visit it during the current festival, the report said, citing a source close to her. While serving as a minister, Takaichi visited the shrine during its spring and autumn festivals and on August 15, the anniversary of Japan's surrender in World War II. However, she has refrained from doing so since becoming prime minister on October 21 last year. According to Kyodo News, Japanese Minister of State for Economic and Fiscal Policy Minoru Kiuchi visited the Yasukuni Shrine on Saturday morning, becoming the first member of Takaichi's cabinet reported to have visited the shrine during the autumn festival. Kiuchi offered ""ma","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:19:47 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/Japanese-prime-minister-sends-offering-to-war-linked-Yasukuni-Shrine-1Rj3kl8NfK8/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:20
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,AI executives say industry can't self-police after early warning shots,AI executives say industry can't self-police after early warning shots,"AI executives say industry can't self-police after early warning shots AI executives say industry can't self-police after early warning shots Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Demis Hassabis, chief executive officer of Google DeepMind, at the International AI Summit in Dublin, Ireland, October 14, 2026. /VCG Two of the biggest names in AI say the systems they built are getting away from them – and that no company should be above the law. Google DeepMind co-founder Demis Hassabis called recent hacking attacks by AI agents ""early warning shots,"" warning that the world could face major incidents in a year or two if systems aren't made more secure. ""I think these (hacking incidents) are early warning shots for us that systems aren't that powerful yet, so the incidents aren't that major,"" Hassabis, also chief scientist at Google parent Alphabet, told an AI summit in Ireland's capital city Dublin on Wednesday. ""But they could be (major) looking into next year and the next couple years if we don't do more work as an industry, as individual companies and governments on securing these systems."" Microsoft President Brad Smith told the conference that rogue AI behavior had made 2026 a ""sobering year"" and that new laws were urgently needed for safety to catch up with innovation. ""No company or technology should be above the law. But we need law, we need regulation. It needs to be sensible, it needs to be balanced, it needs to take into account innov","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:37:38 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-14/AI-executives-say-industry-can-t-self-police-after-early-warning-shots-1ReWMR4DOBq/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:20
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Africa Watch: The US’s new health deal: What’s the catch for Africa?,Africa Watch: The US’s new health deal: What’s the catch for Africa?,"Africa Watch: The US’s new health deal: What’s the catch for Africa? The US is reshaping its global health aid through five-year agreements with African countries, promising funding for programmes tackling HIV, tuberculosis and malaria. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Africa Watch Copied The US is reshaping its global health aid through five-year agreements with African countries, promising funding for programmes tackling HIV, tuberculosis and malaria. However, the deals have raised concerns over access to sensitive health data, pathogen information and biological samples. Can African countries secure vital US health funding without compromising control over their health data and biological resources? On this episode of Africa Watch, Daniel Arapmoi breaks down what Africa stands to gain and what it risks as the US ties health funding to new data-sharing agreements. Credit List: Executive Producers: Sun Lan, Wang Haiyang Planning Editor: Mathias Muindi Reporter: Daniel Arapmoi Digital Producers: Francisca Wanjiru,Tracy Omballa Creative Designer: Bemnet Goitom Video Editor and Graphic Designer: Edwin Ondiek Cameraman: Nyaga Karuri","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:14:41 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-14/Africa-Watch-The-US-s-new-health-deal-What-s-the-catch-for-Africa--1ReAMrzdr0I/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:20
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Chinese FM meets Israeli president,Chinese FM meets Israeli president,"Chinese FM meets Israeli president Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Israeli President Isaac Herzog at the latter's request on the sidelines of the Seventh Summit of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia on Thursday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi, also a member of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee, meets with Israeli President Isaac Herzog on the sidelines of the Seventh Summit of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia (CICA) in Baku, Azerbaijan, October 15, 2026. /Xinhua Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with Israeli President Isaac Herzog at the latter's request on the sidelines of the Seventh Summit of the Conference on Interaction and Confidence Building Measures in Asia in Baku, Azerbaijan, on Thursday. Herzog said the Jewish and Chinese peoples have a long history of exchanges. The two peoples helped each other during the World Anti-Fascist War, forging a friendship that has become a memorable chapter in history. Israel firmly adheres to the one-China policy and is committed to advancing friendly relations with China, he said. Israel is willing to take the 35th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries next year as an opportunity to expand exchanges and cooperation in areas such as science and technology, investment and people-to-people exchanges, he added. Herzog briefed Wang on Israel's views and position on the situation in the Middle East, saying that Is","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:24:13 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/Chinese-FM-meets-Israeli-president-1RibaPyuRHO/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:20
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Aden airport hit; Saudi-led coalition intercepts drones, missiles","Aden airport hit; Saudi-led coalition intercepts drones, missiles","Aden airport hit; Saudi-led coalition intercepts drones, missiles Ballistic missiles launched by the Houthi group struck the international airport in the southern Yemeni port city of Aden on Friday night, Aden's security administration said, while the Saudi-led coalition said earlier it had intercepted fresh drones and missiles over Saudi Arabia and the Red Sea. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A truck loaded with firewood drives through the Al-Basateen neighborhood in Aden, Yemen, October 13, 2026. /VCG Ballistic missiles launched by the Houthi group struck the international airport in the southern Yemeni port city of Aden on Friday night, Aden's security administration said, while the Saudi-led coalition said earlier it had intercepted fresh drones and missiles over Saudi Arabia and the Red Sea. Aden's security administration said in a statement that two missiles landed inside the grounds of Aden International Airport, with preliminary information indicating no casualties. A local security official earlier told Xinhua that two missiles had landed near Aden International Airport, while a third struck a military base near the headquarters of the Saudi-led coalition forces in Al Buraiqa district in western Aden. Three powerful explosions rocked the city, the temporary seat of the internationally recognized Yemeni government, during the attack, a Xinhua reporter on the ground and local residents said. Ambulances were seen heading toward the affected areas. Shortly after the attack, Houthi-run al-Masirah TV cited a military leader within the group as saying the group had targeted ""the headquarters of Saudi forces and weapons depots"" at Badr military camp nea","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:34:21 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/news-1Rj1y9HibcI/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:20
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,President Xi Jinping's key quotes on global governance,President Xi Jinping's key quotes on global governance,"President Xi Jinping's key quotes on global governance President Xi Jinping's key quotes on global governance Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied China will host the 2026 Global Governance Forum (Xiongan) from October 23 to 25 in Xiongan New Area, north China's Hebei Province, the Chinese People's Institute of Foreign Affairs (CPIFA) announced on Friday. President Xi Jinping has on multiple occasions elaborated on China's firm stance on global governance, emphasizing the need to practice true multilateralism, align with the trend toward greater democracy in international relations, and work toward a more just and equitable global governance system. The following are some highlights of his remarks in this regard:","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:37:20 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/President-Xi-Jinping-s-key-quotes-on-global-governance-1Ri53w8SMBW/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:21
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Saudi-led coalition says it destroyed two missile launchers in Yemen,Saudi-led coalition says it destroyed two missile launchers in Yemen,"Saudi-led coalition says it destroyed two missile launchers in Yemen Saudi-led coalition says it destroyed two missile launchers in Yemen Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The Saudi-led coalition said it destroyed two ballistic missile launchers in Yemen's Saada Province, according to a statement early on Saturday. The Houthis have yet to comment.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:50:10 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/news-1Rj2GhcKLQY/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:21
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Foreign ministers of Djibouti, Republic of Congo to visit China","Foreign ministers of Djibouti, Republic of Congo to visit China","Foreign ministers of Djibouti, Republic of Congo to visit China Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Djibouti Abdoulkader Houssein Omar will pay an official visit to China from October 19 to 25, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson announced on Friday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Djibouti Abdoulkader Houssein Omar will pay an official visit to China from October 19 to 25, a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson announced on Friday. Minister of Foreign Affairs, La Francophonie and Congolese Abroad of the Republic of the Congo Constant-Serge Bounda will pay an official visit to China from October 19 to 25, the spokesperson added. According to the spokesperson, the two foreign ministers will visit at the invitation of Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi, who is also a member of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China Central Committee.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:01:55 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Foreign-ministers-of-Djibouti-Republic-of-Congo-to-visit-China-1Ri2FvJGZuE/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:21
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Who's paying for Trump's ballroom? WaPo names the donors,Who's paying for Trump's ballroom? WaPo names the donors,"Who's paying for Trump's ballroom? WaPo names the donors Nvidia and Apple each committed $25 million for US President Donald Trump's planned White House ballroom, according to a Washington Post report on Thursday that showed $333 million in private donations for the project. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Work continues on the construction of the ballroom at the White House, Washington, DC, US, May 19, 2026. /VCG Apple and Nvidia have each handed over $25 million for US President Donald Trump's planned White House ballroom, according to a Washington Post report on Thursday. Two more $25 million cheques came from the Adelson family, longtime backers of Trump and his Republican Party, and from billionaire Charles Ergen, co-founder of Dish Network, the report added. The president's pet project has pulled in $333 million in private donations, while Trump himself is not on the list, according to the Post. The Post reported that the ""vast majority of the funds raised came from companies and wealthy individuals with interests before the federal government"" and that half the total came from firms or executives with federal contracts under Trump's second term. Federal contractors Lockheed Martin, Microsoft and Palantir each gave $10 million, the Post reported. The companies did not immediately respond to a request for comment. Nvidia said it was proud to donate to a nonpartisan trust that serves Americans. ""As an American company, our support for the United States is paramount, and independent of any business interests."" Apple declined to comment. Reuters has not verified th","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:22:26 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Who-s-paying-for-Trump-s-ballroom-WaPo-names-the-donors-1RifOmd64dG/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:21
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,El Niño-linked dry spell disrupts fresh milk supply in Kenya,El Niño-linked dry spell disrupts fresh milk supply in Kenya,"El Niño-linked dry spell disrupts fresh milk supply in Kenya Prolonged dry conditions linked to the El Niño climate pattern have disrupted fresh milk supplies in Kenya, leaving supermarket shelves empty. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Africa Copied Prolonged dry conditions linked to the El Niño climate pattern have disrupted fresh milk supplies in Kenya, leaving supermarket shelves empty and pushing up retail prices as dairy farmers struggle with rising production costs. In the capital, Nairobi, consumers have faced intermittent shortages of fresh milk in recent weeks, with supermarkets struggling to maintain consistent supplies amid growing demand. Milk is a staple in many Kenyan households, and the shortages have forced consumers to search across multiple retail outlets for their preferred brands. A Nairobi resident said finding fresh milk had become increasingly difficult, with some popular brands disappearing from supermarket shelves. Retailers say deliveries often sell out within hours. One supermarket manager reported that fresh milk arriving in the morning is frequently sold out between 9 a.m. and 11 a.m. due to high demand. The shortages have also driven up retail prices, adding pressure on household budgets already strained by the rising cost of living. Dry conditions and rising feed costs hit production According to the Kenya Dairy Board, formal-sector processors collected at least 81 million liters of raw milk in July, representing a 5.8% decline compared with the same period last year. Vict","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:46:58 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/El-Ni-o-linked-dry-spell-disrupts-fresh-milk-supply-in-Kenya-1RifjyYfd28/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:21
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"China slams official US-Taiwan exchanges, EU Parliament's remarks","China slams official US-Taiwan exchanges, EU Parliament's remarks","China slams official US-Taiwan exchanges, EU Parliament's remarks China slams official US-Taiwan exchanges, EU Parliament's remarks Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied China has firmly pushed back against two recent Taiwan-related provocations. A senior Democratic Progressive Party official visited Arizona in the United States to inaugurate a so-called economic and cultural office. Meanwhile, the European Parliament released a report on EU-China political relations that challenged restrictions on Taiwan’s participation in international exchanges and claimed the EU has “never endorsed” the one-China principle. China’s State Council Taiwan Affairs Office spokesperson Chen Binhua has laid out the country’s official position on both.","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:42:33 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-14/China-slams-official-US-Taiwan-exchanges-EU-Parliament-s-remarks-1ReTUuxi5sA/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:21
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,California ports boom despite global tariff uncertainty,California ports boom despite global tariff uncertainty,"California ports boom despite global tariff uncertainty California ports boom despite global tariff uncertainty Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Martin Markovits Copied The Ports of Los Angeles and Long Beach are seeing record cargo volumes ahead of the holiday shopping season despite steep U.S. tariffs on Chinese imports. Following the recent meeting between Chinese President Xi Jinping and U.S. President Donald Trump, proposed tariff reductions on toys and other consumer goods are raising hopes that American businesses and shoppers will see lower prices. CGTN's Martin Markovits reports. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:34:11 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/California-ports-boom-despite-global-tariff-uncertainty-1RfyqQALUaI/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:22
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Wildfire consumes Brazil's Amazon,Wildfire consumes Brazil's Amazon,"Wildfire consumes Brazil's Amazon Wildfire consumes Brazil's Amazon Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied Residents near the Brazilian Amazon are facing a dangerous wildfire threat, along with dangerous and unhealthy smoke. So far in October, the Amazonas state registered 1,558 hotspots, raising alarms for authorities about potential criminal action. For more, check out our exclusive content onCGTN Nowand subscribe to our weekly newsletter,The China Report.","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:31:37 GMT",https://newsus.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/Wildfire-consumes-Brazil-s-Amazon-1RfgMe4dejm/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:22
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Against Nature, Against All Odds | Breaking Through, Episode 4","Against Nature, Against All Odds | Breaking Through, Episode 4","Against Nature, Against All Odds | Breaking Through, Episode 4 Snow-capped mountains, freezing temperatures and endless marshland. Many of the Red Army soldiers had only thin clothes and straw sandals to wear; others had to go barefoot. When their food ran out, they resorted to eating their leather belts and gnawing on bones. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Snow-capped mountains, freezing temperatures and endless marshland. Many of the Red Army soldiers had only thin clothes and straw sandals to wear; others had to go barefoot. When their food ran out, they resorted to eating their leather belts and gnawing on bones. Yet, against all the odds, they kept going. Journalist Vivienne Nunis retraces the historic Long March route through some of China's most unforgiving landscapes, while Mike Walter encounters modern communities finding radical new ways to survive and thrive in the Gobi Desert. Though nearly a century separates these stories from the Long March, the question remains the same: What does it take to keep going when nature itself seems determined to stop you? Tune in to CGTN's Long March documentaryBreaking Throughto find out.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:18:37 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Against-Nature-Against-All-Odds-Breaking-Through-Episode-4-1RhXhhs9Vy8/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:22
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Mekele residents call for peace and recovery after takeover,Mekele residents call for peace and recovery after takeover,"Mekele residents call for peace and recovery after takeover Life is slowly returning to normal in Mekele, days after federal forces retook control of the Ethiopian city. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Life is slowly returning to normal in Mekele, days after federal forces retook control of the Ethiopian city. Shops are reopening and banks have resumed operations, but shortages, rising prices and months of unpaid salaries continue to weigh on residents. Many are struggling to afford basic necessities, while a shortage of cash is making it difficult for pensioners and other customers to access their money. Residents say their priority is not who controls the city, but lasting peace, economic recovery and the restoration of essential services. With the TPLF leadership having left the city, residents hope the latest change in control will bring stability and allow families to rebuild their lives.","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:13:28 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-15/Mekele-residents-call-for-peace-and-recovery-after-takeover-1Rf09rqXwMU/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:22
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Anthropic investors eye lower valuation as growth cools before IPO,Anthropic investors eye lower valuation as growth cools before IPO,"Anthropic investors eye lower valuation as growth cools before IPO Some current Anthropic investors and prospective investors in its upcoming initial public offering are weighing a lower valuation for the AI company after its latest financial disclosures, four people familiar with the matter said, amid broader concerns over the ballooning cost of financing AI. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied An attendee enters the Anthropic headquarters during an investor day in San Francisco, California, US, October 14, 2026. /VCG Some Anthropic investors are weighing a lower valuation for the AI company ahead of its IPO, after its latest financial disclosures, four sources familiar with the matter said. The shift comes amid broader worries about the ballooning cost of financing AI. Investors who attended Anthropic's investor day on Wednesday in San Francisco discussed a valuation of around $1.5 trillion, three of the people said, a significant step down from the roughly $2 trillion previously expected for the November share sale. At the meeting, Anthropic told prospective investors its third-quarter revenue jumped 45% from the previous quarter to $16.8 billion, and that it was profitable on an adjusted basis. Those numbers eased some concerns about the cost of developing AI systems. But some investors were disappointed by the slowing sequential growth rate in the latest quarter, the sources added, as Anthropic's revenue more than doubled from the first quarter to $11.6 billion in the second. They spoke on condition of anonymity because they are not authorized to speak publicly. Anthropic did not immediately respond to requests for comment. A cooler reception for Anth","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:29:09 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Anthropic-investors-eye-lower-valuation-as-growth-cools-before-IPO--1RigTSISjUk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:23
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China urges EU to show sincerity in resolving trade issues,China urges EU to show sincerity in resolving trade issues,"China urges EU to show sincerity in resolving trade issues Both China and the European Union (EU) should show sincerity in solving problems, a spokesperson for China's Ministry of Commerce said on Friday, urging the EU to work with China to promote the healthy and stable development of bilateral economic and trade relations. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Both China and the European Union (EU) should show sincerity in solving problems, a spokesperson for China's Ministry of Commerce said on Friday, urging the EU to work with China to promote the healthy and stable development of bilateral economic and trade relations. The spokesperson made the remarks in response to a question about the EU summit's proposed ""dual-track"" approach toward China, which combines continued intensive consultations with increased restrictions, including the possible use of the bloc's anti-coercion instrument. China-EU economic and trade consultations aim to properly resolve differences through dialogue and consultation while taking each other's concerns into account, the spokesperson said. The understanding reached between China and the EU on hybrid vehicles was based on three principles agreed upon by both sides: compliance with World Trade Organization rules, a fact-based approach and non-discrimination. It was mutually beneficial and reciprocal, safeguarding the practical interests of Chinese enterprises while addressing EU concerns and preventing an escalation of trade frictions, the spokesperson said. The claim that EU pressure had produced results was entirely groundless, the spokesperson said, adding that the EU should not expect to ","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:42:36 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/China-urges-EU-to-show-sincerity-in-resolving-trade-issues-1RijDMApHws/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:23
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,A new railway corridor: How Nanning links Chinese and ASEAN markets,A new railway corridor: How Nanning links Chinese and ASEAN markets,"A new railway corridor: How Nanning links Chinese and ASEAN markets A new railway corridor: How Nanning links Chinese and ASEAN markets Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied From Nanning in south China's Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, goods move by rail across borders, connecting businesses with customers across ASEAN markets. Nanning International Railway Port is a key logistics hub on the New International Land-Sea Trade Corridor, linking southwest China with ASEAN trade routes. Better connections mean new opportunities, stronger local industries and closer regional ties. Follow CGTN reporter Wang Tao as he explores how goods move – and markets come together.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:47:15 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/A-new-railway-corridor-How-Nanning-links-Chinese-and-ASEAN-markets-1Rif5HQq3qo/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:23
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"China mulls export curbs on AI, biomedicine and solar tech","China mulls export curbs on AI, biomedicine and solar tech","China mulls export curbs on AI, biomedicine and solar tech China mulls export curbs on AI, biomedicine and solar tech Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Chinese authorities began public consultation on Friday over a revised export control list, with plans to add AI, biomedicine and photovoltaics technologies. Solar panels installed at a fish hatchery in Maopo Village, Guizhou Province, southwest China, October 12, 2026. /VCG The Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Science and Technology are proposing changes covering 40 technologies across three sectors, according to a notice from the Commerce Ministry. Exporters will also have to register these technologies before shipping them, the ministry said. Public consultation runs from October 16 to November 15, 2026. Details are on the Commerce Ministry's website.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:29:26 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/China-mulls-export-curbs-on-AI-biomedicine-and-solar-tech-1Ri9gvMUqUE/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:23
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,US companies to top CIIE exhibition area for eighth straight year,US companies to top CIIE exhibition area for eighth straight year,"US companies to top CIIE exhibition area for eighth straight year US companies will top the exhibition area at the ninth China International Import Expo (CIIE) for the eighth time, with their area up 1,500 square meters from last year, an official said on Friday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The first batch of exhibits for the ninth China International Import Expo (CIIE) cleared customs and entered China from Shanghai ports on October 12, 2026. /VCG US companies will top the exhibition area at the ninth China International Import Expo (CIIE) for the eighth time, with their area up 1,500 square meters from last year, an official said on Friday. The ninth CIIE will be held in Shanghai from November 5 to 10. Launched in 2018 as the world's first national-level expo dedicated to imports, the CIIE was designed to expand China's opening up and turn its vast market into a shared opportunity for the world. Preparations for the ninth CIIE are basically complete. A total of 162 countries, regions and international organizations will take part, with 4,142 overseas companies exhibiting, China's Vice Minister of Commerce Yan Dong told a press conference. The overall exhibition area will exceed 440,000 square meters for the first time. In the enterprise exhibition, companies from the United States, Germany, Britain and France will lead the pack in terms of exhibition space.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:19:51 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/US-companies-to-top-CIIE-exhibition-area-for-eighth-straight-year-1RilLvAAXwk/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:23
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"Ethiopia PM names interim Tigray government, eyes polls in six months","Ethiopia PM names interim Tigray government, eyes polls in six months","Ethiopia PM names interim Tigray government, eyes polls in six months Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed has appointed an interim administration in the northern Tigray region to restore stability and pave the way for elections within six months. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Africa Copied Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed Ali attends the BRICS Summit in New Delhi, India, September 12, 2026. /VCG Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed has appointed an interim administration in the northern Tigray region to restore stability and pave the way for elections within six months, following renewed fighting between federal forces and a rebel alliance. The move comes after the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) launched an offensive against government forces last month, reigniting a conflict that claimed hundreds of thousands of lives between 2020 and 2022. The latest hostilities have further strained relations between Ethiopia and neighboring Eritrea. Addis Ababa has accused Asmara of supporting the rebels, allegations Eritrea denies. The TPLF, which dominated Ethiopian politics for decades before Abiy took office in 2018, has suffered significant territorial losses. Federal troops have reportedly captured large parts of Tigray, including the regional capital, Mekelle. Interim administration tasked with restoring stability According to Abiy's office, the caretaker administration will serve for six months, focusing on restoring peace, rebuilding institutions and creating conditions for free and transparent elections. The prime minister urged Tigray","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:50:47 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/Ethiopia-PM-names-interim-Tigray-government-eyes-polls-in-six-months-1RitaUJrJCw/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:23
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Tianjin conference calls for global vocational education cooperation,Tianjin conference calls for global vocational education cooperation,"Tianjin conference calls for global vocational education cooperation Tianjin conference calls for global vocational education cooperation Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied Officials and educators from more than 100 countries and regions have gathered in Tianjin, China, for the 2026 World Vocational and Technical Education Development Conference. They are discussing how international cooperation can help vocational education adapt to technological change, better meet industry needs and equip workers with the skills of the future.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:12:34 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Tianjin-conference-calls-for-global-vocational-education-cooperation-1Ri1Cxqaaoo/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:23
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,EU summit ends with mounting bills and unresolved divisions,EU summit ends with mounting bills and unresolved divisions,"EU summit ends with mounting bills and unresolved divisions Behind the EU summit's limited progress lay three pressing challenges: a budget difficult to agree upon, a growing security bill complicated by tensions with Washington, and an energy crisis testing Europe's economic resilience. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Ursula von der Leyen (L), president of the European Commission, and Antonio Costa, president of the European Council, during a news conference at a European Council meeting in Brussels, Belgium, October 16, 2026. /VCG The two-day European Union (EU) summit concluded in Brussels on Friday without a breakthrough on the bloc's long-term budget, as rising security commitments and soaring energy costs exposed a growing gap between Europe's ambitions and its ability to deliver. Behind the summit's limited progress lay three pressing challenges: a budget difficult to agree upon, a growing security bill complicated by tensions with Washington, and an energy crisis testing Europe's economic resilience. Tough budget negotiations The European Commission has proposed a nearly 2-trillion-euro ($2.24 trillion) budget for 2028-2034, seeking to increase investment in competitiveness, defense and technology. The Irish presidency's latest compromise would reduce the Commission's proposal by around 141 billion euros, yet the revised plan has drawn resistance from opposing camps. European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen warned that the compromise would cut budgetary flexibility by half, leaving 99.5% of funds predetermined. ""This proposal puts us in a straitjacket,"" she said","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:47:50 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/EU-summit-ends-with-mounting-bills-and-unresolved-divisions-1Rj3f0YKAxy/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:24
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Israeli settler attacks injure 19 Palestinians in West Bank,Israeli settler attacks injure 19 Palestinians in West Bank,"Israeli settler attacks injure 19 Palestinians in West Bank At least 19 Palestinians, including two children aged eight and 12, were injured in attacks by Israeli settlers across the occupied West Bank on Friday, according to the Palestinian Wall and Settlement Resistance Commission. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied Palestinian volunteers extinguish an olive tree and a Palestinian-owned vehicle set alight, reportedly by Israeli settlers, near the village of Turmus Ayya, north of Ramallah, in the Israeli-occupied West Bank, October 16, 2026. /VCG At least 19 Palestinians, including two children aged eight and 12, were injured in attacks by Israeli settlers across the occupied West Bank on Friday, according to the Palestinian Wall and Settlement Resistance Commission. The commission said in a statement that it documented 34 attacks and violations targeting Palestinian farmers, land and crops across the West Bank that day. Two foreign journalists were also injured in the clashes. Among them was American photojournalist Heidi Levine, who was hospitalized after being beaten by masked Israeli settlers while covering the olive harvest near Ramallah, according to media reports. The attacks took place in several areas, including Ramallah, Nablus, Jenin, Tulkarm and Hebron. Settlers, under the protection of Israeli forces, surrounded and beat Palestinian farmers harvesting olives, forced them off their land and detained some of them, the statement said. The injured included women, elderly people and emergency responders. The attacks also caused significant property damage. Five Palestin","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:28:18 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-17/Israeli-settler-attacks-injure-19-Palestinians-in-West-Bank-1Rja0LxP2dW/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:24
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Shared love of pickleball draws young Americans and Chinese together,Shared love of pickleball draws young Americans and Chinese together,"Shared love of pickleball draws young Americans and Chinese together Shared love of pickleball draws young Americans and Chinese together Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied A group of about 30 American college students are in China this week for a people-to-people exchange program built around pickleball. Beyond friendly matches with their Chinese peers, they're also exploring some of the country's historic landmarks, technology hubs and urban renewal projects. The visit comes as China has pledged to invite 100,000 young Americans to China for exchanges and study over the next five years. The program is jointly organized by China Center for International People-to-People Exchange (CCIPE), the Arts Chinese Students and Scholars Association (ART CSSA), and other relevant organizations. The International Youth Partnership Program, an initiative of the Foundation for the Development of Science and Technology in China, is a key component of the event and is jointly advanced by the Foundation and ART CSSA. CGTN follows their journey to see how a shared love of sport is bringing young people from the two countries closer together.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:36:07 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/Shared-love-of-pickleball-draws-young-Americans-and-Chinese-together-1RhGZh1Hh8Q/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:24
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,Ebola vaccine clinical trial to begin in DR Congo by end of October,Ebola vaccine clinical trial to begin in DR Congo by end of October,"Ebola vaccine clinical trial to begin in DR Congo by end of October The first clinical trial of an Ebola vaccine in the Democratic Republic of Congo is expected to begin by the end of October, the World Health Organization (WHO) said Tuesday. Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied The first clinical trial of an Ebola vaccine in the Democratic Republic of Congo is expected to begin by the end of October, the World Health Organization (WHO) said Tuesday. The country's worst-ever Ebola outbreak has surpassed 9,000 cases, with more than 4,000 deaths. The outbreak is caused by the Bundibugyo strain, for which no approved vaccine or treatment is available. Governor of Ituri province Gaby Kasongo Mulumba receives the first dose of the Ervebo Ebola vaccine to encourage the population to do so, at an Ebola vaccination center in Bunia, Ituri province, Congo, September 19, 2026. /VCG The trial, known as Tumaini, will assess whether Ervebo, a vaccine approved for the more common Zaire strain, offers protection against Bundibugyo. It is also expected to include two candidate vaccines targeting the strain, developed by the University of Oxford and Moderna. Anthony Scott, chair of the WHO's Strategic Advisory Group of Experts on Immunisation, said the trial would provide urgently needed evidence to guide vaccine policy decisions. However, insecurity and population displacement continue to hamper outbreak control by restricting access to healthcare, disrupting surveillance and delaying research, the WHO said. Meanwhile, Doctors Without Borders is conducting","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:37:32 GMT",https://newsaf.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-14/Ebola-vaccine-clinical-trial-to-begin-in-DR-Congo-by-end-of-October-1ReIPiODdbW/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:24
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,"CENC: M6.9 earthquake hits Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia","CENC: M6.9 earthquake hits Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia","CENC: M6.9 earthquake hits Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia CENC: M6.9 earthquake hits Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. CGTN Copied A magnitude-6.9 earthquake hit the Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia, on Friday at a depth of 150 kilometers, according to the China Earthquake Networks Center (CENC).","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:39:07 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/news-1RhE8yHVzby/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:24
CGTN (EN),China (State),en,China urges Japan to abandon nuclear weapons ambitions,China urges Japan to abandon nuclear weapons ambitions,"China urges Japan to abandon nuclear weapons ambitions China urges Japan to abandon nuclear weapons ambitions Our Privacy Statement & Cookie Policy By continuing to browse our site you agree to our use of cookies, revised Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. You can change your cookie settings through your browser. Copied China has criticized Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi for remarks suggesting Japan could consider allowing nuclear weapons into the country. Speaking on Wednesday, Takaichi said there was room to revisit a 2010 statement by then-Foreign Minister Katsuya Okada on the possibility of allowing US forces to bring nuclear weapons into Japan under exceptional circumstances. Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said on Friday that the remarks reveal the Japanese government's growing nuclear ambitions and risk undermining regional and global peace and stability.","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:07:50 GMT",https://news.cgtn.com/news/2026-10-16/China-urges-Japan-to-abandon-nuclear-weapons-ambitions-1Ri01AxruMM/p.html?UTM_Source=cgtn&UTM_Medium=rss&UTM_Campaign=World,2026-10-18 01:49:24
The Hindu,South Asia,en,"Clashes and fires break out as protesters rally across France, joining students","Clashes and fires break out as protesters rally across France, joining students","Clashes and fires break out as protesters rally across France, joining students Police fired tear gas and water cannons to push back people wearing hoods and masks and throwing fireworks, paving stones and other objects at officers in the Place de la République, northeast of the Paris city centre You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Published- October 18, 2026 07:05 am IST - Paris This photograph shows a fire burning and destroying the city hall after a group of individuals forced entry into the building during ongoing protest action against the ""high cost of living"", in Limoges, central France on October 17, 2026 as part of a nationwide call for mobilisation bringing together various groups expressing their anger: former ""Yellow Vest"", secondary school and university students, climate activists and even farmers. | Photo Credit: AFP Cars were set on fire and shops were looted in Paris on Saturday (October 17, 2026) as police used tear gas and water cannons to disperse violentprotesters who joined nationwide demonstrationsagainst rising living costs and in support of high school students' grievances. Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez's office reported “a growing number of violent incidents” across the country, including assaults on officers, looting and damage to public buildings. Police made at least 272 arrests across the country, including in Paris. Protesters across France responded to calls on social media to revive the ","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 07:05:54 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/clashes-and-fires-break-out-as-protesters-rally-across-france-joining-students/article71598941.ece,2026-10-18 01:49:25
The Hindu,South Asia,en,Trump waives sanction threat over Russian oil purchases,Trump waives sanction threat over Russian oil purchases,"Trump waives sanction threat over Russian oil purchases Move offers relief to Indian refiners amid West Asia conflict; decision comes ahead of U.S. midterm elections You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- October 18, 2026 06:56 am IST - Washington US President Donald Trump gestures as he attends a MAGA Inc. dinner at Mar-a-Lago resort, in Palm Beach, on October 16, 2026 | Photo Credit: Reuters U.S. President Donald Trump on Saturday (October 17, 2026) waived key provisions of a new law that authorised punitive tariffs on countries purchasing Russian oil, offering relief to India. The ‘Lindsey O. Graham Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act of 2026’ (SRIA Act), ratified on September 18, authorised increasing tariffs on countries continuing to buy Russian oil by as much as 100% as Washington sought to tighten Moscow’s oil revenues. The waiver announced on Saturday (October 17, 2026) assures Indian refiners of greater flexibility to continue to purchase oil from Moscow, with supplies from West Asia affected because of the resurgence of conflict. The decision by Mr. Trump that comes just ahead of the October 18 deadline set by the Congress for a determination on sanctions is also expected to ease the discussions during U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio’s visit to Mumbai and Jamnagar from Octobe","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:56:05 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/donald-trump-waives-sanctions-tariffs-on-purchase-of-russian-oil-and-gas/article71595243.ece,2026-10-18 01:49:25
The Hindu,South Asia,en,"Indian student groups in London protest against CEC Gyanesh Kumar, SIR; Govt supporters hold counter-protest","Indian student groups in London protest against CEC Gyanesh Kumar, SIR; Govt supporters hold counter-protest","Indian student groups in London protest against CEC Gyanesh Kumar, SIR; Govt supporters hold counter-protest While the “Stop Vote Chori” protest cheered for activist Dhruv Rathee as the keynote speaker, chants of “Modi, Modi” rang out from a smaller group across the Gandhi statue, being kept apart by Metropolitan Police officers You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- October 18, 2026 06:48 am IST - London People supporting and opposing the Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar and the Cockroach Janta Party gather at Parliament Square, in London on October 17, 2026 | Photo Credit: ANI Hundreds gathered at Mahatma Gandhi’s statue at Parliament Square in London on Saturday (October 17, 2026) for a protest organised by the Opposition Congress and UK-based Indian students’ groups against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar and the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) of electoral rolls. Also Read:Delhi anti-CEC protests: Dipke released after signing peace bond, sporadic protests continue While the “Stop Vote Chori” protest cheered for activist Dhruv Rathee as the keynote speaker, chants of “Modi, Modi” rang out from a smaller group across the Gandhi statue, being kept apart by Metropolitan Police officers. Anti-CEC protest updates on October 17, 2026 The face-off between the groups got heated as each tried to drown out the other’s chants. “We don’t want any foreign interference. I am here at Parliament Square to address Indians and NRIs,” said Mr.","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:48:17 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/indian-student-groups-in-london-protest-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-sir-govt-supporters-hold-counter-protest/article71597243.ece,2026-10-18 01:49:25
The Hindu,South Asia,en,Earthquake of 6.9 magnitude hits near Ozernovskiy in Russia,Earthquake of 6.9 magnitude hits near Ozernovskiy in Russia,"Earthquake of 6.9 magnitude hits near Ozernovskiy in Russia Scientists estimated its magnitude at 6.5 at first, but later revised it to 6.9. It was felt as a magnitude-5 earthquake in the region, says Geological Survey You are logged in Loading... You don’t have any Active Subscription. Subscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one. Your active subscription(s) Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Products you've access to Additional Subscription Benefits Account Settings Need help with your subscription? Updated- October 18, 2026 06:44 am IST - Moscow Image used for repesentational purposes only. | Photo Credit: Getty Images/iStockphoto Anearthquakeof magnitude 6.9 struck 76 km northeast of Ozernovskiy inRussiaon Friday (October 16, 2026), the U.S. Geological Survey said. The epicentre, with a depth of 143.2 km, was initially determined to be at 52.01 degrees north latitude and 157.25 degrees east longitude, it said. A perceptible earthquake with an intensity of up to four magnitude points has been registered in Kamchatka, Russia's state-runTASSnews agency reported, citing the Kamchatka branch of the Russian Academy of Sciences’ Geophysical Service. “Instrumental intensity in Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky amounted to up to four points,” scientists said. Scientists estimated its magnitude at 6.5 at first, but later revised it to 6.9. It was felt as a magnitude-5 earthquake in the region, it said. “According to verified information, the magnitude of this seismic event was 6.9. Its epicentre was located on land, 156 km southwest of Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky, at a depth of 138 km. In Petropavlovsk-Kamcha","Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:44:43 +0530",https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/earthquake-near-ozernovskiy-russia/article71591222.ece,2