Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Limoges Town Hall 'largely lost' after far-left rioters set historic building on fire amid French unrest,Limoges Town Hall 'largely lost' after far-left rioters set historic building on fire amid French unrest,"Limoges Town Hall 'largely lost' after far-left rioters set historic building on fire amid French unrest Rioters set fire to the historic Limoges Town Hall, collapsing its roof and destroying much of the landmark as France&apos;s protests rage on. Far-left protests and riots have broken out across Europe and in France, where police and violent rioters have clashed, leading to destructive fires to businesses and infrastructure. (Credit: Reuters) A historic building in the French town of Limoges, about three hours south of Paris, has been ""largely lost"" after it was set on fire by rioters as demonstrations continue acrossFrance. The Limoges Town Hall was built in 1883, and was made a historic landmark in 1975. ""The roof has collapsed onto lower floors, except the west wing, and two-thirds of the exterior has already disappeared,"" the local prefect, Maurice Barate, told the AFP news agency. The tower roof of the 143-year-old Limoges Town Hall collapses. MASSIVE FIRE DESTROYS 400-YEAR-OLD FOOD MARKET, LEAVING HISTORIC LANDMARK IN RUINS Barate called it ""a deliberate act by hooligans,"" adding that it was a ""catastrophe for heritage."" The destruction came as far-leftanti-government protestsand violent clashes entered their fourth week in the European country over the cost of living. On Saturday, outgoing PresidentEmmanuel Macronwrote on social media: ""There is no place for violence in our republic."" FRANCE EXPLODES AGAIN AS STUDENTS RIOT OVER EDUCATION Fire destroys Limoges Town Hall after rioters broke into the historic building to protest the ""high cost of living,"" in Limoges, central France on Saturday.(Pascal Lachenaud / AFP via Getty Images) ""Those who have broken, attacked the prefectures as well as businesses, looted ","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:56:37 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/limoges-town-hall-largely-lost-after-far-left-rioters-set-historic-building-fire-amid-french-unrest,2026-10-18 01:49:49
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Three men get 158 years each for murdering American and Australian surfers, dumping bodies in Mexican well","Three men get 158 years each for murdering American and Australian surfers, dumping bodies in Mexican well","Three men get 158 years each for murdering American and Australian surfers, dumping bodies in Mexican well Three men were sentenced to 158 years each in Ensenada, Baja California, for the murders of surfers Callum and Jake Robinson and Carter Redd Rhoad. Fox News Flash top headlines are here. Check out what's clicking on FoxNews.com. Three men inMexicoreceived 158-year prison sentences Friday for the murders of Australian surfers Callum and Jake Robinson and their American friend Carter Redd Rhoad. A federal judge in the town of Ensenada,Baja Californiasentenced Jesús Gerardo García, Irineo Francisco and Ángel Jesús each to 158 years and nine months in prison for murder, robbery with violence and vehicle theft with violence. An accomplice of García's — Ary Gisell Silva Raya — was also convicted of aggravated robbery with violence and vehicle theft with violence and sentenced to 20 years in November after agreeing to an abbreviated trial. AMERICANS WARNED POPULAR TRAVEL ROUTES THIS SUMMER COULD CARRY CRIME AND KIDNAPPING RISKS Jesus Gerardo 'N', known as 'El Kekas', one of three men found guilty of murdering Australian brothers Callum and Jake Robinson and their American friend Carter Rhoad during a surfing trip in April 2024, is pictured in this handout image released October 16, 2026.(Baja California State Attorney General's Office (FGE)/Handout via REUTERS) García, Francisco and Jesús were convicted last week of killing the Robinson brothers and Rhoad, which authorities said was carried out in order to steal the tires from the deceased men's truck. ""The attackers pull out a gun they were carrying and kill the person who initially resisted the robbery, then on the other two,"" Baja California prosecutor María Elena Andrade sa","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:38:52 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/three-men-158-years-murdering-american-australian-surfers-dumping-bodies-mexican-well,2026-10-18 01:49:50
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Former US ambassador says South Korea prosecuted him over speech made on American soil,Former US ambassador says South Korea prosecuted him over speech made on American soil,"Former US ambassador says South Korea prosecuted him over speech made on American soil Ambassador Morse Tan faces trial in South Korea over comments he made about crimes allegedly committed by its president, claims Korean authorities have refuted. Fox News correspondent Lucas Tomlinson reports on President Donald Trump’s plan to scale back joint military exercises with South Korea on ‘The Story.’ A former U.S. diplomat appeared in court in South Korea Friday facing charges of defamation against President Lee Jae Myung for comments made on American soil in a case that has left him stranded in the Asian country. Morse Tan's troubles began after he delivered a talk in June 2025 at the National Press Club in Washington, D.C., and responded to a question where he brought up theSouth Koreanleader's alleged involvement in a crime as an adolescent. Since visiting the country in May, Tan has not been allowed to leave due to the case against him, having been charged under the Act on Promotion of Information and Communications Network Utilization and Information Protection, etc., and the Criminal Act. Tan issued his remarks about Lee’s alleged juvenile crimes at a National Press Club event titled: ""Report on Election Fraudin the June 3 South Korean Presidential election."" In response to a question about President Lee and other issues, Tan responded by citing allegations from a few years back that Lee was involved in a gang rape and murder when he was a teenager. He added that Lee, now 62, was sent to a juvenile detention center and did not complete junior high and high school. SOUTH KOREAN PRESIDENT JUMPS TO INVEST IN MILITARY AFTER TRUMP CUTS JOINT EXERCISES South Korean President Lee Jae Myung speaks during a press conference o","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:31:01 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/former-us-ambassador-says-south-korea-prosecuted-him-over-speech-made-american-soil,2026-10-18 01:49:51
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Violence erupts at France protests as Macron warns unrest is being exploited,Violence erupts at France protests as Macron warns unrest is being exploited,"Violence erupts at France protests as Macron warns unrest is being exploited French President Emmanuel Macron called for calm as tear gas, water cannons and over 8,000 arrests mark weeks of violent clashes across the country. Fox News correspondent Stephanie Bennett details the ‘convergence of grievances’ that brought protests to a breaking point on ‘Fox Report.’ Violent clashes broke out across France Saturday as demonstrations entered a fourth week. Earlier in the week, PresidentEmmanuel Macronmade some of his most direct comments yet on the protests as he enters his final six months in office. In his weekly cabinet meeting, Macron ""stressed that young people have legitimate concerns,"" government spokeswoman Maud Bregeontold the AFP,""but these are being exploited for political purposes and turned into urban violence."" Bregeon added that Macron called on his ministers to come up with ""concrete responses"" to the unrest within weeks. FRANCE EXPLODES AGAIN AS STUDENTS RIOT OVER EDUCATION This comes as anational day of protestover rising costs of living and additional student grievances led to violence in Paris and other major cities today. While many of the protests were without violence, many have descended into violent riots. Police used tear gas and water cannons Saturday to disperse violent groups in the capital, where people wearing hoods and masks threw fireworks and other objects at officers in the Place de la République. The interior ministry reported assaults on police, looting and damage to public buildings, saying there have been at least 272 arrests nationwide. A rioter faces off with French riot police amid clashes Saturday during a demonstration against the cost of living and rising fu","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:03:16 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/violence-erupts-france-protests-macron-warns-unrest-being-exploited,2026-10-18 01:49:51
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"'Vast majority' of Iran's attempted attacks on Strait of Hormuz are unsuccessful, CENTCOM spokesman says","'Vast majority' of Iran's attempted attacks on Strait of Hormuz are unsuccessful, CENTCOM spokesman says","'Vast majority' of Iran's attempted attacks on Strait of Hormuz are unsuccessful, CENTCOM spokesman says U.S. Central Command Spokesperson and U.S. Navy Capt. Tim Hawkins tells Fox News Digita the Strait of Hormuz remains &quot;open&quot; for commercial shipping. U.S. Central Command spokesperson and U.S. Navy Capt. Tim Hawkins speaks to Fox News Digital about Operation Epic Fury against Iran. The ""vast majority"" ofIran's attempted attackson shipping in the Strait of Hormuz are ""unsuccessful"" as the key waterway remains open for transit, U.S. Central Command spokesperson and U.S. Navy Capt. Tim Hawkins told Fox News Digital this week. Hawkins spoke after CENTCOM said the GFS Pride, a Singapore-flagged, Cyprus-owned container ship was hit by an Iranian projectile in the Strait of Hormuz Wednesday and sunk while being towed ashore due to a fire on board the ship. ""The vast majority of Iran's attempted attacks on innocent civilian mariners transiting an international waterway, being the Strait of Hormuz, they are unsuccessful,"" Hawkins said. ""As a matter of fact,the U.S. militaryhas assisted in providing coordinated protection for thousands of ships that have safely transited. LIVE UPDATES: IRANIAN ARMY SPOKESPERSON SAYS STRAIT OF HORMUZ WILL REOPEN 'IF AMERICA LEAVES THE REGION' ""That translates to about 97% of the ships that have sought to transit the Strait of Hormuz have done so successfully without being hit by an Iranian projectile. ""But let's be clear here. What the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps of Iran is doing is unjustified, and it's also unsuccessful because they are not achieving their objective of closing the Strait of Hormuz,"" he added. ""It is open, it is available for transit and we've seen that transit continue this v","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:46:37 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/vast-majority-irans-attempted-attacks-strait-hormuz-unsuccessful-centcom-spokesman-says,2026-10-18 01:49:52
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Pope Leo XIV discharged from hospital, will return to Vatican after surgery to remove lung cancer","Pope Leo XIV discharged from hospital, will return to Vatican after surgery to remove lung cancer","Pope Leo XIV discharged from hospital, will return to Vatican after surgery to remove lung cancer Pope Leo XIV received blood tests and a chest X-ray at Gemelli Hospital, confirming he is well enough to return to the Vatican after surgery. A crowd of supporters greets Pope Leo XIV outside of Gemelli Hospital in Rome, Italy, Saturday, Oct. 17 as the pontiff returns to the Vatican after surgery to remove a cancerous node in his right lung. Credit: Reuters. Thousands of supporters gathered outside Gemelli Hospital in Rome Saturday yelling ""Papa!"" afterPope Leo XIVwas released after surgery to remove a cancerous node in his lung. The Holy See announced early Saturday he would be leaving to return to the Vatican. ""Following the doctors’ assessment this morning, Pope Leo XIV will be discharged today from Gemelli Hospital, where he was hospitalized for surgery on his right lung,"" a statement from the Holy See read. ""He will leave the hospital in the early afternoon and return to the Vatican. Tomorrow, he will lead the Angelus prayer from the window of the papal apartment."" Pope Leo reacts while sitting in a car as he leaves Gemelli Hospital after his lung surgery and cancer diagnosis, in Rome, Italy, Oct. 17, 2026.(Reuters/Remo Casilli) The pope received blood tests and a chest X-ray Saturday, both of which confirmed he is well enough to return to the Vatican,according toVatican News. Before he departed, Pope Leo reportedly visited the children's oncology ward. While in the hospital, the Pope received letters from some of the children in the ward. ""Pope Leo, our prayers are for you,"" a girl named Eleonora, who had been receiving treatment in the oncology ward, wrote to him, according toletters releasedby Vatican News.","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:19:52 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/pope-leo-xiv-discharged-hospital-return-vatican-surgery-remove-lung-cancer,2026-10-18 01:49:53
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,ChinaAid raises alarm over imprisoned Chinese pastor's health as family seeks answers,ChinaAid raises alarm over imprisoned Chinese pastor's health as family seeks answers,"ChinaAid raises alarm over imprisoned Chinese pastor's health as family seeks answers ChinaAid founder Bob Fu says reports of Pastor Wang Yi&apos;s advanced liver cancer in a Chinese prison are credible but cannot be independently verified. ChinaAid founder Bob Fu warns that imprisoned Chinese pastor Wang Yi may have advanced liver cancer as his family struggles to obtain medical information. The founder of Christian human rights organization ChinaAid is raising concerns over the health of an imprisoned Chinese pastor who may be suffering from advanced liver cancer, and his family continues to face restrictions on visitation and access to medical information. Rev. Dr. Bob Fu, founder and president of ChinaAid, told Fox News in an interview that reports concerning Pastor Wang Yi's health are ""very worrying,"" citing information received from multiple sources inside China. Wang, the founding pastor of Early Rain Covenant Church in Chengdu, has been imprisoned since December 2018 and is serving a nine-year sentence on charges of inciting subversion of state power and illegal business operations. Although Fu believes that reports of advanced liver cancer are credible, he acknowledged that his organization has not been able to independently confirm the diagnosis. REPORT DETAILS RISING PRESSURE ON UNDERGROUND CATHOLICS AS CHINA DENIES CRACKDOWN ChinaAid President Bob Fu urged the Trump administration to press Chinese officials for answers about imprisoned pastor Wang Yi's health and restricted family visits.(ChinaAid) Fu said ChinaAid was ""not able to really independently verify"" the reports, citing restrictions on access to Wang and the absence of an independent medical examination. The organization first publicly rai","Sat, 17 Oct 2026 06:00:44 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/chinaaid-raises-alarm-imprisoned-chinese-pastor-health-family-seeks-answers,2026-10-18 01:49:53
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Recovering from lung surgery, Pope Leo urges Putin to agree to ceasefire in Russian-held Ukraine city","Recovering from lung surgery, Pope Leo urges Putin to agree to ceasefire in Russian-held Ukraine city","Recovering from lung surgery, Pope Leo urges Putin to agree to ceasefire in Russian-held Ukraine city Pope Leo called Vladimir Putin from his hospital bed to urge a ceasefire in Oleshky, Ukraine, where food deliveries have been blocked since May. Pulmonologist Cedric Rutland joins 'Fox & Friends' to share medical insights on Pope Leo's health following lung cancer surgery. Dr. Rutland explains the typical recovery process for lung surgery, noting why the pope is expected to remain in the hospital for a week. Pope Leo XIV called Russian PresidentVladimir Putinwhile recovering from surgery in the hospital to urge him to call a ceasefire in the city of Oleshky in Ukraine. ""During the conversation, the Holy Father expressed his deep concern about the grave humanitarian situation in the city of Oleshky, in the Kherson region, and called for a ceasefire to allow the delivery of food and medical assistance and the voluntary and safe evacuation of the civilian population,""the Vaticansaid in a statement. ""Finally, theHoly Fatherreaffirmed the Holy See’s commitment to promoting dialogue and peace."" TRUMP ANNOUNCES IMMEDIATE ENERGY CEASEFIRE BETWEEN RUSSIA AND UKRAINE Pope Leo called Russian President Vladimir Putin while recovering from lung surgery to discuss Ukraine.(Vatican Media via AP; Andrew Harnik/Getty Images) The situation inOleshkyis dire with no humanitarian food deliveries allowed in the Russian-controlled city since May. It also has no electricity, gas or running water, and the hospital is barely functional. The pope wasdiagnosed with lung cancerTuesday and underwent a procedure to remove the lower lobe of his right lung. The 71-year-old remained in the hospital recovering on Friday but seemed to be doing well. Alo","Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:10:21 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/recovering-lung-surgery-pope-leo-urges-putin-agree-ceasefire-russian-held-ukraine-city,2026-10-18 01:49:54
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Autistic teen lured to fake Snapchat meetup, brutally beaten by group of teens: report","Autistic teen lured to fake Snapchat meetup, brutally beaten by group of teens: report","Autistic teen lured to fake Snapchat meetup, brutally beaten by group of teens: report Video captured the violent beating of a 15-year-old boy with autism near a Stawell train station after he was lured through a Snapchat meetup. Fox News Flash top headlines are here. Check out what's clicking on FoxNews.com. Three teenage boys were charged after a 15-year-old boy with autism was beaten and robbed near a train station inAustraliain a violent attack captured on video as other teenagers watched. The assaulthappened Oct. 5 in Stawell, a town in the Australian state of Victoria, after the victim was reportedly lured to the area through a Snapchat meetup arranged with two girls, according to Australian news outlet news.com.au. Video ofthe attackshows several teenagers punching and kicking the boy, knocking him to the ground and repeatedly striking him as he attempts to get away. One attacker demands the victim hand over his shoes before the group allows him to leave. TEXAS TEENS ACCUSED OF USING DATING APPS TO LURE YOUNG MEN INTO VIOLENT ROBBERIES THAT LEFT ONE VICTIM SHOT The Stawell railway station in Victoria, Australia, near where a 15-year-old boy was allegedly attacked and robbed by a group of teenagers Oct. 5, 2026.(Google Maps) Victoria Police announced Tuesday that detectives had charged one 14-year-old boy and two 15-year-old boys after an investigation. Detectives from the Northern Grampians Crime Investigation Unit executed four search warrants in the region before arresting the teenagers, police said. All three face charges of affray, robbery, recklessly causing injury and theft. They are expected to appear in a children's court at a later date. TEEN BURGLARY RING LINKED TO NEARLY 80 BAY AREA ","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:40:32 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/autistic-teen-lured-fake-snapchat-meetup-brutally-beaten-group-teens-report,2026-10-18 01:49:55
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Houthis emerge as global threat beyond Iran control amid Saudi strikes, former envoy warns","Houthis emerge as global threat beyond Iran control amid Saudi strikes, former envoy warns","Houthis emerge as global threat beyond Iran control amid Saudi strikes, former envoy warns Tim Lenderking warns Houthi rebels are building homegrown weapons capabilities independent of Iran, turning Yemen&apos;s conflict into a global threat. Fox News chief foreign correspondent Trey Yingst reports on claims that Iran-backed Houthis are developing advanced missiles using Chinese parts and examines the potential threat to Saudi Arabia and stability across the Middle East on 'The Story.' TheHouthisare increasingly operating independently of Tehran, posing a ""clear and very present danger"" on the international stage as the terror group rearms and sharpens its strike capabilities, a former U.S. envoy warned Thursday. The warning came amid deadly missile and drone attacks on Saudi Arabia in recent days and growing threats to global shipping routes and critical Middle East infrastructure in the run-up. Turki al-Maliki, spokesperson for the Saudi-led coalition in Yemen, also confirmed Thursday that Houthi attacks on King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh had killed 17 and injured 333 others from Oct. 7-11. Speaking at a news conference in Riyadh, al-Maliki said the Oct. 10 attack involved 10 drones, missiles and other projectiles. ""King Khalid International Airport has been subjected to 20 attacks since (Oct. 1),"" he noted. Tim Lenderking, who served as U.S. special envoy for Yemen from 2021 to 2025 and was posted to Saudi Arabia from 2013 to 2016, said Saudi officials had warned more than a decade ago that the Houthis would become a major threat, a prediction he says has now materialized. SAUDI FOREIGN MINISTER WARNS HOUTHI THREAT GOES GLOBAL AS TRUMP HOLDS FIRE The Houthis are increasingly operating independently ","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:25:57 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/houthis-emerge-global-threat-iran-control-saudi-attacks-says-former-envoy,2026-10-18 01:49:56
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Albania rioters clash with police for Socialist government as European unrest spreads,Albania rioters clash with police for Socialist government as European unrest spreads,"Albania rioters clash with police for Socialist government as European unrest spreads Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama vowed not to resign as protests in Tirana erupted for a third day, with police deploying tear gas and water cannons. Clashes between police and protesters who are against Albania's Socialist government erupted in the country's capital of Tirana for the third consecutive day on Thursday. (Credit: Reuters) Clashes between police and protesterswho are against Albania's Socialist government erupted in the country's capital for the third consecutive day Thursday as Prime Minister Edi Rama vowed he will not resign. Rioters in Tirana were seen throwing rocks at a police cordon outside Albania's Education Ministry, promptinglaw enforcementto respond with tear gas and water cannons, according to The Associated Press. The clashes followed riots on Wednesday when protesters attacked government buildings, banks and businesses, leaving 89 people injured, including 61 police officers. ""As for calls for my resignation, governments are changed through democratic elections. We had elections last year, not a revolution,"" Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama told Reuters on Thursday. ALBANIAN PROTESTERS FLOOD STREETS DEMANDING PRIME MINISTER'S RESIGNATION AMID CORRUPTION ACCUSATIONS Riot police officers detain a hooded protester during clashes near the Ministry of Education in Tirana, Albania, on Tuesday, Oct. 13, 2026.(Hameraldi Agolli/AP) ""My responsibility is to listen, address legitimate concerns and keep Albania moving forward,"" he added. ""The alternative would be a betrayal of the Albanians who gave me a strong mandate to complete negotiations on European Union membership."" Thursday's protests included stud","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:44:31 -0400",