als, many of whom w","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:30:16 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/not-wanted-irish-hotel-reportedly-cancels-70-rooms-reserved-antisemitism-conference-attendees,2026-10-18 01:49:58
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,UN inquiry member says some genocide claims against Israel unverified as Gaza reports population growth,UN inquiry member says some genocide claims against Israel unverified as Gaza reports population growth,"UN inquiry member says some genocide claims against Israel unverified as Gaza reports population growth Experts say Palestinian Ministry of Health mortality figures contradict famine declarations and genocide allegations as Gaza&apos;s population grew in 2025. Elie Wiesel Foundation Chairman Elisha Wiesel joins 'The Story' to discuss New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani facing bipartisan backlash over his social media post regarding the October 7 attacks. The allegations of genocide against Israel took more hits this week following the reported admission by a senior member of the U.N. Commission of Inquiry on Israel that claims had not been independently verified. This comes as the Palestinian Ministry of Health data shows Gaza’s population grew in 2025. Critics say the accusations fueled antisemitism around the world and that those pushing the genocide claims — including major international media outlets — need to be made accountable for their words. In September 2025, the Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory, including East Jerusalem and Israel (COI) released a report stating that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza since October 2023. In the report, the COI cited an article from the Guardian stating that 83% of Gazans killed in the conflict were civilians. ISRAEL SLAMS UN REPORT AS 'POLITICAL BLOOD LIBEL' FOR ALLEGING DELIBERATE TARGETING OF PALESTINIAN CHILDREN Chair of the Independent International Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory, including East Jerusalem, and Israel, South African Judge Navanethem ""Navi"" Pillay, right, speaks next to Commission Member Chris Sidoti during a press conference in Geneva on September 16, 2025.(Fabrice COFFRINI/AFP via Get","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:37:38 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/un-inquiry-member-says-some-genocide-claims-against-israel-unverified-gaza-reports-population-growth,2026-10-18 01:49:59
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,El Salvador's Bukele announces plan to free up to half of prisoners jailed in gang crackdown,El Salvador's Bukele announces plan to free up to half of prisoners jailed in gang crackdown,"El Salvador's Bukele announces plan to free up to half of prisoners jailed in gang crackdown Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele unveiled a plan to free up to half of 90,000 detainees arrested under the state of emergency targeting gangs. Fox News congressional correspondent Bill Melugin has details on the arrest of Alexis Antonio Cedillos-Campos, an illegal immigrant from El Salvador suspected of brutally stabbing a woman in Virginia, on ‘Special Report.’ Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele has unveiled a plan that could allow the conditional early release of up to half of those detained under a state of emergency that authorities used to arrest more than 90,000 people in the past four and a half years as part of an effort to curbviolent criminal gangactivity. Bukele's plan to cut the prison population was announced on Tuesday night. It would focus on freeing prisoners who were deemed gang collaborators, a broad term that can include various people, including gang lookouts and those who make extortion payments. ""There are many people who have indeed committed crimes, but their crime was collaborating with gangs,"" Bukele said. ""They deserve to be in jail, but we come from a country where collaborating with gangs wasn’t so unusual, and if we were to arrest everyone who collaborated with gangs, we would have to arrest 20% of the population."" Without offering details, the president indicated that authorities plan to analyze cases to determine potential early release with monitoring, which could apply to half of the people detained during the state of emergency. TRUMP ADMINISTRATION SAYS FEDERAL AUTHORITIES HAVE ARRESTED MORE THAN 10,000 SUSPECTED GANG MEMBERS Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele has unveiled a plan th","Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:01:59 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/el-salvador-bukele-announces-plan-free-half-prisoners-jailed-gang-crackdown,2026-10-18 01:50:00
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Trump wishes Pope Leo speedy recovery after lung cancer diagnosis, speaks highly of pontiff's brother","Trump wishes Pope Leo speedy recovery after lung cancer diagnosis, speaks highly of pontiff's brother","Trump wishes Pope Leo speedy recovery after lung cancer diagnosis, speaks highly of pontiff's brother President Donald Trump revealed Pope Leo XIV&apos;s brother is a friend and avid MAGA supporter with memorabilia &quot;all over&quot; his house while wishing the pontiff well. President Trump describes his friendship with the pontiff's brother while sharing a heartfelt message for Pope Leo amid his reported cancer battle. President Donald Trumpwished Pope Leo XIV a speedy recovery Wednesday following his lung cancer diagnosis, revealing that he is friends with the pontiff's brother, whom he described as an enthusiastic MAGA supporter. Speaking to reporters aboard Air Force One while traveling from Arizona to Montana, Trump expressed optimism about the 71-year-old pontiff's recovery following surgery to remove part of his right lung. ""I want to see Pope Leo get well. I hear the prognosis for that type of a problem. It's a cancer. It's big stuff. Anytime you have cancer,"" the president said. ""But the prognosis seems to be good, I've watched. And we just want to wish him our love and our best wishes."" POPE LEO XIV BEGINS HISTORIC 4-DAY VISIT TO FRANCE President Donald Trump speaks to reporters after a campaign rally in Bullhead City, Arizona, on Oct. 14, 2026. Later that day, Trump wished Pope Leo XIV a speedy recovery following his lung cancer diagnosis.(Kent NISHIMURA / AFP via Getty Images) Trump then discussed his friendship with the pope's brother and his wife, describing them as enthusiastic supporters of the president. ""His brother is a friend of mine, who's a great — he's a fantastic guy — and his wife. You know, they're big Trump supporters. They have MAGA all over their house,"" he continued. ""And I can say that his brother loves him a lot. L","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:38:47 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/trump-wishes-pope-leo-speedy-recovery-after-lung-cancer-diagnosis-speaks-highly-pontiffs-brother,2026-10-18 01:50:01
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,Woman found floating in sea after going overboard from Royal Caribbean ship,Woman found floating in sea after going overboard from Royal Caribbean ship,"Woman found floating in sea after going overboard from Royal Caribbean ship A 44-year-old woman clung to a lifebuoy for 20 hours in the Ionian Sea after reportedly jumping from Royal Caribbean&apos;s Odyssey of the Seas near Zakynthos. The woman was found clinging to a flotation device after spending nearly 24 hours at sea. (Credit: Hellenic Coast Guard) A woman who went overboard from a Royal Caribbean cruise ship was rescued after spending 20 hours in the water clinging to a lifebuoy, the Hellenic Coast Guard said. The 44-year-old Salvadoran national was traveling aboardOdyssey of the Seasas it sailed through the Ionian Sea near the island of Zakynthos on Saturday, the Greek Ministry of Foreign Affairs told USA Today. The cargo ship MSC Rossella III was assisting in the search and spotted the woman inside the bright orange lifebuoy in dark waters. The vessel alerted authorities, and aGreek Coast Guard crewarrived to toss her ropes and pull her to safety. CRUISE PASSENGER JUMPS FROM BALCONY AND DIES AFTER FALLING OVERBOARD INTO OCEAN A Royal Caribbean passenger was rescued in the waters near a Greek island last week after she jumped overboard.(Hellenic Coast Guard; Getty Images) The woman reportedly told authorities she jumped off the ship because she ""wanted to disembark,"" a Coast Guard spokesperson told Agence France-Presse, adding that ""she was 20 hours at sea."" Following her rescue, she was transported to the port of Katakolo and brought to a local hospital, where a prosecutor ordered a psychiatric evaluation, according to the Hellenic Coast Guard. CARNIVAL CRUISE SHIP PASSENGER DIES AFTER FALLING FROM BALCONY – FBI INVESTIGATES HIGH-SEAS HORROR Greek authorities reportedly deployed a Coast Guard vesse","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:44:29 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/woman-found-floating-sea-going-overboard-royal-caribbean-ship,2026-10-18 01:50:01
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Cartels use drones to scout border agents and map smuggling routes, expert warns","Cartels use drones to scout border agents and map smuggling routes, expert warns","Cartels use drones to scout border agents and map smuggling routes, expert warns The U.S. military detected 378 cartel drone incursions along the Mexico border in 30 days, and experts warn cartels will continue to innovate. Fox News correspondent Max Gorden has the latest on new technology the Pentagon is using to intercept cartel drones at the border on 'America's Newsroom.' MEXICO CITY —Mexican cartelsare said to be using commercial and modified drones to watch U.S. security personnel, map patrol routines and support smuggling corridors along the southern border as authorities expand efforts to disable the aircraft. The U.S. military detected 378 drone incursions along the border during the previous 30 days, Brig. Gen. Brian Filler of Joint Task Force-Southern Border recently told reporters. He said the trend was increasing, and the aircraft were typically commercial drones with cameras used for surveillance tied to smuggling and human trafficking. ""On the border, the most common application is surveillance and reconnaissance as cartels look to establish a pattern of life for U.S. security personnel and support smuggling outcomes across the border,"" Austin Doctor told Fox News Digital. Doctor directs strategic initiatives at the National Counterterrorism Innovation, Technology and Education Center and teaches criminology and criminal justice at the University of Nebraska at Omaha. US MILITARY LAUNCHES FIRST AUTONOMOUS WARFARE COMMAND TO DEPLOY UNMANNED SYSTEMS ACROSS LATIN AMERICA A new law allows law enforcement in Arizona to shoot down drones suspected of participating in criminal activity along the U.S.-Mexico border.(iStock) A U.S. Customs and Border Protection spokesperson confirmed the g","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:51:45 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/cartels-use-drones-scout-border-agents-map-smuggling-routes-expert-warns,2026-10-18 01:50:02
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Pope Leo undergoes blood tests, X-ray following cancer surgery, Vatican says","Pope Leo undergoes blood tests, X-ray following cancer surgery, Vatican says","Pope Leo undergoes blood tests, X-ray following cancer surgery, Vatican says Pope Leo XIV began walking and resumed eating after thoracic surgery at Rome&apos;s Gemelli Hospital, with blood tests and an X-ray being part of his recovery. Pulmonologist Dr. Cedric Rutland joins 'Fox & Friends' to share medical insights on Pope Leo's health following lung cancer surgery. Dr. Rutland explains the typical recovery process for lung surgery, noting why the pope is expected to remain in the hospital for a week. Pope Leo XIVunderwent blood tests and a chest X-ray Wednesday following surgery to remove a small nodule on his lung, with his recovery going ""as expected,"" the Vatican announced. The development comes afterthe Holy See Press Officesaid ""the night passed calmly for the Pope"" at Rome’s Gemelli Hospital. The 71-year-old pontiff on Tuesday underwent thoracic surgery to remove the lower lobe of his right lung with doctors confirming he had lung adenocarcinoma, a form of lung cancer, according to a statement released by the Holy See Press Office. ""This morning, the Holy Father underwent the blood tests and chest X-ray scheduled after surgery. The results confirm that his postoperative recovery is progressing normally: the values are within the expected range for the type of operation performed,"" it attributed Dr. Luigi Carbone and Professor Stefano Margaritora as saying. Pope Leo XIV arrives at the Agostino Gemelli Polyclinic in Rome, on Tuesday, Oct. 13, 2026, where he's expected to be operated to remove a lung nodule.(Alessandra Tarantino/AP) POPE LEO DIAGNOSED WITH LUNG CANCER AFTER SURGEONS REMOVE PART OF RIGHT LUNG, VATICAN SAYS ""The Holy Father has undergone respiratory physiotherapy and has begun walking aro","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:29:03 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/pope-leo-undergoes-blood-tests-x-ray-following-cancer-surgery-vatican-says,2026-10-18 01:50:03
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,African nations on ‘knife’s edge’ as US embassy warns Americans of long-range attacks,African nations on ‘knife’s edge’ as US embassy warns Americans of long-range attacks,"African nations on ‘knife’s edge’ as US embassy warns Americans of long-range attacks With regional tensions mounting, the Horn of Africa risks war between Ethiopia and Eritrea. Following attacks in Addis Ababa, the U.S. Embassy warned citizens of long-range threats. Traffic moved through Ethiopia's capital Addis Ababa on Friday (Oct. 2), a day after explosions were heard in the city. (Reuters.) The entire Horn ofAfricaregion is said to be on a knife’s edge. As explosions reportedly claimed to be caused by drones hit Ethiopia's capital city in early October, the U.S. Embassy in Addis Ababa warned U.S. citizens of the danger of ""long-range attacks."" Analysts say there’s a high probability that Ethiopia and Eritrea are about to erupt in a new war, with worrying regional backing for both sides. Former CIA analyst and National Security Council Africa Director Cameron Hudson says the Trump administration needs to become more involved. He told Fox News Digital, ""Regional leaders will say privately that they don’t want a regional war. But with so many armed actors and so much meddling going on in each other’s countries, a regional conflagration becomes increasingly likely. It is this kind of miscalculation that the Trump administration needs to be working now to guard against."" EXCLUSIVE: TRUMP ENVOY BLASTS SOUTH AFRICA OVER HATEFUL ‘KILL' CHANT, SAYS COUNTRY IS DRIFTING TOWARD US FOES The U.S. Embassy in Addis Ababa took to its website to caution Americans in Ethiopia that it ""is aware of reports of possible long-range attacks directed at Ethiopian military installations on several instances in October of this year. U.S. citizens should accordingly exercise caution and follow the advice of local authorities."" The Embassy also hit out at reporte","Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:39:14 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/african-nations-knifes-edge-us-embassy-warns-americans-long-range-attacks,2026-10-18 01:50:04
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Greta Thunberg joins massive French student protests as cars burn, police fire tear gas","Greta Thunberg joins massive French student protests as cars burn, police fire tear gas","Greta Thunberg joins massive French student protests as cars burn, police fire tear gas Greta Thunberg joined student protesters in France amid over 6,100 arrests and widespread school closures as violent clashes with riot police escalate. The Swedish activist rallied alongside students outside a high school near Paris as demonstrations over classroom conditions spread across France, with clashes erupting in several cities. (Credit: AP) Climate activistGreta Thunbergjoined student protesters in France on Tuesday after weeks of violent confrontations with police, thousands of arrests and widespread school closures over demands for education reform. The 23-year-old Swedish activist appeared outside a high school in Saint-Denis, north of Paris, where students were demanding more teachers, better facilities and shorter school days, Reuters reported. More than 6,800 people have been detained since the protests began in September, according to French authorities. Demonstrators have set fires, erected barricades and confronted riot police in cities across France, although many protests have remained peaceful. FRANCE EXPLODES AGAIN AS STUDENTS RIOT OVER EDUCATION Climate activist Greta Thunberg speaks with students outside a high school in Saint-Denis, near Paris, France, on Oct. 13, 2026, as nationwide protests over education reform continue.(JULIEN DE ROSA / AFP via Getty Images) Thunberg, who rose to prominence organizingschool strikes over climate change, criticized the French government's response to the demonstrations. ""We are inspired by the young people who are demanding their basic rights,"" Thunberg told reporters, according to Reuters. She also described the police response as ""extremely violent."" About 161,5","Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:31:12 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/greta-thunberg-joins-massive-french-student-protests-cars-burn-police-fire-tear-gas,2026-10-18 01:50:05
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,‘Peace through strength’: Trump Gaza plan gains global backing one year on,‘Peace through strength’: Trump Gaza plan gains global backing one year on,"‘Peace through strength’: Trump Gaza plan gains global backing one year on Donald Trump&apos;s Board of Peace excludes UNRWA from Gaza&apos;s future as the EU pledges $1 billion and demilitarization efforts gain global momentum. Ret. Four-Star Gen. Jack Keane breaks down the next phase of President Donald Trump's Gaza peace deal on 'Fox & Friends.' Keane explains how the historic agreement mandates the complete disarmament of Hamas and other armed groups, leading to the withdrawal of Israeli forces and the transition of power to a new Palestinian government. A year has passed since PresidentDonald Trumpmade history by brokering a ceasefire between Israel and Hamas, setting in motion an ambitious peace plan aimed at bringing lasting stability to the region. In the days and months since the ceasefire and Trump’s 20-point peace plan took hold, progress has drawn support from across the globe — including from unexpected quarters. Senior advisor to the Board of Peace Josh Gruenbaum told Fox News Digital that the success of the last 12 months was largely attributable to President Donald Trump’s leadership and commitment to seeking peace. TRUMP-BACKED BOARD OF PEACE, ISRAEL 'WILL TAKE ACTION' IF HAMAS REMAINS OUT OF COMPLIANCE: NETANYAHU ADVISOR President Donald Trump poses with the signed agreement at a world leaders' summit on ending the Gaza war, amid a U.S.-brokered prisoner-hostage swap and ceasefire deal between Israel and Hamas, in Sharm el-Sheikh, Egypt, October 13, 2025.(Suzanne Plunkett/Reuters) ""The unlock was somebody who came in, who really knew the file because they had the chance to study it and understand it,"" Gruenbaum said. Trump and his team, including U.S. special envoy to the Middle Eas","Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:18:26 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/peace-through-strength-trump-gaza-plan-gains-global-backing-one-year,2026-10-18 01:50:06
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer after surgeons remove part of right lung, Vatican says","Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer after surgeons remove part of right lung, Vatican says","Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer after surgeons remove part of right lung, Vatican says Pope Leo XIV arrived at Gemelli Hospital in Rome for lung nodule removal after doctors said the growth was identified at a &quot;very early stage.&quot; Doctors later confirmed he had a form of lung cancer. Pope Leo XIV arrived at Agostino Gemelli Hospital in Rome for a procedure to remove a small node in his lung Tuesday. Pope Leo XIVunderwent a procedure at Agostino Gemelli University Hospital in Rome to remove a small nodule on his lung Tuesday, the Vatican said. The 71-year-old pontiff underwent thoracic surgery to remove the lower lobe of his right lung and doctors confirmed he had lung adenocarcinoma, a form of lung cancer, according to a statement released by theHoly See Press Office. The diagnosis was confirmed through a tissue examination conducted during the operation, consistent with findings from preoperative tests, the Vatican said. The pope spent approximately three hours in the operating room, although the surgery itself lasted about 90 minutes. Doctors said the procedure was successful and there were no complications. POPE LEO ANNOUNCES TUMOR ON LUNG, SURGERY PLANNED IN 'NEXT FEW DAYS' Pope Leo XIV is welcomed by Health Director Andrea Cambieri as he arrives at the Gemelli University Hospital for an operation to remove a lump from his lung in Rome on Tuesday.(Alberto Pizzoli/AFP via Getty Images) Leo awoke normally following surgery and, after a brief observation period, returned to his room on the hospital's 10th floor, according to the statement from Dr. Luigi Carbone and Professor Stefano Margaritora. ""Doctors found a small lump in the lung,"" Leo said after an Angelus address at St. Peter's Square on Monday. ""It was identified at a very early stage and well si","Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:24:55 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/pope-leo-diagnosed-lung-cancer-after-surgeons-remove-part-of-right-lung-vatican,2026-10-18 01:50:07
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"NATO warns Russia: 'We will break' forces, destroy 'anything and everything' if you attack","NATO warns Russia: 'We will break' forces, destroy 'anything and everything' if you attack","NATO warns Russia: 'We will break' forces, destroy 'anything and everything' if you attack Gen. Alexus Grynkewich outlined NATO&apos;s strategy to &quot;block, blunt and break&quot; enemy forces at the Warsaw Security Forum amid rising Russia tensions. Professor Azeem Ibrahim says Russia’s heavily militarized Baltic enclave has become a testing ground for hybrid warfare targeting European infrastructure. NATO's top military commander warned Monday that what he called the ""lethal alliance"" would destroy ""anything and everything"" supporting an attack on allied territory and ""break"" enemy warfighting systems to thwart any potential future Russian assault. ""Should the adversary choose to press the attack or commit his reserves, we will break the warfighting system engaged against us,""U.S. Air ForceGen. Alexus Grynkewich said at theWarsaw Security Forum in Poland, in an apparent warning to Moscow. ""This includes not just the attacking force itself, but anything and everything that supports, sustains, and controls that force,"" he said during a panel titled ""Theory of Victory: How Do We Achieve Military Success Against Russia in Deterrence and Defence?"" on the first day of the forum. US ALLIES NEED TO SHOOT DOWN RUSSIAN AIRCRAFT TESTING NATO BOUNDARIES, CZECH PRESIDENT WARNS NATO's top military commander warned Monday that the alliance would destroy ""anything and everything"" supporting an attack on allied territory and ""break"" enemy warfighting systems to thwart any potential future Russian assault.(Photo by Artur Widak/Anadolu via Getty Images) Grynkewich, NATO's supreme allied commander in Europe, also outlined a three-pronged strategy of ""blocking, blunting and breaking"" enemy forces, making clear that while NATO is a defensive","Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:22:08 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/nato-warns-russia-we-break-forces-destroy-anything-everything-you-attack,2026-10-18 01:50:08
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,British adventurer returns home after 28-year walk around the world,British adventurer returns home after 28-year walk around the world,"British adventurer returns home after 28-year walk around the world Adventurer Karl Bushby swam the English Channel and celebrated with fish and chips after his 28-year, 30,000-mile walk from Chile to England. Adventurer Karl Bushby has finally stepped foot on UK soil as he completes a 28-year long journey across the world, Fox News' Stephanie Bennett reports. AdventurerKarl Bushbyhas finally stepped foot on UK soil after a 28-year journey across the world. On Oct. 5, he announced heswam the English Channel, from France to England. While resting in Dover, he said, ""I’m staring at the Union Jack flying outside this hotel. I’ve seen many flags over the days, but that one is special."" On social media he shared one of his first meals back, overjoyed to have authentic British fish and chips again. DALE 'GREY BEARD' SANDERS RECLAIMS TITLE AS OLDEST PERSON TO THRU-HIKE THE APPALACHIAN TRAIL AT 91 Karl Bushby celebrates after swimming across the Caspian Sea from Kazakhstan to Azerbaijan in September 2024.(Resul Rehimov/Anadolu via Getty Images) His journey is not over yet. He hopes to reach the finish line — his mother’s home in Hull — by the end of the month. According tohis website, he received a birthday card in the 1990s from his father about two soldiers arguing over an impossible feat, walking from London to New York via the Bering Strait. Karl grabbed a map and drew a single line, knowing he found his life’s mission. NAVY VETERANS REUNITE AFTER 30 YEARS FOR 'GRUELING' CROSS-COUNTRY BIKE CHALLENGE HONORING 9/11 Bushby is shown moving through Dover, England, on Oct. 9 as he begins the final 250-mile leg of his 28-year journey. On Nov. 1, 1998, the ex-paratrooper started his journey in","Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:28:09 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/british-adventurer-returns-home-after-28-year-walk-around-world,2026-10-18 01:50:10
Fox News (World),North America (Conservative),en,"Zelenskyy accuses Putin of defying Trump's ceasefire push, sends pointed message to White House","Zelenskyy accuses Putin of defying Trump's ceasefire push, sends pointed message to White House","Zelenskyy accuses Putin of defying Trump's ceasefire push, sends pointed message to White House Volodymyr Zelenskyy accuses Vladimir Putin of attacking Ukraine&apos;s gas infrastructure hours after Trump announced an immediate energy ceasefire. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy joins 'America's Newsroom' to express his support for President Donald Trump's energy ceasefire, calling it a 'good first step' toward ending the war. Ukrainian PresidentVolodymyr Zelenskyytold Fox News on Monday that Russia continued attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure despite President Donald Trump's announcement of what he called an immediate energy ceasefire, accusing Vladimir Putin of rejecting Washington's peace efforts and calling for greater pressure on Moscow. ""We are ready today for energy ceasefire, as President Trump said. But I'm not sure that Putin is ready because even after yesterday's messages from the president about energy ceasefire, Putin attacked our gas infrastructure,"" Zelenskyy told Bill Hemmer in a live interview on ""America's Newsroom."" Asked whether Ukraine would honor the ceasefire, Zelenskyy answered, ""Of course,"" insisting that Kyiv had already refrained from striking Russian energy facilities overnight. TRUMP ANNOUNCES IMMEDIATE ENERGY CEASEFIRE BETWEEN RUSSIA AND UKRAINE A family walks past an apartment building that was hit by a Russian drone, amid Russia's attack on Ukraine, in Kharkiv, Ukraine, October 12, 2026.(Thomas Peter/Reuters) ""We didn't attack any energy objects on the territory of Russia because President Trump said that there will be an energy ceasefire between Ukraine and Russia. And we didn't attack, but Russia attacked our gas stations, energy infrastructure, infrastructure and other","Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:36:46 -0400",https://www.foxnews.com/world/zelenskyy-blasts-putin-defying-trumps-ceasefire-push-sends-pointed-message-white-house,2026-10-18 01:50:12
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Trump Says US and Canada Have Reached Last-Minute Deal to Delay 50% US Tariffs on Canadian Imports,Trump Says US and Canada Have Reached Last-Minute Deal to Delay 50% US Tariffs on Canadian Imports,"Trump Says US and Canada Have Reached Last-Minute Deal to Delay 50% US Tariffs on Canadian Imports The announcement, which Trump made on his social media platform, buys time for more negotiations and avoids, for now, another strain in already tense relations between the historic allies. Washington:President Donald Trump said Tuesday he was delaying 50% U.S. tariffs on $20 billion worth of Canadian imports after the two countries reached a last-minute deal hours before the sanctions were to go into effect. The announcement, which Trump made on his social media platform, buys time for more negotiations and avoids, for now, another strain in already tense relations between the historic allies. “I have paused the 50% Tariffs against Canada, that were scheduled to kick in tomorrow morning for three days, based on the fact that Canada and the U.S.A., subject to the finalisation of documents, have a DEAL!” Trump posted on Truth Social less than two hours before the 12:01 a.m. Wednesday deadline. If they had gone into effect as scheduled at 12:01 a.m. Wednesday, Trump’s import taxes would have hit Canadian products ranging from hockey sticks to tongue depressors. But the political impact would likely have been bigger than the economic one. Canada had threatened to retaliate against any new tariffs with levies of its own, aggravating a trade fight between countries that sold each other $880 billion worth of goods and services last year. Canadian officials did not immediately respond to requests for comment Tuesday night. Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney and Trump had spoken twice by phone in the past two days about the ongoing negotiations, including a call Tuesday afternoon, Carney’s office said, underscoring the last-minute push for a deal. Both countries had re","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:51:34 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-says-us-and-canada-have-reached-last-minute-deal-to-delay-50-us-tariffs-on-canadian-imports-2026-08-19-135042,2026-10-18 01:50:13
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'Allegations Lack Seriousness': Turkiye Denies Israel's Claims Over Syria Airstrikes,'Allegations Lack Seriousness': Turkiye Denies Israel's Claims Over Syria Airstrikes,"'Allegations Lack Seriousness': Turkiye Denies Israel's Claims Over Syria Airstrikes &quot;These air strikes should stop, and we stand against them,&quot; Dujarric said at a UN press briefing on Tuesday. As per Al Jazeera, Egypt's Foreign Ministry also condemned the Israeli strikes, calling them a &quot;dangerous escalation that threatens security and stability in the region&quot;. Ankara:Turkiye on Wednesday rejected Israel's claim that its airstrikes on Syria's Abu al-Duhur military airport were linked to a planned Turkish troop deployment, saying the allegations ""lack seriousness"" and seek to legitimise strikes on Syria's sovereignty and territorial integrity. In a post on X, the Turkish Presidential Communications Directorate said, “The allegations put forward by the Israeli Prime Ministry, which lack seriousness, aim to legitimize Israel's unlawful airstrikes targeting the sovereignty and territorial integrity of Syria.” It added, ""The accusations raised stem from Netanyahu's intent to continue his expansionist and destabilizing policies in the region ahead of elections in Israel."" Turkiye said it supports the establishment of lasting peace in the region, adding that ""the sole path to this lies in Netanyahu abandoning his aggressive and coercive policies and demonstrating respect for international law"". ""Turkey will steadfastly continue its cooperation with the Syrian Government on legitimate grounds to establish peace, stability, and prosperity in Syria, and will never allow Syria to be destabilized,"" it said. The remarks came after Israel carried out airstrikes on the Abu al-Duhur military airport in Syria's eastern Idlib province. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office said that Syria was allowing Turkish troops to deploy at an airbase near Aleppo. Meanwhile, on Tuesday (local time), UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres' spokesperso","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:27:49 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/allegations-lack-seriousness-turkiye-denies-israel-s-claims-over-syria-airstrikes-2026-08-19-135061,2026-10-18 01:50:13
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,'Substantial Progress Made': Canadian PM Carney as American Tariffs Postponed for 3 Days,'Substantial Progress Made': Canadian PM Carney as American Tariffs Postponed for 3 Days,"'Substantial Progress Made': Canadian PM Carney as American Tariffs Postponed for 3 Days Sharing the remarks in a letter posted on X, Prime Minister Carney reassured that while rigorous engagements remain in place with Washington, Canada remains focused on building a stronger, more independent, and more competitive economy at home. Ottawa:With Ottawa and Washington continually engaged in discussions over the 50 per cent tariff on a select range of Canadian goods, Prime Minister Mark Carney said that the implementation of the tariffs has been postponed until August 21. Sharing the remarks in a letter posted on X, Prime Minister Carney reassured that while rigorous engagements remain in place with Washington, Canada remains focused on building a stronger, more independent, and more competitive economy at home. ""Over the last number of weeks, Canada has engaged in intensive discussions with the United States to address outstanding trade issues and deliver greater certainty and real benefits for Canadian businesses, workers, farmers and families,"" he said. The Canadian Prime Minister observed that while significant headway has been made, key work remains to be done. Substantial progress has been made, although there is important work still to be done. As this work is ongoing, the United States has agreed to postpone the implementation of its 50% tariff on a range of Canadian goods under Section 338 of the U.S. Tariff Act of 1930 until the end of day, August 21,"" he said. The announcement comes in the nick of time as the Trump administration's latest round of tariffs was originally scheduled to take effect at 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time on Wednesday. According to Canadian public broadcaster CBC, the levies would have applied to hundreds of products worth more than USD 28 billion, from plywood and cement to wine ","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:09:03 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/substantial-progress-made-says-canadian-pm-carney-as-american-tariffs-postponed-for-3-days-2026-08-19-135058,2026-10-18 01:50:15
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Former Pakistan PM Imran Khan's Sister Noreen Meets Him at Adiala Jail After 9 Months,Former Pakistan PM Imran Khan's Sister Noreen Meets Him at Adiala Jail After 9 Months,"Former Pakistan PM Imran Khan's Sister Noreen Meets Him at Adiala Jail After 9 Months The development came after a three-member Pakistani Supreme Court bench, headed by Justice Shahid Waheed, directed the government earlier in the day to facilitate weekly meetings between Imran and his family amid concerns over his health. Rawalpindi:Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf (PTI) founder Imran Khan's sister, Noreen Niazi, met him at Adiala Jail on Tuesday after a gap of around nine months, following the Pakistani Supreme Court's order allowing weekly meetings between the former Prime Minister and his family, The Express Tribune reported. According to The Express Tribune, this meeting lasted approximately 15 minutes. Noreen briefed Imran about the Supreme Court's order regarding his transfer to Islamabad's Shifa Hospital, enquired about his health, and discussed some ongoing legal matters with him.After the meeting, Noreen confirmed that she had met Imran but did not speak to the media, in line with an assurance given before the court, the report said. She later left Adiala Jail along with her sisters Aleema Khan and Uzma Khan. The Express Tribune reported that Imran also met his wife, Bushra Bibi, with their meeting lasting around 30-35 minutes. Earlier, Bushra Bibi met her daughter, Mubashra Sheikh, and sister-in-law Mehrunnnisa. Speaking to the media after the meeting, Aleema expressed happiness over the Supreme Court order. ""Words cannot describe how happy I am about the meeting. I cannot even imagine where I would have got sweets from. I have appeared before the ATC Rawalpindi from the Supreme Court,"" she added. Asked whether she had received any indication that circumstances were changing, Aleema said, ""Where are we supposed to get any indication from? Do you mean this meeting? Yes, something has happened","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:34:57 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/former-pakistan-pm-imran-khan-s-sister-noreen-meets-him-at-adiala-jail-after-9-months-2026-08-19-135039,2026-10-18 01:50:16
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,"Trump Claims Over 24,000 Noncitizens Voted Illegally in 2020","Trump Claims Over 24,000 Noncitizens Voted Illegally in 2020","Trump Claims Over 24,000 Noncitizens Voted Illegally in 2020 The White House and the Trump administration have drawn direct comparisons between election administration in both countries, asserting that the US relies heavily on self-attestation for citizenship relative to international peers. Washington, DC:US President Donald Trump on Tuesday (local time) claimed that more than 24,000 noncitizens voted illegally in the 2020 election, citing an ongoing review by the US Census Bureau. In a post on Truth Social, Trump said, ""The Census Bureau has begun checking the Voter Records from 2020 against their Citizenship Records. On the first 128,000,000 Voters, the Census Bureau proves that over 24,000 Noncitizens voted illegally!"" ""The Census Bureau is going to analyse the next 32,000,000 Voters, and this number will explode,"" he added. Trump also reiterated his claim about the 2020 election, saying, “I won the election!” He further called for the passage of the SAVE America Act, saying, ""We must pass THE SAVE America Act. Thank you for your attention to this matter!"" His remarks came after he endorsed the proposed Safeguard American Voter Eligibility (SAVE) America Act, introduced in Congress on January 29, which aims to overhaul federal voting standards in the United States. It mandates that state election authorities require physical proof of US citizenship (such as a passport or birth certificate) upon voter registration, alongside valid photo identification at the ballot box; limits mail voting strictly to specific exceptions, including illness, physical disability, active military service, or travel; and directs US states to purge non-citizens from federal voter registries using federal databases. Earlier, in a post on Truth Social on Monday (local time), Trump rec","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:38:56 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/trump-claims-over-24000-noncitizens-voted-illegally-in-2020-2026-08-19-135040,2026-10-18 01:50:16
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,MEA Cites Security Concerns for Continued Kartarpur Corridor Closure as SGPC Seeks More Pilgrim Visas,MEA Cites Security Concerns for Continued Kartarpur Corridor Closure as SGPC Seeks More Pilgrim Visas,"MEA Cites Security Concerns for Continued Kartarpur Corridor Closure as SGPC Seeks More Pilgrim Visas MEA Spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal made the remarks while responding to questions on demands for an increase in the number of pilgrim visas and the reopening of the Kartarpur Sahib Corridor. New Delhi:The Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) on Tuesday reiterated that pilgrimage travel between India and Pakistan is governed by bilateral arrangements, while services along the Sri Kartarpur Sahib Corridor continue to remain suspended due to the prevailing security situation. MEA Spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal made the remarks while responding to questions on demands for an increase in the number of pilgrim visas and the reopening of the Kartarpur Sahib Corridor. Jaiswal was also asked about a high-level delegation from the Shiromani Gurdwara Parbandhak Committee (SGPC) meeting Pakistan's Charge d'Affaires in New Delhi to seek an increase in the visa quota for Sikh pilgrims travelling to Pakistan. ""We also have seen some reports about the meeting that you just talked about,"" Jaiswal said. “Every year, as you know, there is a bilateral arrangement between the two countries under which our jathas, Sikh jathas, visit pilgrimage sites in Pakistan.” On the demand from the SGPC and other Sikh organisations for the resumption of services along the Sri Kartarpur Sahib Corridor, the MEA spokesperson said the corridor remains closed in view of the existing security environment. ""On the Kartarpur corridor issue, we had recently addressed a question in the Parliament as well,"" Jaiswal explained. ""As you are aware, the Kartarpur corridor services of Sri Kartarpur Sahib corridor were suspended with effect from 7th May of 2025 given the extant security situation, which continues to be","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 08:13:52 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/mea-cites-security-concerns-for-continued-kartarpur-corridor-closure-as-sgpc-seeks-more-pilgrim-visas-2026-08-19-135033,2026-10-18 01:50:18
