 Welcome to the post-American order in the Persian Gulf,"" Rezaei said in a post on X. This comes after Trump, earlier on Tuesday, shared an AI-generated image of the Strait of Hormuz on his Truth Social platform, depicting the strategic wa","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:46:33 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/we-will-correct-delusions-of-this-deluded-man-iran-hits-back-at-trump-s-assertion-over-hormuz-as-new-us-territory-2026-08-19-135034,2026-10-18 01:50:18
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,Israel and Syria Agreed to Maintain 'Status Quo' on Security Matters: Netanyahu,Israel and Syria Agreed to Maintain 'Status Quo' on Security Matters: Netanyahu,"Israel and Syria Agreed to Maintain 'Status Quo' on Security Matters: Netanyahu The statement came after reports of Israeli airstrikes on the Abu al-Duhur Airbase in Syria, with the US Special Presidential Envoy for Syria and Iraq, Tom Barrack, expressing concern over what he called an &quot;unnecessary escalation.&quot; Tel Aviv:Israel and Syria had agreed to maintain a status quo on security matters, but Syria was on the verge of breaching the understanding by allowing Turkish troops to deploy at an airbase near Aleppo, the Prime Minister's Office of Israel said on Tuesday. In a post shared on X, the office of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel had repeatedly warned Syria that such a deployment would pose a threat to its security. ""The Prime Minister's Office: Israel and Syria agreed to a status quo in security matters, which Syria was on the verge of breaching by permitting Turkish troops to deploy at an airbase near Aleppo. Israel repeatedly warned Syria that such a deployment would pose a threat to Israel's security. Syria chose to ignore these warnings,"" the post read. ""Israel will not tolerate threats to its security, and would welcome a return to the status quo,"" it added. The statement came after reports of Israeli airstrikes on the Abu al-Duhur Airbase in Syria, with the US Special Presidential Envoy for Syria and Iraq, Tom Barrack, expressing concern over what he called an ""unnecessary escalation."" Barrack said the confirmed Israeli airstrikes did not contribute to regional stability and highlighted Syria's recent efforts towards de-escalation with Israel. ""We are deeply concerned that the confirmed Israeli airstrikes on Abu al-Duhur Airbase constitute an unnecessary escalation that does not advance regional stability,"" Barrack said in a post on X. He added that ","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:37:11 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/israel-and-syria-agreed-to-maintain-status-quo-on-security-matters-netanyahu-2026-08-19-135032,2026-10-18 01:50:19
Republic TV,India (International/Geopolitical),en,At Least 30 Dead After Artisanal Gold Mine Collapses in Central African Republic,At Least 30 Dead After Artisanal Gold Mine Collapses in Central African Republic,"At Least 30 Dead After Artisanal Gold Mine Collapses in Central African Republic Residents, emergency workers, and fellow miners immediately scrambled to initiate desperate rescue efforts, retrieving at least 30 bodies from the debris while administering emergency care to surviving workers pulled from the wreckage. Bangui:At least 30 miners have been killed, and numerous others remain missing following the collapse of an artisanal gold mine in the western region of the Central African Republic (CAR) on Tuesday, August 18. The disaster occurred during morning operations in the Abba region of the Nana-Mambéré prefecture. Residents, emergency workers, and fellow miners immediately scrambled to initiate desperate rescue efforts, retrieving at least 30 bodies from the debris while administering emergency care to surviving workers pulled from the wreckage. Video footage emerging from the site highlighted chaotic scene conditions as rescue personnel and locals worked frantically through heavy mud to locate trapped survivors. Lacking modern machinery, workers were seen using rudimentary tools and their bare hands to clear earth from the collapsed pit. Speaking on the disaster, Deputy Mayor Souleymane Bi issued an urgent plea for international and regional aid to support the ongoing operations. ""It is horrible, and we are calling for help from organisations and all people of goodwill to help pull from the hole those who are unable to do so,"" Bi stated, emphasising that local resources are severely stretched as search efforts continue. Government spokesman Evariste Ngamana expressed deep condolences on behalf of the administration to the affected families and workers, adding that authorities are mobilising relief resources to support the site. The incident highlights the severe risks associated w","Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:33:38 +0530",https://www.republicworld.com/world-news/at-least-30-dead-after-artisanal-gold-mine-collapses-in-central-african-republic-2026-08-19-135029,2026-10-18 01:50:20
